{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192554": {
      "title": "Council on East Asian Studies: Postdoctoral Associates Position",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: MacMillan Center Location: New Haven, CT The Yale University Council on East Asian Studies seeks applications for up to four Postdoctoral Associates for an appointment period from July 1 st , 202 7 – June 30 th , 202 9 . Inaugurated in the 1999-2000 academic year, the Postdoctoral Associates Program at the Council on East Asian Studies provides promising scholars specializing in East Asia two years at Yale University during which they can prepare their dissertations for publication, pursue research projects, gain experience teaching advanced seminars to undergraduates, and utilize Yale’s resources. Proposals with single region or transregional emphasis on China, Japan, and/or Korea are welcome. Housed in the MacMillan Center for International and Area Studies, the Council on East Asian Studies provides an important interdisciplinary forum at Yale for academic exploration and support for the study of East Asia, bringing together scholars who specialize in, across, and beyond China, Japan, and Korea. The salary for this position is commensurate with experience and complies with the Yale Office of Postdoctoral Affairs compensation policy and includes a benefits package . For more information and complete application requirements, please visit macmillan.yale.edu/eastasia/postdoctoral-program . Requirements: Ph.D. awarded between 202 4 and June 15, 202 7 in any field specializing in East Asia; remain in residence for duration of appointment; during appointment revise doctoral dissertation or complete research project resulting in publishable manuscript; provide one lecture as part of the CEAS Postdoctoral Associates Lecture Series; and teach one undergraduate course for majors in East Asian studies. Proposals with single region or transregional emphasis on China, Japan, and/or Korea are welcome. To apply, please submit cover letter, CV, dissertation abstract (250 words), course syllabus , course proposal form (available to download here ), statement regarding intended research project (no more than 2500 words), writing sample (no more than 30 pages), and 3 letters of recommendation by Friday, January 1 , 202 7 . The writing sample can be a dissertation chapter, journal article, or other such academic paper. Letters of recommendation must be uploaded via a dossier service or from the recommenders directly. Please be sure that your recommenders address your teaching abilities in their letters. Names of references will not be accepted in lieu of confidential letters of recommendation. No late applications will be accepted. All application materials must be submitted online through Interfolio: ENTER LINK HERE"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194718": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Human-Computer Interaction",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Computer Science Location: New Haven, CT The Computer Science (CS) Department in the Yale School of Engineering & Applied Science (SEAS) invites applications for one tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Human-Computer Interaction (HCI). The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Applicants are expected to excel in HCI research and to teach at the undergraduate and graduate level within the Computer Science curriculum. In support of the SEAS Strategic Vision, we are particularly interested in candidates whose research intersects with Human-AI Interaction. We seek scholars who investigate the symbiotic relationship between humans and intelligent systems. Examples (in no particular order) include scholars who advance human-AI collaboration or teaming, develop novel interfaces and interaction paradigms for AI agents, engineer AI-driven pedagogical tools to enhance learning outcomes, create AI-powered interfaces for end-user programming of complex computing systems, design AI-powered assistive interfaces, or build creative interfaces that leverage AI. Successful candidates are expected to have a strong record of publication in premier HCI venues such as CHI, CSCW, UIST, or IUI. Yale provides many opportunities for research collaborations, offering an intellectual environment in which Human-Computer Interaction can engage not only with Computer Science and Engineering, but with the extraordinary breadth of scholarship and creative practice across the university. Yale faculty regularly have the opportunity to teach excellent students, both graduate and undergraduate. An overview of academic programs offered by the CS department can be found on the department’s website: http://cpsc.yale.edu/ . Candidates must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at the time of hire in Computer Science or a related discipline. Applicants are asked to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a teaching statement, a research statement, and three confidential letters of recommendation through Interfolio. A helpful teaching statement should describe the candidate’s teaching experience and explain how they could contribute to the curriculum at Yale. The research statement should include a research vision and, if relevant, potential collaborations across Yale. To ensure full consideration, please submit all materials by December 15, 2026. Review of applications will begin after December 16, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Contact Alicia Vignola (alicia.vignola@yale.edu) with any questions regarding the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195274": {
      "title": "Baltic Studies Program: Juris Padegs Post-Doctoral Associate, 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: MacMillan Center Location: New Haven, CT The Yale Baltic Studies Program invites applications for a Post-Doctoral Associate position of four months during the 2027-28 academic year for researchers from Latvian or Estonian universities in any field in the humanities or social sciences. Housed in the MacMillan Center for International and Area Studies, the Yale Baltic Studies Program is an interdisciplinary forum for the study of the Baltic Sea region, with an emphasis on the lands that comprise contemporary Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania. The program sponsors workshops, symposia, and lectures, and serves as a resource for and liaison among students and scholars whose work involves the Baltic region. The scholar will be expected to be in residence in New Haven, Connecticut to participate in the activities of the Yale Baltic Studies Program, and to make at least one public presentation at Yale during the period of the appointment. The salary for this position is commensurate with experience and complies with the Yale Office of Postdoctoral Affairs compensation policy and includes a benefits package . Applicants should have completed their Ph.D. or be set to complete it before August 2027, and at the time of application must be working in, or affiliated with, a university or research institute in Latvia or Estonia. Preference will be given to scholars who currently reside, or recently resided, in Latvia or Estonia. The review of applications will begin on February 1, 2027 and will continue until the position is filled. Only on-line submissions will be accepted through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/195274 Application Materials Required (all application materials must be submitted in English): Cover letter: please indicate clearly what months of the year you propose to be in New Haven and the rationale for the proposed period. Curriculum vitae Research statement (no more than 1000 words) Two reference letters, one from the applicant’s academic supervisor and one from an additional faculty member or appropriate administrator at the university or institute at which the applicant is affiliated. The reference letters should address the applicant’s research and the broader significance of this research for higher education and research in either Latvia or Estonia. These letters are to be submitted by the reference writers through the Interfolio site. Proof of English language proficiency such as TOEFL score, IELTS score, or transcript from a previously attended institution where the primary language of instruction is English. For inquiries regarding this position or application process, please contact Bradley Woodworth, Baltic Studies Coordinator, at bradley.woodworth@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195250": {
      "title": "Professor of Operations Management (AY 27-28)",
      "description": "Posted: Oct 08, 2026 Deadline: Nov 30, 2026 Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management (SOM) is soliciting applications for a full-time, tenured professor in Operations Management. Qualifications This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Operations Management, Operations Research, or a directly related field. Applicants must have a minimum of six years of experience as a faculty member at a top-tier business school. The selected candidate must be highly accomplished, well-published, and highly respected in their field. The candidate hired for this position will be expected to continue conducting and publishing their research at a high level as well as excellent teaching and advising to students in SOM's PhD, and master's programs. Appointment terms This is a full-time, tenured faculty position located at the Yale School of Management in New Haven, Connecticut. Appointments will be made for the 2027-28 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and at least two samples of their research via Interfolio. Finalists will be contacted for additional materials, including references, at a later date. Timing Complete applications must be submitted by November 30, 2026 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195271": {
      "title": "Baltic Studies Program: Joseph P. Kazickas Post-Doctoral Associate, 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: MacMillan Center Location: New Haven, CT The Yale Baltic Studies Program invites applications for a Post-Doctoral Associate position of four to five months during the 2027-28 academic year for researchers from Lithuanian universities in the following fields: law, economics, business and finance, environmental policy, political science, international relations, and history. Housed in the MacMillan Center for International and Area Studies, the Yale Baltic Studies Program is an interdisciplinary forum for the study of the Baltic Sea region, with an emphasis on the lands that comprise contemporary Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania. The program sponsors workshops, symposia, and lectures, and serves as a resource for and liaison among students and scholars whose work involves the Baltic region. The scholar will be expected to be in residence in New Haven, Connecticut, to participate in the activities of the Yale Baltic Studies Program, and to make at least one public presentation at Yale during the period of the appointment. The salary for this position is commensurate with experience and complies with the Yale Office of Postdoctoral Affairs compensation policy and includes a benefits package . Applicants should have completed their PhD or be set to complete it before August 2027, and at the time of application must be working in, or affiliated with, a university or research institute in Lithuania. Preference will be given to scholars who currently reside, or have recently resided, in Lithuania. The review of applications will begin on February 1, 2027 and will continue until the position is filled. Only online submissions will be accepted through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/195271 Application Materials Required (all application materials must be submitted in English): Cover letter: please indicate clearly what months of the year you propose to be in New Haven and the rationale for the proposed period. Curriculum vitae Research statement (no more than 1000 words) Two reference letters: one from the applicant’s academic supervisor and one from an additional faculty member or appropriate administrator at the university or institute at which the applicant is affiliated. The reference letters should address the applicant’s research and the broader significance of this research for higher education and research in Lithuania. These letters are to be submitted by the reference writers through the Interfolio site. Proof of English language proficiency such as TOEFL score, IELTS score, or transcript from a previously attended institution where the primary language of instruction is English. For inquiries regarding this position or application process, please contact Bradley Woodworth, Baltic Studies Coordinator, at bradley.woodworth@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195097": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance (AY 27-28)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management (SOM) is soliciting applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Finance at the rank of Assistant Professor. Qualifications This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Finance, Economics, or a directly related field. We are seeking applications from graduating students, post-docs and others who show exceptional promise. The selected candidate will teach graduate- and/or Ph.D.-level courses and advise and mentor students, while conducting high-quality research, representing early demonstration of intellectual leadership in their area of study. Individuals who are currently ABD must be awarded their degree before December 31, 2027. Appointment terms This is a full-time, tenure-track position located at the Yale School of Management in New Haven, Connecticut. Appointments will be made for the 2027-2028 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027. The initial term is typically three years. Appointment as Associate Professor (untenured) may be possible for more experienced applicants who have held a full-time ladder-track faculty role for a few years provided they meet the University’s qualifications for that rank. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, job market paper, research statement (optional) and contact information for three references via Interfolio. Reference requests will be immediately sent via e-mail to proposed letter writers. Timing We plan to hold virtual interviews starting in December 2026, and recommend that applicants submit their materials by November 15, 2026 to ensure full consideration. The deadline to submit an application is December 15, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195222": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics (AY 27-28)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management (SOM) is soliciting applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Economics at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Applicants in all areas of Economics will be considered. Qualifications This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Economics or a directly related field. Individuals who are currently ABD must be awarded their degree before December 31, 2027. The selected candidate(s) will be expected to conduct high-quality research, representing early demonstration of intellectual leadership, in their area of study and teach and advise students in SOM’s master’s and executive education programs. Appointment terms This is a full-time, tenure-track position located at the Yale School of Management in New Haven, Connecticut. Appointments will be made for the 2027-2028 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027. The initial term is typically three years. Individuals with little to no prior work experience in a full-time faculty position will be considered at the Assistant Professor rank, but more experienced applicants who have held a full-time ladder-track faculty role for a few years may be eligible for hire as Associate Professor (tenure-track) provided they meet the University’s qualifications for that rank. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, job market paper, and research statement (optional) via Interfolio. Candidates applying from doctoral programs or post-docs are also required to submit contact information for three references. Reference requests will be immediately sent via e-mail to proposed letter writers. Advanced assistant and associate professors being considered for the position will be contacted for references if they do not wish to supply these at the time of application. Timing Complete applications must be submitted no later than November 13, 2026 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195156": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Pediatric Hospital Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Hospital Medicine Location: New Haven, CT As an Assistant Professor in the Academic Clinician Track, the candidate will be responsible for the care of hospitalized children at locations within the Yale New Haven Health System. This includes coverage at our tertiary academic medical center in New Haven, CT as well as our community hospital sites in Bridgeport, Greenwich and New London. The candidate will also manage the care of otherwise healthy newborns, supervise pediatric hospital medicine fellows, residents and medical students and contribute to the mission and values of the Section of Pediatric Hospital Medicine and the Department of Pediatrics at Yale. Requirements include board certification or eligibility in pediatrics. Ideal candidates will have demonstrated interest and abilities in clinical care and education and will have excellent interpersonal skills. In addition, the candidate should have a track record in mentoring and educating residents in all aspects of pediatric medicine. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of reference to: https://apply.interfolio.com/195156."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194965": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate, Condensed Matter Physics Theory",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Physics Location: New Haven, CT The Condensed Matter Theory group at Yale University invites applications for a postdoctoral position with an anticipated start date in the Summer or Fall of 2027. Preference will be given to applicants with expertise in quantum aspects of condensed matter theory and research interests in the general areas of electron correlations, low-dimensional and topological solids, and physics of superconducting qubits. The postdoctoral scholar is encouraged to work independently and in collaboration with Prof. Leonid Glazman. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at the time of hire. Candidates should forward their CV with publication list and outline of research interests, and arrange for three recommendation letters. Candidates may also include up to four selected preprints and reprints. Electronic submission (in PDF format) of applications and supporting materials is strongly preferred. Please submit all materials, including recommendation letters, to https://apply.interfolio.com/194965 . Early applications are strongly encouraged. Applications and letters must be received prior to November 6, 2026 to guarantee full consideration. Contacts: Leonid Glazman ( leonid.glazman@yale.edu ) ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194235": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Chemical and Environmental Engineering Location: New Haven, Connecticut USA The Department of Chemical and Environmental Engineering (CEE) at Yale University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor , with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The search will consider a ll areas of environmental engineering, with some preference given to candidates working in air quality or computational modeling and environmental data science. Candidates who can establish strong collaborations, both within the department and across the university are especially encouraged to apply.  The successful candidate will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates should hold a PhD or equivalent degree in environmental engineering or a closely related discipline at the time of hire, and be dedicated to teaching environmental engineering courses and developing an internationally recognized research program. Applications should include a cover letter, CV, three representative publications, a description of research and teaching interests, and the names and email addresses of three referees, all submitted through Interfolio. The review of applications will begin on November 9, 2026 and completed applications must be received by December 1, 2026. Inquiries should be directed to the department chair, Prof. John Fortner, at john.fortner@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193677": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate, Classics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: Classics Location: New Haven, CT The Classics Department at Yale is accepting applications for a one-year postdoctoral fellowship and lecturer for 2027-28; the fellowship is renewable for a second year, contingent upon a successful informal review in January 2028.  The anticipated start date of the appointment is August 1, 2027. We invite applications from scholars in any field of research relating to Greco-Roman antiquity. The ideal candidate will have expertise which complements that of the current faculty. The fellow will have a 1-1 teaching expectation or equivalent advising/mentoring responsibilities within the Department, depending on curricular need. Compensation will be commensurate with Yale University postdoctoral compensation policies and the candidate’s experience. The position is benefits-eligible . Applicants must have a Ph.D. (degree conferred 2023 or later) in any field of research relating to Greco-Roman antiquity.  Applicants must have their Ph.D. in hand by the start date of the appointment. The application can be submitted online via Interfolio and must include a) cover letter; b) curriculum vitae; c) letters from three references; and d) a writing sample of no more than 25 pages. Review of applications will begin December 8, 2026. Email inquiries may be addressed to Andrew Johnston, Associate Professor of Classics and History ( andrew.johnston@yale.edu ). Candidates included in the final short list will be interviewed either in person or online. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio’s Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now https://apply.interfolio.com/193677"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194314": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate, Pre-Modern Cultures and Civilizations",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: Archaia Location: New Haven, CT Yale University seeks to appoint a Postdoctoral Associate for a one-year position with a secondary appointment as a Lecturer in an appropriate department, renewable for a second year contingent upon a successful review, beginning in the academic year 2027–2028 within Archaia: the Yale Program for the Study of Global Antiquity . Archaia is a collaborative forum that brings together scholars and graduate students working on early and pre-modern cultures and civilizations at Yale in the Humanities and Social Sciences in addition to the Divinity and Law Schools and various University collections and libraries, including the Yale University Art Gallery, the Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, the Peabody Museum of Natural History, and the Institute for the Preservation of Cultural Heritage. Participating departments and disciplines include Classics, East Asian Languages and Literatures, Near Eastern Languages and Civilizations, History, Religious Studies, Archaeology and Anthropology, History of Art, and the Divinity School. In addition to hosting conferences and colloquia, the year-long Ancient Societies Workshop (ASW), and study tours, Archaia offers a graduate qualification for students interested in research beyond departmental lines. For additional information, see https://archaia.yale.edu/certification . Information about past post-doctoral fellows can be found here . Past Archaia seminars and ASW topics have included environmental humanities, ancient music, comparative linguistics in pre-modern languages, ancient comparative law, ancient ritual, antiquity through the digital humanities, and the archaeology of Dura Europos. Anticipated upcoming topics include writing, materiality, and ancient concepts of embodiment; we are also open to other innovative and cross-disciplinary proposals for future workshops and core seminars. We especially welcome applicants working in areas beyond the ancient Mediterranean world. The postdoctoral associate is expected to take an active role in Archaia programming while pursuing research in their own area of expertise. Additionally, the associate’s duties include: (1) participating in the Archaia Steering Committee, coordinating the graduate certification program, and participating in the graduate forum as a mentor; (2) offering, in the first year, a graduate seminar and/or a study tour (the seminar may be connected with the tour); (3) in the second year of the appointment, co-teaching the Archaia core seminar with a Yale faculty member and/or co-organizing the Archaia Study Tour. The postdoctoral associate will receive guidance from and report to the Archaia co-chairs and will also be provided with at least one mentor from a field/department close to their area of training and expertise. Compensation will be commensurate with Yale University postdoctoral compensation policies and the candidate’s experience. The position is benefits-eligible . Requirements: • A Ph.D. in Near Eastern Languages and Civilizations, Classics, East Asian Studies, South Asian Studies, History, Religious Studies, Archaeology, Anthropology, History of Art, or a related field. • The intellectual training and trajectory of the postdoctoral associate must show a commitment to cross-disciplinary or cross-cultural research in more than one of the areas, languages, and/or disciplines represented by Archaia. • The successful applicant will be able to demonstrate a desire and ability to build collaborative relationships across departments and collections and will possess strong organizational skills. • We especially encourage applications from scholars underrepresented in the study of antiquity. Applicants and referees should upload documentation via Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/194314 Applicants must supply: (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement (1000 words max.) detailing the work that the associate wishes to pursue at Yale, (4) three brief descriptions (not syllabi) of up to 500 words each, for a) a co-taught global antiquity seminar to be offered as an Archaia core course; b) a graduate seminar related to your own research specialization, and with some concern for global antiquity; c) a travel study opportunity (5-10 days) (5) a teaching portfolio (including teaching evaluations or other evidence of teaching effectiveness and syllabi for courses taught or planned), (6) three letters of recommendation addressed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Molly Zahn ( molly.zahn@yale.edu ) Review of applications will begin Dec. 1, 2026. For any questions please contact the chair of the committee, Molly Zahn ( molly.zahn@yale.edu ) and Keith Mazzadra ( keith.mazzadra@yale.edu ), Archaia Program administrator."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194892": {
      "title": "Leadership In Radiology and Public Health:  The Yale Informatics Fellowship",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT Role: Dual appointment as Yale MPH Candidate and Yale Diagnostic Radiology Clinical Instructor. For Whom: Post-residency Diagnostic Radiologist who aspires to be an informatics leader in Private or Academic Practice. With an active clinical presence in their chosen Diagnostic Radiology division alongside a broader role in the department’s informatics initiatives, the Radiologist will become experienced in much of the gamut of clinical and informatics activities in our department. Overview : During a two-year cycle, beginning in July, the candidate will complete the MPH program at Yale University and a clinical imaging position with roles corresponding to the needs of the section applied to. In addition, the candidate will play a leadership role on one or more projects from the Chair’s office. Projects may include (but not be limited to): research; operational programing; innovation initiatives; teleradiology programmatic growth; or process improvement. The candidate will work as a Clinical Instructor as defined by the imaging section. The candidates' clinical work will be proctored and reviewed on a regular basis by the section’s Attending Physicians. Beginning in late July, the candidate will begin the eMPH program on the Health Informatics track. Over the next 24 months, the candidate will spend 3 class sessions on campus and engage in the online education program. The fellow will NOT be scheduled for clinical work during the period leading up to, nor including, the class times. The fellowship will conclude at the end of 24 months, with the fellow receiving a certificate of completion of fellowship from Yale Diagnostic Radiology as well as the MPH degree from Yale University. The candidate will submit three letters of recommendation (two from clinical mentors/colleagues, and one from an academic mentor who can attest to the candidate’s potential in informatics) and affirm that they will have completed a certified diagnostic radiology residency program as of the start date; and are either board certified or eligible for the diagnostic radiology board certification exam. Students will also need to formally apply and be accepted to the Executive Master of Public Health (eMPH) program. Interested applicants should upload their CV & Cover Letter to:"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194684": {
      "title": "Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation – Adult Reconstruction/Arthroplasty- Assistant/Associate Professor (RFP-2395)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation Location: Bridgeport, CT The Yale Department of Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation, in collaboration with the Yale School of Medicine and Yale New Haven Health System, Northeast Medical Group seek an Orthopaedic Arthroplasty surgeon for a full-time faculty position with interest and expertise in Orthopaedic Adult Reconstruction. This position will have an expectation of clinical service commitment at the Yale New Haven Health Bridgeport Hospital region in Fairfield County Connecticut . Responsibilities will include clinical service, with the possibility of teaching, and research activities depending on the wishes and skill set of the candidate.  Physicians with a sole focus on clinical care are welcome to apply. Academic appointment will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Our department anticipates that the successful candidate will have a dynamic personality, outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion, as well as academic collaboration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be board-certified or board-eligible Orthopaedic surgeons with fellowship training in Arthroplasty/Adult Reconstruction. Interested candidates should apply via: https://apply.interfolio.com/194684 Questions regarding the position should be directed to: Julianna Bulter, julianna.butler@yale.edu , Chief of Staff, and Priscilla Rivera, priscilla.rivera@yale.edu , Interim Chief of Staff, Office of the Chair."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194361": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, Applied and Computational Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Deadline: May 31, 2027 Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Applied and Computational Mathematics Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Applied and Computational Mathematics (ACM) in the School of Engineering & Applied Science (SEAS) at Yale University invites applications for a tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek candidates from across applied and computational mathematics. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, numerical analysis and scientific computing; differential equations and mathematical modeling; inverse problems and control; and stochastic methods. We particularly welcome research that advances computational methods, including the use of artificial intelligence and machine learning for discovery in applied mathematics and scientific computing. Research motivated by applications is welcome when its contributions are of broad mathematical or computational significance. ACM builds on Yale's established strengths in applied mathematics and on the University's strong tradition of collaboration across departments and schools. Its home in SEAS places fundamental mathematical research in close interaction with engineering and the applied sciences. The successful candidate will play a leading role in the development of this growing department and in building collaborations across Yale. Candidates must hold a PhD or equivalent degree in mathematics, applied mathematics, or a related field. Candidates should have a distinguished research record and internationally recognized leadership in their field, together with an ambitious ongoing research agenda. Excellence in teaching and advising is essential, and candidates will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants should submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, and a teaching statement via Interfolio. Letters of recommendation are not required at the application stage. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to Eric Michielssen at eric.michielssen@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194056": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Applied and Computational Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Deadline: May 31, 2027 Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Applied and Computational Mathematics Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Applied and Computational Mathematics (ACM) in the School of Engineering & Applied Science (SEAS) at Yale University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek candidates from across applied and computational mathematics. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, numerical analysis and scientific computing; differential equations and mathematical modeling; inverse problems and control; and stochastic methods. We particularly welcome research that advances computational methods, including the use of artificial intelligence and machine learning for discovery in applied mathematics and scientific computing. Research motivated by applications is welcome when its contributions are of broad mathematical or computational significance. ACM builds on Yale's established strengths in applied mathematics and on the University's strong tradition of collaboration across departments and schools. Its home in SEAS places fundamental mathematical research in close interaction with engineering and the applied sciences. The successful candidate will help shape this growing department and build collaborations across Yale. Candidates must hold a PhD or equivalent degree in mathematics, applied mathematics, or a related field at the time of hire. Candidates must have demonstrated originality and outstanding promise in research, with the potential to establish an independent research program. Excellence in teaching and advising is essential, and candidates will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants should submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, and a teaching statement through Interfolio. Applicants should also arrange for three confidential letters of recommendation to be submitted through Interfolio. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to Eric Michielssen at eric.michielssen@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194417": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, Connecticut The Department of Health Policy and Management at the Yale School of Public Health invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the level of Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Policy and Management, starting in Fall 2027. Rank will be commensurate with experience. We welcome applications from those interested in conducting empirical research in health policy, healthcare management, health services research, demography, political science, sociology, health economics, public policy, and related fields. Candidates must have a doctoral degree by the start of appointment, a well-developed research plan, publications in peer-reviewed journals (or the potential to publish therein), and the ability to compete effectively for extramural funding. In addition, the selected candidate will be expected to participate in masters and doctoral student teaching and mentoring. Information about the Department and YSPH can be found at http://publichealth.yale.edu/hpm/ and http://publichealth.yale.edu, respectively. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and recent writing sample or job market paper. For fullest consideration, applications should be submitted by Oct 31. Only complete applications will be considered. Confidential inquiries can be sent to jason.l.schwartz@yale.edu Please apply on-line at:"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194475": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - Urogynecology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences Location: Bridgeport, CT The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences is seeking faculty interested in joining the Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery Section in our nationally leading academic department. The position is seeking candidates at or meeting the Yale School of Medicine criteria at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level, rank and track commensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidate must be a fellowship trained Urogynecologist and possess excellent surgical skills and have demonstrated excellence in clinical care. Interested candidates should submit application materials at: https://apply.interfolio.com/194475"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194469": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Physician Associate Program",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Physician Associate Program Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine Physician Associate Program (Yale PA Program) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenured faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The Yale PA Program has a long history of educating outstanding clinicians and leaders in healthcare. We seek a dynamic individual interested in joining an innovative, dedicated, and collaborative faculty. This faculty appointment is in the Section of General Internal Medicine, PA Program at the Yale School of Medicine. This position will focus on innovation and delivery of the pre-clinical curriculum and teach in both the pre-clinical and clinical phases of the program. In person teaching is required in New Haven, CT. Additional responsibilities include: student assessment, remediation, student advisement, scholarship, service, and 20% clinical practice. All faculty collaboratively participate in admissions, strategic planning, curriculum development, and continuous review and evaluation of the curriculum in support of accreditation standards. Yale University offers competitive compensation and excellent benefits. Master’s degree from an ARC-PA accredited PA program (or related medical discipline, i.e., MD or DO) is required. Minimum 2 years of educating PA students as a faculty member or a clinical preceptor is required.  At least 3 years of clinical experience as a practicing PA is also required. Preference will be given to candidates with a minimum 3-years’ experience as a full-time clinician and demonstrated effective teaching experience in the classroom and/or clinical setting. Current certification by the NCCPA (or ABMS- or AOA-approved specialty board) and CT State licensure (or eligibility for licensure). Demonstrated excellent interpersonal skills and a strong interest in delivering an experiential, student-focused curriculum. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. Candidates should apply directly through Interfolio at the link: https://apply.interfolio.com/194469 Candidates are asked to provide their CV, Cover Letter, and three letters of recommendation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188718": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Quantum Condensed Matter Theory",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Physics Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Physics at Yale University ( http://physics.yale.edu ) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the area of theoretical condensed matter physics, broadly defined. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at time of hire and will join an active group of theorists in Physics and Applied Physics. Yale provides a unique research environment owing to its excellent group of theorists and experimentalists engaged in condensed matter physics and related fields. The search is especially aimed at candidates whose research program centers on quantum condensed matter physics with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate is expected to: Lead an internationally recognized and forefront research program. Excel in teaching courses and mentoring students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Be an active and engaged member of the Physics Department and of the University. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at time of hire. Applications that are complete by November 18, 2026 will receive full consideration.  Interested applicants should create a profile in Interfolio [ https://apply.interfolio.com/188718 ] and submit the following documents: A cover letter. A curriculum vita (CV) including an up-to-date list of publications. A research statement (up to 4 pages), highlighting future research plans, both short-term and long-term. A teaching statement (up to 2 pages), outlining the applicant’s prior experience, teaching philosophy and approaches to pedagogy. In addition, applicants should arrange for a minimum of three confidential letters of recommendation. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. We also welcome nominations for the position, which should be directed to the email address below. Please address questions and nominations to the chair of the search committee, Prof. Walter Goldberger, to PhysTheorySearch@mailman.yale.edu . More Information: https://physics.yale.edu/opportunities"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193330": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, African Art",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: History of Art Location: New Haven, CT The Department of the History of Art at Yale University is looking to hire a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor with an initial 5-year appointment in African art before 1950, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027 . Expertise in the histories of art, performance, architecture and visual cultures of the African continent and its islands, grounded in substantial research and professional engagement in the region, as well as a commitment to teaching introductory courses in African art history, is required. The teaching expectation is normally 4 courses per academic year, plus service to the program, including mentorship of undergraduate and graduate students. The appointee must hold a PhD in the History of Art or have completed all requirements for the PhD by June 2027. Applicants must demonstrate strong research focus on the visual arts. Applicants should submit an application via apply.interfolio.com/193330 . They should submit a cover letter, CV, writing sample, statement about pedagogy, and two sample syllabi (one for an introductory lecture class, the other for an upper-division course/seminar), reflecting the breadth of the applicant’s teaching expertise should be submitted online, along with three confidential letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please email: Pamela Lee, Professor and Search Chair at pamela.lee@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194292": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences Location: Bridgeport and Greenwich, CT The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences at Yale School of Medicine seeks an outstanding candidate focusing on minimally invasive gynecologic surgery (MIGS) at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Consultive gynecological hospital care and gynecology call coverage is shared amongst members of the division; no inpatient obstetric coverage is expected. The current clinical coverage area is Bridgeport and Greenwich, CT. The candidate must have demonstrated excellence in the delivery of patient-centered, equitable, comprehensive clinical care and possess excellence complex surgery skills in minimally invasive gynecology surgery (MIGS). The applicant is required to be Board certified/eligible in general obstetrics and gynecology and have completed an AAGL-accredited complex benign gynecology fellowship (formally FMIGS). Interested candidates should submit application materials at: https://apply.interfolio.com/194292"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193877": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Materials Science and Energy Sciences Institute",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Materials Science Location: Yale University West Campus Yale University seeks to recruit a faculty member at the Assistant Professor level to the SEAS Department of Materials Science and Yale's  interdisciplinary Energy Sciences Institute, which unites members of multiple departments. The Institute is one of several science and engineering initiatives located at Yale's West Campus, a 137-acre campus whose acquisition in 2007 has provided the University with unparalleled opportunities to expand its activities in cutting-edge research areas. We seek a creative scholar in the areas of energy conversion, energy storage, and/or energy sustainability who will have a primary appointment in the Department of Materials Science. Candidates should have an outstanding record of research that demonstrates originality in addressing significant questions in the study of energy. The successful candidate is expected to initiate a vibrant research group, be an interactive member of the Materials Science Department, and teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at the time of hire. Applicants should upload a cover letter; a curriculum vitae (CV); a statement of current and future research plans (up to 3 pages); a teaching statement (up to one page); and up to five reprints of papers published or in press. Applicants should arrange for three referees to upload letters of recommendation by November 9, 2026. Review of applications will begin on November 9, 2026, and complete applications received by this date will receive full consideration. For questions regarding this position, please email Owen Miller at owen.miller@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194185": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, ICU, Assistant/Associate Professor (2393)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia, ICU. Clinical assignments may include Yale New Haven Hospital, Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Bridgeport Hospital, and/or Lawrence + Memorial Hospital, with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care as well as resident and fellow education.  There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/194185 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194030": {
      "title": "Surgery, Vascular Surgery, Saint Raphael Campus, Assistant Professor (2388)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Vascular Surgery Location: New Haven, CT Assistant Professor of Surgery (Vascular Surgery) Yale School of Medicine, Department of Surgery The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Surgery, Division of Vascular Surgery and Endovascular Therapy is seeking a board-eligible or board-certified vascular surgeon for a full-time faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. We are seeking a vascular surgeon with a strong commitment to clinical excellence, academic inquiry, and the education of future surgeons. The successful candidate will join a nationally recognized and collegial team providing comprehensive vascular and endovascular care at St. Raphael’s Campus (SRC) and YNHH. Responsibilities include: Providing the full spectrum of open and endovascular vascular surgery care in both inpatient and outpatient settings Participating in and contributing to the education of medical students, residents, and vascular fellows Engaging in clinical research, quality improvement, and academic activities aligned with the mission of the Department of Surgery Collaborating with multidisciplinary teams to advance innovation and excellence in patient care Qualifications: MD or equivalent degree Board eligible or certified in Vascular Surgery Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut Demonstrated commitment to teaching, clinical scholarship, and academic advancement Yale School of Medicine and Yale New Haven Health offer a rich environment for academic growth, professional development, and multidisciplinary collaboration. The Department of Surgery values diversity, mentorship, and innovation in clinical practice, education, and research. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a statement of academic and clinical interests through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/194030. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193628": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Infectious Diseases",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Infectious Diseases Location: New Haven, CT  Full time faculty positions are available at the level of Assistant/Associate professor in the Section of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Internal Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine.  Applicants should have an M.D., training in infectious diseases, and potential for a career in academic medicine. Candidates are expected to participate in the clinical and educational activities of the section. Applicants should have an M.D., training in infectious diseases, and potential for a career in academic medicine. Please apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/193628"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193951": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor on the Educator Scholar Track in Health Policy and Management",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, Connecticut The Department of Health Policy and Management in the Yale School of Public Health is seeking applicants at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor in the Public Health Educator Scholar Track, with a strong record of teaching and research scholarship in Health Policy, Management, Political Science, Sociology, or a related field. The position emphasizes teaching advanced concepts and methods to M.P.H. and Ph.D. students. The selected candidate must be an exemplary teacher and will eventually be expected to take a leadership role in the educational mission of the department, in addition to maintaining an externally funded research program. Candidates must have a doctoral degree by the start of appointment and a well-developed teaching philosophy. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a successful candidate is identified. Candidates are asked to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a teaching statement, and the names and contact information of three individuals who can serve as references. Information about the Department and YSPH can be found at http://publichealth.yale.edu/hpm/ and http://publichealth.yale.edu , respectively."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193780": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting (AY 27-28)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management (SOM) is soliciting applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Accounting at the rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor. Qualifications This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Accounting. Applicants with a Ph.D. in a field that is broadly related, such as Finance or Economics, will also be considered if they have a demonstrated interest in Accounting. Individuals who are currently ABD must be awarded their degree before December 31, 2027. The selected candidates are expected to conduct high-quality research, representing early demonstration of intellectual leadership, in their area of study and advise students in SOM's Ph.D., master's, and executive education programs. Appointment terms This is a full-time, tenure-track faculty position located at the Yale School of Management in New Haven, Connecticut. Appointments will be made for the 2027-28 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027. Individuals with little to no prior work experience in a full-time faculty position will be considered at the Assistant Professor rank, but more experienced applicants who have held a full-time ladder-track faculty role for a few years may be eligible for hire as Associate Professor (tenure-track) provided they meet the University’s qualifications for that rank. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, the job market paper that will be the primary topic of their job talk, and a research statement (optional). Candidates applying from doctoral programs or post-docs are also required to arrange for three letters of reference. Reference requests to proposed letter writers will be immediately sent via e-mail. Advanced assistant and associate professors being considered for the position will be contacted for references if they do not wish to supply these at the time of application. Timing Complete applications must be submitted in Interfolio no later than November 1, 2026 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193781": {
      "title": "Professor of Accounting (AY 27-28)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management (SOM) is soliciting applications for a full-time, tenured professor in Accounting. Qualifications This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Accounting. Applicants with a Ph.D. in a field that is broadly related, such as Finance or Economics, will also be considered if they have a demonstrated interest in Accounting. Applicants must have a minimum of five years of experience as a faculty member at a top-tier business school. The selected candidate must be highly accomplished, well-published, and highly respected in their field. The candidate hired for this position will be expected to continue conducting and publishing their research and will teach and advise students in SOM's Ph.D., master's, and executive education programs. Appointment terms This is a full-time, tenured faculty position located at the Yale School of Management in New Haven, Connecticut. Appointments will be made for the 2027-28 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and at least two samples of their research. Finalists will be contacted for additional materials, including references, at a later date. Timing Complete applications must be submitted no later than November 1, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193444": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Computational Biophysics and Biochemistry",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Biological Science: Molecular Biophysics and Biochemistry Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Molecular Biophysics & Biochemistry ( http://mbb.yale.edu /) at Yale University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty appointment in Quantitative and Computational Biophysics and Biochemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor. This search will focus on candidates with innovative quantitative and computational research programs that will advance our understanding of biomolecular and cellular processes. Research programs that combine experimental and computational approaches are welcome. The Department, which is a member of both the Yale Faculty of Arts & Sciences and the Yale School of Medicine, pursues a broad range of basic and applied research topics that contribute to the undergraduate teaching and medical research missions of the University. Applications from candidates interested in Yale priority areas (see the University-Wide Science Strategic Plan and the Yale School of Medicine Research Strategic Planning ), are especially encouraged. The Department is especially interested in candidates who, through their research, teaching, service, and interactions with other departments, will contribute to the excellence of the academic community across multiple dimensions. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Applicants must have met the requirements for a PhD or equivalent degree at time of hire in quantitative and computational biophysics and biochemistry or a related field. Communication skills conducive to excellence in teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels are necessary. Applicants should create a profile on Interfolio https://apply.interfolio.com/193444 and upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of current and future research plans (3 page maximum), teaching statement (1 page maximum, with attachments such as syllabi allowed), and up to 5 reprints of papers published or in press, and 3 confidential letters of evaluation. Review of applications will begin on October 31, 2026, and will continue until the search is closed. Candidates must be available to attend an in-person symposium during the week of January 11, 2027. Please address questions to Lisa Serman, Chair’s Assistant, at lisa.serman@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193518": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Soviet and Post-Soviet Culture",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: Slavic Languages and Literatures Location: New Haven, CT Yale University's Department of Slavic Languages and Literatures invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position in Soviet and/or post-Soviet culture, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate would teach graduate and undergraduate courses on Soviet and/or post-Soviet culture and contribute service to the department and university. The area of specialization is fully open. Near-native knowledge of Russian is required, with proficiency in other relevant languages considered a plus. Candidates need a PhD or equivalent in Slavic, Comparative Literature, or a related field by the time of hire. Materials addressed to Professor Marijeta Bozovic, Chair Submitted via Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/193518 Required: cover letter, current CV, writing sample (max 25 pages, prepared for anonymous review), and three letters of recommendation from outside Yale Deadline: October 20, 2026, with review continuing until filled Preliminary interviews conducted by Zoom Contact for questions: marijeta.bozovic@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193823": {
      "title": "Co-Chair and Open-Rank Faculty Position of Playwriting Program",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: David Geffen School of Drama at Yale Location: New Haven, CT David Geffen School of Drama (DGSD) at Yale University seeks an experienced and dynamic theatre practitioner to lead a pre-eminent MFA program in Playwriting. The Geffen School, in partnership with Yale Repertory Theatre (YRT), trains and advances leaders in the practice of every theatrical discipline, making art to inspire joy, empathy, and understanding in the world. DGSD’s and Yale Rep’s core values are artistry, belonging, collaboration, and discovery: working together as a medical school and teaching hospital might, our community comprises eight three-year MFA programs—Acting, Design, Directing, Dramaturgy and Dramatic Criticism, Playwriting, Stage Management, Technical Design and Production, and Theater Management—as well as a one-year Technical Internship program. DGSD is committed to the development of a robust theater landscape and makes access a priority: all students in degree and certificate programs receive 100% tuition remission. The Co-Chair of the Playwriting program reports to the Dean of DGSD and, in collaboration with the Co-Chair, supervises all activities of the Playwriting Program, as well as teaching classes and serving as a mentor to students. In addition to offering classes in the craft, the Playwriting program produces projects for each year’s cohort in which they collaborate with students from other disciplines in the school: New Play Lab (first year), Langston Hughes Festival (second year), and the Carlotta Festival (third year). RESPONSIBILITIES Teaching and Mentoring 1. Establish curriculum and class schedule, balancing pedagogical needs with budgetary constraints as well as faculty and space availability. 2. Teach two (2) courses in each of the fall and spring semesters. 3. Oversee quality of teaching; participate in review of faculty. Ensure ongoing student review and evaluation. 4. Conduct script analysis tutorials and production-oriented tutorials with playwriting students for New Play Labs, Langston Hughes Festival, and Carlotta Festival productions as needed. 5. Establish and communicate departmental expectations and requirements to playwriting students. Support, guide, encourage and evaluate their progress. 6. Foster DGSD connections to field resources and promote career placement for playwriting students and alumni. 7. Promote a culture of mutual respect, collaboration, and inclusion. 8. Other duties as requested by the Dean. Program Administration 1. Collaborate with DGSD Deans and Chairs to determine strategy and policy. 2. Determine and implement student recruitment strategy and process. In concert with Playwriting Program faculty, participate in selecting incoming class, including but not limited to, reading scripts, conducting interviews, prioritizing top choices and alternates, following up with admitted students concerning site visits and matriculation. 3. Hire faculty, including but not limited to, conducting searches, interviews, setting up and observing demonstration classes, calling references. In concert with the Dean and Associate Dean/Managing Director establish salaries; negotiate salaries. 4. Select, contract, and supervise Lecturers, visiting faculty, and workshop leaders. 5. Determine, oversee, and monitor Playwriting Program budget and departmental work-study assignments. 6. Collaborate with the Student Labor Supervisor on all work-study related matters. 7. Collaborate with Managing Director’s Office and Casting Director to hire guest artists for the Workshop with Actors course, as well as for other projects, as necessary. 8. Serve as the central coordinator and information point for DGSD departments on the work of the playwrights and all aspects of the department. 9. Handle requests for information about the program from prospective faculty, students, and the field, as well as recommendations for students and graduates as appropriate. 10. Represent Program and serve as primary department liaison and expert resource for DGSD, Yale, and the field. 11. Other related duties as requested by Dean. Production Supervision 1. Supervise script selection and development of student plays. 2. Work closely with Dean and Chairs of Directing, Dramaturgy, and Technical Design and Production Programs on scheduling and selection of Playwright/Director/Dramaturg teams. 3. Work closely with Dean and Chair of Acting Program on casting of Langston Hughes Festival and Carlotta Festival Productions. 4. Work closely with Design Program Advisors on the development of designs for Carlotta Festival Productions. 5. Coordinate industry outreach, travel, and accommodations for the Carlotta Festival. 6. Monitor Carlotta Festival marketing copy, proofread marketing materials, and contribute to creating copy as required. 7. Promote and champion Carlotta Festival plays with agents, national and local theatres, and new play development centers. RANK AND TERM OF APPOINTMENT The appointment will be at an open rank commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience (Assistant Professor Adjunct/Associate Professor Adjunct/Professor in the Practice), for a term of no less than three years beginning July 1, 2027, renewable, and includes competitive salary with full faculty benefits. Minimum base salary: $110K. Plus an administrative supplement of $15K tied to the role of Co-Chair. EDUCATION/EXPERIENCE Applicants should have at least 10 years of directly related professional experience combining work in the theater and teaching in the field. Preferred: BA or MFA in Drama or another Fine Arts Degree TRAITS AND ATTRIBUTES The successful candidate will possess: • A track record of artistry, scholarship, teaching and/or service in their communities. • Strongly demonstrated skills in written and verbal communication, strategic thinking, prioritization, time-management, and problem solving. • Ability to function calmly, effectively, and flexibly in an active and collaborative environment. • Demonstrated leadership. • Knowledge of the professional production practices and the various disciplines involved. We invite you to apply by submitting a cover letter, C.V., a teaching statement (philosophy), and the names of three (3) references. These references will receive a request from Interfolio. They must accept this request in order for your application to be considered, however, the committee will ask for a recommendation letter only if you advance beyond the first round of review. You are responsible for sharing this information, and any subsequent updates, with your references. Materials must be submitted through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/193823. Review of applications will begin Wednesday, October 21, 2026, with final considerations on Wednesday, November 4, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193436": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Applied Data Science",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 17, 2026 Deadline: Sep 18, 2027 Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Statistics and Data Science Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Statistics and Data Science (S&DS) at Yale University invites applications for an open-rank faculty position (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek statisticians and data scientists whose research is motivated by important real-world problems and contributes to new statistical, computational, and/or machine learning methodologies to address them. The search is broad and welcomes research spanning modern statistical methods, machine learning, AI, and emerging approaches to data science, with applications across a wide range of scientific, social, and technological domains. We especially value research that engages deeply with substantive questions and benefits from, or contributes to, sustained collaborations with researchers and practitioners in other fields. The Department of S&DS at Yale has experienced substantial and sustained growth in recent years, with significant expansion of its faculty and interdisciplinary connections across the University. The department includes faculty members with joint appointments in a number of other departments and programs, reflecting the broad reach of statistics and data science at Yale. Current faculty have Ph.D.’s in fields including Applied Mathematics, Brain & Cognitive Science, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mathematics, Political Science, and Statistics. Excellence in teaching and advising in Statistics and Data Science is highly valued, and new faculty will have opportunities to develop courses that align with their research interests. The department is collegial and seeks faculty with strong interpersonal skills who can broaden Yale’s intellectual community and effectively teach and mentor students with diverse backgrounds, interests, and career goals. More information about the department may be found at https://statistics.yale.edu Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at the time of hire. Interested candidates should submit the following materials online at https://apply.interfolio.com/193436 Applicants should submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, and a teaching statement. Candidates seeking an appointment without tenure should arrange to have three confidential letters of recommendation submitted via Interfolio. Candidates seeking an appointment with tenure are not required to provide recommendation letters but may choose to arrange for one or two confidential letters of recommendation submitted via Interfolio . Sharing a public Google Scholar page and an academic webpage are strongly encouraged. A helpful teaching statement should describe the candidate’s teaching experience and explain how they could contribute to the curriculum at Yale. Questions regarding the application process can be addressed to Ms. Cheri Cercone, Faculty and Academic Affairs Assistant, at sds_chair@yale.edu The department will begin evaluating applications after November 1 , 202 6 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193767": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor- Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Neonatology Location: New Haven, CT An Assistant/Associate Professor of Pediatrics Full-time faculty position in the Section of Neonatal Perinatal Medicine Yale University School of Medicine is available immediately. This position is predominantly with clinical responsibilities at the Level IV NICU at Yale-New Haven Children’s Hospital in New Haven, CT, including neonatal ECMO, and likely some responsibilities at the Level III-B NICU in Greenwich Hospital. The ideal candidate will have a strong interest in neonatal neurocritical care. The position also includes participation in the academic missions of the Section in clinical care excellence, in delivery of high-quality education, and in superb scholarly programs. The educational mission comprises clinical training of residents, fellows, and multidisciplinary students. This area boasts a beautiful shoreline, affordable housing, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to Boston, Newport, Cape Cod, New York, and the ski slopes of New England. Applicants should be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine and qualified for an appointment to the faculty at Yale School of Medicine. Interested applicants should submit Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and 3 letters of reference electronically to https://apply.interfolio.com/193767. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please address inquiries to Dr. Sarah Taylor, Neonatology Section Chief, at sarah.n.taylor@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193764": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Pediatric Infectious Disease",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Infectious Disease Location: New Haven, CT The PI is a pediatric infectious diseases physician and physician-scientist with a background in basic, translational, or clinical health research spanning pediatric infectious diseases and global health. The Section of Pediatric Infectious Diseases and Global Health at Yale has a long history of federal and non-federal research funding and offers strong institutional support to help new faculty researchers build independent research programs. Section faculty maintain active research programs spanning molecular epidemiology and pathogenesis of respiratory and vector-borne viral infections, viral oncogenesis, helminth and tropical disease immunology, cystic fibrosis-associated pulmonary infection, vaccine epidemiology and clinical trials, and transplant and immunocompromised host infectious diseases. The section is affiliated with the Yale Institute for Global Health, the Center for Infection and Immunity, and the Center for Global Infectious Disease Research, and collaborates with epidemiologists, computational biologists, and global health researchers domestically and at international partner sites. The role will include bench work including tissue culture and tissue processing, performance of molecular assays, and data analysis. T he career pathway focuses initially on development or utilization of research materials, techniques, or technologies, research method/design development, research staff and trainee training and supervision, and management/training for major laboratory equipment. In time, there is opportunity for major roles in project direction, leading/participating in scholarly products, and supporting the preparation of grant applications. The ideal candidate will possess strong experience and knowledge in the areas of cellular and molecular biology and have the ability to perform bioinformatics/systems biology analysis. Eagerness to learn new cutting edge techniques is required. Evidence for clinical perspective is preferred but not required. However, a sense of purpose and dedication toward the goal of clinical application of research discovery is required. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, three letters of reccomendation and cover letter to: https://apply.interfolio.com/193764"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193753": {
      "title": "Neurosurgical Oncology/General Neurosurgery (2368)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurosurgery Location: New Haven The Department of Neurosurgery at Yale School of Medicine is accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor with expertise in general neurosurgery, spine and subspecialty interest in the surgical treatment of brain tumors. The interested candidate should have completed an ACGME accredited neurosurgical residency and be interested in joining a busy clinical program. Fellowship training in neurosurgical oncology in primary tumors is required for this position. Candidates must hold an MD or equivalent and be board certified or board eligible. The candidate should be facile in the surgical management of spinal disorders and brain tumors with a focus and emphasis on complex primary brain and skull-based tumors (i.e. gliomas, meningiomas, schwannomas). The candidate will be joining a high volume neurosurgical practice with a heavily integrated research enterprise and will be able to develop a robust practice while having the guidance and mentorship of our team. The applicant should have a strong interest in teaching and mentoring with an excellent team of residents and fellows, as well as be committed to enhancing our field with contributions through clinical/translational or basic science research. Interested individuals should forward a cover letter, CV and three names of individuals that would support your application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193585": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Interventional Psychiatric Services Old Saybrook",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: Old Saybrook, CT The Yale School of Medicine seeks applicants for a full-time faculty position that will carry an academic appointment at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Psychiatry, Interventional Psychiatry Program. The faculty member will provide evaluations and treatments in clinical and clinical research protocols conducted through the programs and assist in the coverage of the inpatient mood disorders unit. Candidates are required to have clinical experience with electroconvulsive therapy, and ideally will also have prior experience with ketamine/esketamine or transcranial magnet stimulation (TMS) treatments of mood disorders. Previous experience in clinical research, and inpatient psychiatry is highly desired. This work will be performed at any of the IPS locations in New Haven or Old Saybrook. Yale-New Haven Hospital is the major teaching and clinical research facility of the Yale University School of Medicine and consistently ranks among the best hospitals in the United States. Yale-New Haven Hospital encompasses the Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital a 118 bed, acute care, psychiatric facility that consists of five main inpatient programs and several specialized step-down intensive outpatient/day hospital programs for adolescents and adults across two hospital campus locations and access to Interventional Psychiatric Services including ECT and Ketamine. Benefits Yale University offers Yale Signature Benefits, including but not limited to: - Medical coverage through Yale Health and Aetna - Dental coverage through Delta Dental - Vision coverage options through Eyemed - Yale University Retirement Account Plan - Paid time off - Disability coverage - Life insurance - Mortgage loan program - Commuter benefits - Yale Homebuyer program - College tuition benefit plan Yale - Advantage discount program (Discounts for Activities, Travel, services, shopping, etc.) Living in/near New Haven New Haven is recognized as a city of innovation, culture, diversity, and prosperity. It is located between Boston and New York on Long Island Sound, and has outstanding cultural amenities (museums, theater, music, and sports), award-winning restaurants (including several of the nation’s best pizza parlors), boutique shops and national brands, quaint neighborhoods and bustling downtown areas with a variety of living options. New Haven is accessible by plane, train, and automobile, and is easy to navigate on foot, by bicycle, or bus. A free shuttle service provided by Yale covers many areas in the city. Applicants must be a licensed physician in CT and be legally employable. Applicants should upload a curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation to Interfolio using this link: apply.interfolio.com/193585 . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193602": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- VA CT- Neuropsychiatry",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: West Haven, CT VA Connecticut Healthcare System and Yale University School of Medicine, Department of Psychiatry are recruiting a Psychiatrist with experience and interest in mood disorders, psychotic disorders and other serious mental illness to serve as an attending at VA CT Healthcare System. The applicant will work with a multidisciplinary team of healthcare professionals in order to provide evaluation, consultation and treatment for patients in an outpatient setting, including opportunities to work in the Treatment Refractory Depression Clinic providing ketamine, rTMS, ECT and other cutting-edge treatments. The individual will also be responsible for teaching residents, medical students and other trainees, and will be responsible for initiating scholarly work related to teaching or research. Applicants must be board eligible or certified in psychiatry and be legally employable.  Preference will be given to applicants who have relevant clinical experience in these specific clinical areas and related disorders and a history of academic productivity including publications and/or independent funding and be in a position to initiate and produce scholarly work. Interested applicants can submit a CV and 3 letters of recommendation to https://apply.interfolio.com/193602. Questions related to this position can be directed to Ismene Petrakis, MD Chief of Mental Health Services of VA CT Healthcare System, 950 Campbell Ave, West Haven, CT 06516."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193615": {
      "title": "Cardiothoracic Imaging Radiologist (1738, 1740)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging at Yale University School of Medicine is seeking board eligible/certified radiologists with expertise in cardiothoracic imaging for a faculty appointment on the Academic Clinician or Clinician Educator Scholar track. Academic rank at Yale School of Medicine will be commensurate with experience, training, and achievements. The Cardiothoracic Division at the Yale Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging has a track record of providing highest quality, timely and up to date cardiothoracic imaging using state-of-the-art equipment.  The members of the Division are extremely highly valued by all collaborating clinical colleagues for our subspecialist expertise.  We provide cardiothoracic imaging services across the Yale New Haven Health System and are now looking for new skilled attendings to join our team of 13 cardiothoracic radiologists. The Thoracic Section within the Cardiothoracic Division has a close working, interactive relationship with world-renowned pulmonologists, thoracic surgeons, oncologists, radiation oncologists, pathologists, and subspecialists in other fields of medicine. The Cardiac Section within the Cardiothoracic Division, is comprised of both Radiologists and Cardiologists who jointly offer all aspects of cardiac CT and MRI Imaging, The educational mission of the Cardiothoracic Imaging Division extends across all levels of learners and for both radiology and cardiology trainees. Sessions will be performed at Yale New Haven and at Bridgeport Hospitals, the latter being an affiliate of Yale-New Haven Health, located in vibrant Fairfield County, Connecticut, just outside the New York metropolitan area. Board eligible/certified Radiologists with expertise in cardiothoracic imaging are encouraged to apply. Strong clinical leadership, teaching and service development successes may be used for promotion to Associate and Full Professor. Leadership roles and other opportunities for professional development are available depending on the applicant’s interest, goals and experience.  A commitment to teaching residents and fellows is also required. Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to: apply.interfolio.com/193615 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193048": {
      "title": "Lector/Senior Lector I, Vietnamese, Council on Southeast Asian Studies",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: MacMillan Center Location: New Haven, CT The Council on Southeast Asia Studies (CSEAS) at the Whitney and Betty MacMillan Center for International and Area Studies at Yale University invites applications for a Lector in Vietnamese with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for three years, with the possibility of renewal depending on successful performance and ongoing curricular need. Full-time Lectors at Yale teach six courses or the equivalent per academic year, which may be realized as five term courses with a sixth course equivalent of advising and/or other administrative service. Primary duties each academic year will include teaching elementary courses and intermediate courses in Vietnamese in four learning-skill areas: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. Additional advanced language courses will focus on literary, social, political, cultural and/or sociolinguistics topics related to Vietnamese (as determined on the basis of the appointee’s qualifications and expertise). The Lector will advise students and work alongside Yale’s Indonesian and Filipino (Tagalog) language lectors to engage in program building of Southeast Asian Studies at Yale, specifically, in developing overseas language and other study opportunities. They will also engage in developing the broad curriculum and the pedagogic materials for Vietnamese. We are especially interested in candidates whose language and content expertise will complement existing cross-disciplinary scholarship in CSEAS. The successful candidate may also be expected to teach through Yale’s shared course initiative , in which language classrooms across partner institutions are connected via advanced videoconferencing. CSEAS lectors are encouraged to participate in the wide range of professional development opportunities offered through the MacMillan Center, the Center for Language Study, the Poorvu Center for Teaching and Learning, and the Faculty of Arts and Sciences Dean’s Office. Full-time lectors are eligible for Yale’s generous package of benefits, including health coverage. Salary and rank are commensurate with experience and qualifications. If the initial appointment is at the rank of Lector, a promotion review for Senior Lector I must take place in the fifth year or earlier. Senior Lectors at Yale are expected to participate in teaching-related professional activities (e.g., workshops, seminars, training activities, conferences) and have no limits on reappointment, provided the performance is successful and there is ongoing curricular need. The successful candidate must have: 1) native or near-native fluency in Vietnamese; 2) proficiency in English; 3) a bachelor's degree or the equivalent, by the time of hire; 4) experience in teaching Vietnamese as a second language in a college or university environment. It is strongly preferred that the applicants have: 1) an M.A. or other advanced degree in Southeast Asian languages/literatures/linguistics, second language pedagogy, second language acquisition (SLA), applied linguistics, or other related field; and 2) demonstrated ability and enthusiasm for in-class teaching/acquisition, familiarity with language training programs in Southeast Asia, experience with technologically aided language learning methods and their development, interest in the broader field of Southeast Asian Studies and/or other relevant disciplines. Applicants should submit a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a one-page teaching statement; evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., syllabi, course materials, evaluations, teaching video); and three letters of recommendation. We will accept applications immediately with review beginning on October 30, 2026 and continuing until the selections are final. All information from the applicant should be submitted electronically through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/193048 For questions, please contact: Ei Ei Khin, Senior Program Manager, Council on Southeast Asia Studies (CSEAS), The Whitney and Betty MacMillan Center for International and Area Studies, 34 Hillhouse Avenue, P.O. Box 208206 New Haven, CT 06520-8206 USA.  Email: ei.khin@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193258": {
      "title": "Surgery, Surgical Oncology Breast, Assistant, Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Surgical Oncology Location: New Haven, CT  Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology Yale University, School of Medicine The Department of Surgery, Division of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery at the Yale School of Medicine, with expertise in breast reconstruction and microsurgery to join our growing team and serve as Section Chief, Breast Reconstruction . We are seeking an Associate Professor / Assistant Professor level candidate; rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. In addition to clinical duties, our faculty members provide educational training to medical students, residents, and fellows and actively contribute to the academic and research missions of the Department. Applicants should expect to work in a collegial and collaborative environment providing patient-centered care in a multidisciplinary fashion. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the breast reconstruction program and work closely with Breast Surgical Oncology and colleagues across Smilow Cancer Hospital and Yale Cancer Center to further strengthen and grow Yale’s comprehensive breast reconstruction program. Yale Medicine has a wide referral network of primary and specialty care physicians throughout Connecticut and the region. We are seeking candidates with an academic orientation in clinical care, research, and education and demonstrated expertise in reconstructive breast surgery, including microsurgical and implant-based reconstruction. Candidates will join a world-class multidisciplinary breast team at the NCI-Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center at Smilow Cancer Hospital at Yale New Haven and Yale Cancer Center. Seeking a board eligible/board-certified plastic surgeon with expertise in breast reconstruction and microsurgery. Candidates should have exceptional interpersonal and leadership skills and a commitment to advancing the field of breast reconstruction. In addition to program planning and development, candidates should have experience in quality improvement, education, multidisciplinary collaboration, and operational development. All application materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/193258 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Should you have any questions, please reach out to: Name: Bohdan Pomahac, MD Title: Division Chief, Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery Email: Bohdan.Pomahac@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193244": {
      "title": "Surgery, Thoracic Surgery, Assistant, Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Thoracic Surgery Location: New Haven, CT  Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology Yale University, School of Medicine The Department of Surgery at Yale School of Medicine is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible thoracic surgeon to join the Division of Thoracic Surgery at the Assistant or Associate Professor level on the Clinician-Educator Scholar or Academic Clinican Track. The successful candidate will join a highly collaborative and established thoracic surgery program providing comprehensive care to patients with diseases of the chest, including thoracic malignancies, esophageal disease, and other complex thoracic conditions. The position is intended to support continued growth and clinical capacity within the New Haven practice and VA as the Division expands its regional thoracic surgery presence across the Yale New Haven Health System. Candidates should have demonstrated expertise in general thoracic surgery, with experience in minimally invasive and robotic surgical techniques strongly preferred. The successful candidate will participate in the multidisciplinary care of patients with thoracic malignancies and work closely with colleagues across medical oncology, radiation oncology, pulmonary medicine, gastroenterology, radiology, pathology, and other specialties. Responsibilities will include the evaluation and surgical management of thoracic surgical patients, participation in multidisciplinary tumor programs, inpatient and outpatient clinical care, and shared call responsibilities. The position will also include opportunities to participate in the education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Surgeons on the Clinician Educator Scholar track typically advance the Department’s academic mission through research in quality improvement, clinical research, and other academic activities consistent with the candidate’s interests and experience. Applicants must have an MD or equivalent degree, be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut, and be board certified or board eligible in Thoracic Surgery. Academic rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. All application materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/193244 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Should you have any questions, please reach out to: Daniel Boffa, MD Division Chief, Thoracic Surgery Yale School of Medicine Email: Daniel.Boffa@yale.edu Phone: (203) 785-4931"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192466": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Synthetic Biology and Genomics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Biological Science: Molecular, Cellular, and Developmental Biology Location: New Haven, CT  The Department of Molecular, Cellular and Developmental Biology (MCDB) at Yale University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose biological research program resides within synthetic biology, genomics, or artificial intelligence. We also welcome applications from candidates in any area of molecular, cellular, or developmental biology, using any system, who will contribute to the excellence of our community of scholars. We expect the appointee to be a dynamic participant in the departmental mission of teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels in subject areas such as molecular, cellular or developmental biology, biochemistry, genetics, genomics, systems or synthetic biology, plant biology, or neurobiology. The selected candidate must have met the requirements for a Ph.D. or equivalent degree at the time of hire, as well as a proven record of outstanding research that demonstrates originality and self-motivation. Excellent communication skills for research and teaching are necessary. (NOTE: Interviews and talks will be part of a two-day symposium scheduled for January 7-8, 2027) Applicants should create a profile at http://apply.interfolio.com/ 192466 and upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research plans (up to three pages), a teaching statement (one page), and up to five publications. Applicants should also arrange for submission of three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. For questions about the position or application process please contact Mrs. Lucia DeMatteo, Academic Services Supervisor, at mcdb.businessoffice@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193025": {
      "title": "Surgery, Plastic Surgery – Section Chief of Reconstructive Breast Surgery (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Plastic Surgery Location: New Haven, CT  Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology Yale University, School of Medicine The Department of Surgery, Division of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery at the Yale School of Medicine, is currently seeking a board eligible/board-certified plastic surgeon with expertise in breast reconstruction and microsurgery to join our growing team and serve as Section Chief, Breast Reconstruction . We are seeking an Assistant Professor/ Assosciate Professor or Professor-level candidate; rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. In addition to clinical duties, our faculty members provide educational training to medical students, residents, and fellows and actively contribute to the academic and research missions of the Department. Applicants should expect to work in a collegial and collaborative environment providing patient-centered care in a multidisciplinary fashion. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the breast reconstruction program and work closely with Breast Surgical Oncology and colleagues across Smilow Cancer Hospital and Yale Cancer Center to further strengthen and grow Yale’s comprehensive breast reconstruction program. Yale Medicine has a wide referral network of primary and specialty care physicians throughout Connecticut and the region. We are seeking candidates with an academic orientation in clinical care, research, and education and demonstrated expertise in reconstructive breast surgery, including microsurgical and implant-based reconstruction. Candidates will join a world-class multidisciplinary breast team at the NCI-Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center at Smilow Cancer Hospital at Yale New Haven and Yale Cancer Center. Candidates should have exceptional interpersonal and leadership skills and a commitment to advancing the field of breast reconstruction. In addition to program planning and development, candidates should have experience in quality improvement, education, multidisciplinary collaboration, and operational development. All application materials should be submitted electronically to: http://apply.interfolio.com/ 193025 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Should you have any questions, please reach out to: Name: Maren Crawford Title: Senior Physician Recruiter, Department of Surgery Email: maren.crawford@yale.edu Phone/Text: 475-339-6083"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192754": {
      "title": "Associate Research Scientist or Postdoctoral Associate in Computational Immunology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pathology Location: Department of Pathology, YSM The Kleinstein and Yaari labs at Yale School of Medicine are seeking a highly motivated researcher to develop computational methods for multiomic immune profiling, with an emphasis on adaptive immune receptor repertoire sequencing (AIRR-seq). The position can be Associate Research Scientist (research rank faculty) or Postdoctoral Associate , depending on experience. The successful candidate will develop statistical and machine-learning approaches for integrating AIRR-seq with single-cell RNA-seq, paired BCR/TCR data, genomics, immune phenotyping, germline variation, and clinical or experimental metadata. Potential projects include genotype-aware repertoire analysis, modeling clonal expansion and public/private receptor sharing, scalable software development, and applications to vaccination, infection, autoimmunity, and population-scale immune variation. The project will be jointly mentored by Steven Kleinstein and Gur Yaari, combining expertise in computational immunology, AIRR-seq software development, immunogenomics, antibody repertoire analysis, germline variation, and statistical modeling. The successful candidate will join a collaborative environment focused on developing rigorous, interpretable methods that address important biological questions. The ideal candidate will have strong quantitative and programming skills. Experience with AIRR-seq, BCR/TCR repertoire analysis, single-cell genomics, multiomic integration, statistical modeling, or machine learning is desirable but not required. Candidates from computational biology, bioinformatics, computer science, statistics, applied mathematics, physics, bioengineering, immunology, or related fields are encouraged to apply. The position offers opportunities to publish methodological and biological studies, develop open-source software, collaborate with leading immunology and computational biology groups, and contribute to widely used community resources for immune repertoire analysis. All application materials should be uploaded through interfolio, at apply.interfolio.com/192754 .  These include a CV, a brief statement of research interests, and contact information for references.  Specific inquiries may be directed to: Steven Kleinstein: Steven.Kleinstein@yale.edu Gur Yaari: Gur.Yaari@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172321": {
      "title": "Associate Professor with Tenure, Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 01, 2026 Deadline: Aug 31, 2028 Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Biomedical Informatics and Data Science Location: New Haven, CT Associate with Tenure/Full Professor of Biomedical Informatics & Data Science The Department of Biomedical Informatics and Data Science (BIDS) at Yale University School of Medicine invites applications for Associate Professor w/ Tenure and Full Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research and education. Multiple positions will be filled each year. Areas of interest include: • Artificial intelligence in medicine • Biomedical data modeling and ontologies • Biomedical data science • Biomedical natural language processing and knowledge representation • Clinical informatics • Clinical research informatics • Computational biology and bioinformatics • Human computer interaction and usability • Privacy technology Responsibilities include establishing a vigorous and independently funded research program while supervising and mentoring students with diverse backgrounds plus contributing to the graduate and medical school educational missions. We seek individuals with strong records of independent creative accomplishments, who will interact productively with colleagues within the Department and across Yale School of Medicine and the University. We foster an environment of collaboration and scientific discovery, and we value the exchange of new ideas and novel approaches to research, training, and service. Joint appointments with other departments will also be supported. Leadership roles will be considered according to the candidates' interests and prior accomplishments. Strong scientific, management, and interpersonal skills are required. Appointment at the Associate Professor or Full Professor levels will be based on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Biomedical Informatics and Data Science (BIDS) at Yale University is a newly established self-standing Department within Yale School of Medicine, which has a rich history of pre-eminence in biomedical research and clinical care. BIDS faculty are known nationally and internationally for their contributions to biomedical informatics and data science and multidisciplinary collaborations. Today, research at the Yale School of Medicine encompasses a broad range of fields, with researchers aiming to understand, prevent, and treat human disease in a personalized and equitable manner. Yale’s new findings in basic and translational science inform and synergize with impactful clinical research, and with implementation and evaluation of systems in real clinical settings. For more details, see https://medicine.yale.edu/biomedical-informatics-data-science/ . Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research and education. Please submit a cover letter describing qualifications, along with a CV, a two-page summary of current and proposed research, and three letters of reference to one of the following Interfolio websites: https://apply.interfolio.com/172321 Consideration of applications will begin 10/1/2025 on a rolling basis."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192690": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Hemostasis and Thrombosis Program",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Hematology / Oncology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Pediatrics, Section of Hematology/Oncology at the Yale University School of Medicine is seeking an outstanding, full-time Pediatric Hematologist/Oncologist who will be on the academic clinician track at the Assistant Professor level. This position will be primarily within the Hemostasis and Thrombosis program. The clinical focus will be on the care of patients with bleeding and clotting disorders including specialized care of young women and girls with bleeding disorders.  The Hematologist/Oncologist should be committed to excellent clinical care and program development with enthusiasm for improving the quality of care for hemostasis and thrombosis. The job may also include clinical responsibilities at other ambulatory locations of YNHCH specifically those in New Haven and Fairfield counties. The ideal candidate will be enthusiastic about participation in the clinical, research, and educational mission of the Section, including training of residents and fellows, and the opportunity to participate in quality improvement efforts, clinical scholarship, and research. Southern Connecticut boasts beautiful shoreline, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York City, as well as the New England shore and ski areas. Applicants should be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Hematology/Oncology and qualified for an appointment to the faculty at Yale School of Medicine. Training and experience specific to Hemostasis and Thrombosis is strongly preferred. Interested applicants should submit Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and a list of 3 References to: https://apply.interfolio.com/192690. Please address inquiries, along with curriculum vitae, to Lakshmanan Krishnamurti, MD, Professor of Pediatrics, Section Chief of Hematology/Oncology at lakshmanan.krishnamurti@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192694": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Pediatric Endocrinology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Endocrinology Location: New Haven, CT Yale University School of Medicine, Department of Pediatrics, is recruiting a pediatric endocrinologist with expertise in evaluation and treatment of pediatric obesity. This individual would have a unique opportunity to serve as Medical Director for Bright Bodies, the internationally recognized intensive health behavior and lifestyle treatment (IHBLT) that started at Yale. In this capacity, they would build on existing infrastructure with an opportunity to grow the program. In addition, the successful candidate will join our internationally renowned section of 17 pediatric endocrinologists and 8 advanced practice providers, providing clinical care in our New Haven and Trumbull offices. Our section includes physician-scientists with cutting edge programs across a spectrum of areas including clinical care and clinical, translational and basic research in endocrinology, diabetes, obesity, metabolism, thyroid disorders and bone disease. The candidate will devote most of their efforts to our clinical mission, with a focus on obesity care, and will be instrumental in the expansion of our endocrinology services throughout the Yale-New Haven Health system. The applicant will also have opportunities to participate in collaborative and independent research projects. In this role, applicants must demonstrate a track-record of providing outstanding clinical care in inpatient and outpatient settings, as well as expertise for teaching and supervising medical students, residents and endocrinology fellows. Southern Connecticut offers beautiful shoreline, affordable housing, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York, Boston, Newport, Cape Cod, and the ski slopes of New England. Board eligible/certification in Pediatric Endocrinology is required. Board certification in Obesity Medicine is favorable. Interested applicants should submit a Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and a list of 3 references electronically to:https://apply.interfolio.com/192694. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192582": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Neuro-Urologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Urology Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Urology is a nationally recognized academic department dedicated to excellence in patient care, research, and education. We are seeking a faculty member with expertise in Neurourology to join our Division of Lower Urinary Tract Dysfunction and Reconstruction (LUTDR), and advance our clinical, research, and educational missions. This position will be based primarily at Yale New Haven Hospital in New Haven, Connecticut. The candidate will also have the unique opportunity to practice at the Adams Neurosciences Center, a new clinical facility dedicated to the comprehensive care of patients with neurological disorders. This setting will facilitate multidisciplinary collaboration and provide opportunities to develop innovative clinical and research programs at the intersection of urology and neuroscience. There are additional opportunities for collaboration with faculty across Yale School of Medicine and Yale New Haven Health System who share complementary clinical and research interests. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to clinical and academic excellence with the focus on outstanding patient care and innovation.   An active interest in research is a requirement of the position, with opportunities to pursue and expand clinical, translational, or population-based research programs aligned with the candidate’s interests and expertise.  Research areas of particular interests includes neurogenic bladder, bladder innervation, and bladder physiology. Dedicated laboratory space and protected research time will be available for qualified candidates. We welcome applications from early-career and established academic urologists with formal fellowship training in neurourology. The ideal candidate will possess outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, a commitment to academic and clinical collaboration. The successful candidate will help foster a culture of academic and clinical excellence while advancing the missions of division and department and contributing to the broader mission of Yale School of Medicine and Yale New Haven Health System."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192292": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Economics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Economics Location: New Haven, CT  The Department of Economics invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level . The successful applicant will be expected to teach courses in their field of specialization within Economics, and to engage in research. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Applicants must show promise of outstanding scholarly achievement and the Ph.D., or equivalent degree, must be completed, or its completion should be expected within the first year of appointment. To ensure full consideration, please electronically submit a letter of interest, CV, job market paper, and 3 confidential letters of recommendation to: apply.interfolio.com/192292 before November 7, 2026. If you have specific questions about the position for which you are applying, please contact Nicole Whitcher, Assistant to the Chair, (nicole.whitcher@yale.edu)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192556": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow/Research Associate — Yale School of Medicine, Department of Infectious Disease",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Infectious Diseases Location: New Haven, CT (work travel expected to AL) Position Overview This position is situated within the Department of Infectious Disease at Yale School of Medicine with offices located on the medical school campus in New Haven, CT. The Postdoctoral Associate will conduct independent and collaborative research under the mentorship of Dr. Lynn Matthews, in support of NIH-funded projects in the U.S. South. Specifically, we seek a Postdoctoral Associate to contribute to a multi-year, collaborative research program focused on adapting, implementing, and evaluating a combination intervention to advance the goals of Ending the HIV Epidemic (EHE) in Alabama. The project leverages partnerships among academic investigators and state/local public health agencies to evaluate three CDC evidence-based interventions that aim to: increase HIV testing in priority populations using data-driven “precision public health” approaches, reduce time to linkage to care, and reduce time to viral suppression via rapid ART initiation in community clinics in rural Alabama.  The successful candidate may have the opportunity to contribute to other projects in the U.S. South focused on HIV prevention. Key Responsibilities Data Analysis and Interpretation •                     Contribute to design, execution, and ongoing optimization of the hybrid trial evaluating COAST-AL across Mobile County Health Department (MCHD) service areas. •                     Support measurement and interpretation of key effectiveness and implementation outcomes. •                     Apply implementation science frameworks to guide selection of measures, analytic plans, and interpretation of implementation determinants and outcomes. •                     Support or lead “big data” analyses to identify areas with low testing coverage and inform placement/targeting of community-based HIV testing. •                     Integrate, clean and harmonize multiple data sources (e.g., surveillance, programmatic, and commercial testing datasets) to develop implementation plans Mixed-methods research and intervention adaptation •                     Conduct qualitative data collection and analysis (e.g., semi-structured interviews, rapid qualitative methods as appropriate) to adapt intervention components to local context •                     Assess intervention acceptability, feasibility, and appropriateness among clients (in-depth interviews) and providers (surveys), to guide iterative implementation improvements over time. Partnership and stakeholder engagement •                     Collaborate with Alabama Department of Public Health (ADPH), Mobile County Health Department, and other stakeholders to support implementation, troubleshooting, and interpretation of findings, •                     Identify and prioritize sustainability strategies for intervention scale-up, through facilitation of stakeholder discussions. Scholarly dissemination and mentorship •                     Lead/co-lead manuscripts, conference abstracts, and presentations. •                     Contribute to progress reports and future grant proposals focused on rigorous evaluation of implementation strategies to integrate COAST-AL into public health systems. Compensation and Benefits Salary will be based on the Yale Postdoctoral Compensation policy, and support for travel to conferences may also be available. (https://postdocs.yale.edu/postdocs/being-a-postdoc-at-yale/postdoctoral-compensation) and is aligned with university/NIH-related guidelines as applicable. Qualifications Required Qualifications ·         PhD, DrPH, ScD, MD, or equivalent terminal degree by start date in medicine, public health, implementation science, epidemiology, biostatistics, health services research, behavioral science, sociology, informatics, or a related field. ·         Demonstrated research experience/interest in at least one of the following: implementation science, HIV services research, pragmatic/hybrid trials, mixed methods, or applied public health data science. ·         Strong data analysis skills, including familiarity with Stata/R or similar ·         Proficiency in writing as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications and/or equivalent scholarly output. ·         Ability to work and communicate effectively in cross-institutional, multidisciplinary teams and in partnership with public-sector agencies. Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience applying implementation frameworks (e.g., CFIR, RE-AIM) and measuring implementation outcomes (e.g., acceptability, feasibility, appropriateness). ·         Quantitative skills in causal inference and/or longitudinal/time-to-event methods relevant to study outcomes ·         Experience working with HIV surveillance or administrative datasets, including data governance and privacy/security practices. ·         Qualitative methods expertise (coding, thematic analysis, framework analysis) and comfort integrating qualitative + quantitative findings (i.e., mixed methods). ·         Familiarity with rural health, public health clinics, and/or the Southern U.S. HIV epidemic a plus. Application Instructions Applicants should submit: Cover letter describing research interests and fit Curriculum vitae Writing sample or representative publication (or links) Contact information for 2 references https://apply.interfolio.com/192556"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192328": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Professor- Director of the MEG Center- VA CT Healthcare",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: West Haven, CT Yale University School of Medicine announces an open position for an Associate or Full Professor in the role of Director for the MEG Center of the National Center for post traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) at VA Connecticut Healthcare System (VACHS). The Candidate should have a background and research interests relevant to the cognitive neuroscience of PTSD, recognizing that this is a very broad range of research. The Director is expected to provide strategic, scientific, and operational leadership for the MEG Center, oversee the delivery of high-quality MEG research and clinical research support. The position requires advanced expertise in MEG/EEG data acquisition, experimental design, preprocessing, time-frequency and connectivity analyses, source localization/reconstruction, and interpretation of electrophysiological data, as well as proficiency with relevant computational tools and programming environments (e.g., Brainstorm, MNE, Python, MATLAB) and integration of MEG/EEG with structural and functional neuroimaging modalities. Responsibilities include developing and implementing the Center’s scientific vision, fostering collaborations across investigators and disciplines, overseeing MEG data acquisition and analysis, ensuring appropriate equipment and facility operations, and supporting study design, protocol development, and grant-funded research. The Director will also provide mentorship and guidance to research staff and trainees, promote staff development and technical expertise, and represent the Center within the institution and with external collaborators and research partners. Applicants must have a PhD and be legally employable. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. A CV and 3 letters of recommendation are required. Apply to this position through Interfolio using this link apply.interfolio.com/ 192328."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191057": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Mathematics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Mathematics Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Mathematics at Yale University intends to make one or more offers at the level of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor with tenure, or Full Professor with tenure with an anticipated start date of July 1st, 2027. The positions will be open to all fields of Mathematics. We seek scholars with a record of outstanding achievement in research who are accomplished teachers in mathematics. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in their area of expertise at undergraduate and graduate levels. We are interested in candidates with a breadth of expertise in their area of mathematics. Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Mathematics, or a related field is required at time of hire. Application will open August, 26, 2026. For full consideration, please submit the application by October, 26, 2026. To complete your application, submit the following items to: https://apply.interfolio.com/191057 Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Teaching statement Three confidential letters of recommendation are required for the Assistant Professor level only (to be submitted online by the reference writer; one letter must contain an evaluation of the candidate's teaching) If you have any questions, please email Susie Kim, Faculty & Academic Affairs Coordinator in the Department of Mathematics at math.chair@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192329": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Child Abuse Pediatrician",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Child Safety, Advocacy & Healing Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Pediatrics at the Yale School of Medicine seeks a child abuse pediatrician to join a team of professionals working to prevent child maltreatment, provide clinical care to children suspected of maltreatment, and generate scholarship related to the well-being of children and families. Southern Connecticut offers a beautiful shoreline, affordable housing, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York, Boston, Newport, Cape Cod, and the ski slopes of New England. Applicants should be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Child Abuse and qualified for an appointment to the faculty at Yale School of Medicine as either an Assistant or Associate Professor. Interested applicants should submit their Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter, and a list of 3 Professional References to: http://apply.interfolio.com/ 192329. Please address inquiries, to Andrea Asnes, MD, Search Committee Chair, Department of Pediatrics, PO Box 208064, New Haven, CT 06520, email: andrea.asnes@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192254": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Child Psychology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Child Study Center Location: New Haven, CT Yale Child Study Center Clinical Services has an opening for full-time child psychologist dedicated to providing evaluation and treatment services to young children and their families. The successful candidate will be appointed as an Assistant Professor of Child Psychology on the Academic Clinician ladder track.  A primary focus of this position is to provide developmental assessment and evidence-based treatment for children under ten and their families. Additional job responsibilities include: Conducting developmental and psychological assessments of children and adolescents, providing evidence-based treatment to children and their caregivers, with a special emphasis on services for children aged 10 and younger and their families, providing Child Parent Psychotherapy (CPP) to young children who have experienced traumatic events, collaborating with members of clinical teams to inform comprehensive care plans and participation in the psychology training faculty, including training and supervision of practicum students, psychology interns through the Yale Child Study Center’s APA-accredited internship, and/or post-doctoral fellows on the pediatric psychology track. Successful candidates must possess an APA accredited doctoral degree in psychology, postdoctoral experience in clinical or health service psychology. Licensed or license-eligible child psychologists in the state of Connecticut with the following skills or experience are encouraged to apply: Treatment experience with young children (ages 0-10), including provision of Child Parent Psychotherapy Assessment experience providing developmental and psychological evaluations to children Bilingual clinicians able to provide treatment and assessment in Spanish Candidates from diverse backgrounds This position is available to internal candidates only.  Applicants should submit a CV, three letters of reference, a cover letter outlining their relevant experience, and a de-identified developmental or psychological assessment report for a child under 10. Please send materials to apply.interfolio.com /192254.  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192016": {
      "title": "Quantum Information Science and Engineering Theory Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Engineering and Applied Science: Applied Physics: Yale Quantum Institute Location: New Haven, CT, USA The Yale Quantum Institute (YQI) theory group (Yongshan Ding, Aleksander Kubica, Steven Girvin, Shruti Puri) seeks outstanding applicants for multiple postdoctoral openings in quantum information science and engineering. The start date is flexible. The group has broad research interests and successful candidates will have the opportunity to collaborate with theorists and experimentalists in YQI and elsewhere working on a variety of topics of mutual interest.  Current research interests include (but are not limited to): A variety of quantum platforms: Circuit QED and quantum optics of superconducting circuits Rydberg atom array quantum processors and quantum simulators Trapped-ion systems (qubits and oscillator modes) Quantum Error Correction and Fault-Tolerance: Codes and decoders tailored to biased-noise qubits Code surgery compilation Bosonic codes Statistical Mechanics and Non-Equilibrium Many-Body Physics of Error Correction Circuits Design of parametric processes and quantum control of driven non-linear quantum devices Quantum computer architecture, hardware- and noise-aware compilers Computation with Dynamic Circuits that include mid-circuit measurements and feedforward Quantum simulation of many-body and lattice-gauge theory models Microscopic physics of Josephson junctions Other topics of mutual interest About the Yale Quantum Institute The Yale Quantum Institute (YQI) , founded in 2014, serves as a forum to bring together experimental and theoretical researchers at Yale in the field of quantum information physics, quantum optics and nanophotonics, optomechanics, mesoscopic physics, quantum control, quantum measurement, and quantum many-body physics. It provides a synergistic and collaborative setting for Yale’s cutting edge research in these fields. A report from the University Science Strategy Committee identified quantum science as one of Yale’s top priorities . Yale is playing a major role in the Co-Design Center for Quantum Advantage (C2QA) , one of the five DOE national quantum information science research centers, and throughout the State of Connecticut with QuantumCT, a major NSF Regional Economic Engine award, co-led with UConn .  YQI faculty also lead ERASE, an NSF National Quantum Virtual Laboratory focused on development and deployment of a full-stack quantum error correction testbed based on novel dual-resonator (dual-rail) erasure-flag qubits in collaboration with D-Wave New Haven (formerly Quantum Circuits, Inc. of New Haven). We also lead PRACTIQAL, an NSF Quantum Leap Challenge Institute focused on the Physics and Engineering of Practical Quantum Error Correction. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. ( awarded within the past three years ) in physics, engineering, computer science, or closely allied fields (or have satisfied the requirements for that degree by the time they are hired). Preference will be given to applicants with prior experience in the physics/engineering and/or computer science of quantum information and computation. Terms of Appointment All appointments are granted as renewable 1-year contracts up to 3 years duration by mutual agreement with the advisor.  Appointments generally start at the beginning of the academic year, but alternative starting states can be considered. The salary will be $70,000 per year. This position will follow standard Yale policies for postdoctoral appointments.  For more details, please check this website . Key dates Application deadline: November 1, 2026 at 11:59 pm ET Applications and letters will be considered at any time until the position is filled ( Early applications are encouraged). Rounds of online interviews: Winter 2026 Acceptance notification: January 2027 Enrollment & potential visa application: Spring 2027 Start time: Fall 2027 (flexible start date) To apply, please upload the following documents on the Interfolio portal before November 1, 2026 at 11:59 pm ET: cover letter describing (i) your past training, (ii) research interests, (iii) the group you intend to work in and potential research topics/projects you intend to pursue at Yale, and (iv) your career goals. curriculum vitae publication list and reprints of selected publications (3 maximum) three or more references letters If you have difficulties uploading all your documents, you can combine all these into a single pdf."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192174": {
      "title": "General Consultative Cardiologist - Adams Neuroscience Tower Phase II",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT Position Description The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Qualifications Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Application Instructions Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation. For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189395": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Instructor - PCCSM - Pulmonary Vascular Diseases Program",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Pulmonary Location: New Haven, CT Yale School of Medicine, Section of Pulmonary, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine, is seeking a talented clinician/educator/physician scientist to join the Yale Pulmonary Vascular Diseases Program. This position will begin at the rank of Instructor or Assistant Professor based on experience. This ladder-track faculty position requires participation in research, educational and clinical activities as well as the ability to provide attending coverage of the medical intensive care unit, consultative inpatient services, and ambulatory clinics. Candidates must have outstanding skills in the clinical arena and will have the opportunity to take an active role teaching and mentoring trainees. Significant contributions to the clinical, educational, and research missions of the division are expected. Minimum requirements include board eligibility/certification in pulmonary and critical care medicine, fellowship training in pulmonary vascular diseases, clinical experience in critical care and pulmonary disease, and publication track record. ·         M.D. or equivalent, with board certification in Internal Medicine. ·         Board eligibility/certification in Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Medicine. ·         Fellowship training in pulmonary vascular diseases. All applications materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/189395"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191128": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Statistics and Data Science",
      "description": "Posted: Aug 20, 2026 Deadline: Aug 19, 2027 Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Statistics and Data Science Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Statistics and Data Science at Yale University is seeking applicants for a full-time teaching faculty position at the rank of Lecturer with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. Salary will be based on qualifications and experience. We are looking for candidates with strong teaching skills, a passion for teaching, and experience or interest in innovative pedagogy. Successful candidates will contribute creatively to the teaching and further development of our Statistics & Data Science programs, particularly those courses and experiences oriented towards data analysis and interdisciplinary collaboration. In addition to courses for Statistics & Data Science majors, this position will be involved in the teaching of courses in Statistics and Data Science for students of diverse backgrounds and interests throughout the university. The teaching load will be two classes per semester. More information about the department may be found at https://statistics.yale.edu The appointee must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent degree or have completed all requirements for that degree by the time of hire. Interested candidates should submit the following materials online at https://apply.interfolio.com/191128 A cover letter expressing interest in the position A teaching statement detailing teaching philosophy, experience, and the types of courses they are best suited to teach A current curriculum vitae Three letters of recommendation to be submitted electronically via Interfolio. At least two of these letters should explicitly address the candidate’s teaching effectiveness, pedagogical style, and communication skills in undergraduate statistics and data science courses. All teaching evaluations for up to the last five years Optional materials could include evidence of teaching interest, experience, and effectiveness. Questions about the application can be directed to Ms. Cheri Cercone, Faculty and Academic Affairs Assistant, at sds_chair@yale.edu . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all materials by Oct 15, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191948": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Pediatric Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: Emergency Medicine (Pediatrics) Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Pediatrics, Section of Emergency Medicine at the Yale University School of Medicine is seeking an outstanding, full-time Pediatric Emergency Medicine physician at the Assistant Professor level. Experienced applicants may apply. Final rank and appointment (Academic Clinician) will be determined based on a variety of factors including academic record. This position will focus on clinical responsibilities in any of our three EDs: the tertiary-care center at Yale-New Haven Children’s Hospital in New Haven, CT, Community site at our Bridgeport Hospital campus, located in Bridgeport, CT, and community site at our Greenwich Hospital campus, located in Greenwich, CT.  The Yale Pediatric Hospitalist team provides care for admitted patients and our Pediatric Critical Care Transport Team helps to facilitate interhospital transports. The Section of Pediatric Emergency Medicine at Yale has 28 physicians with expertise and national reputations in research, education, toxicology, simulation, ultrasound, global health, and injury prevention, as well as a successful fellowship program. The PEM physician should be committed to excellent clinical care with enthusiasm for improving the quality of care and education of our patients and staff. Clinical services are supported by a team of advanced practice providers, emergency pediatricians, nurses with pediatric expertise and child life specialists. The ideal candidate will be enthusiastic about participation in the clinical and educational mission of the Section, including training of an outstanding cadre of residents and fellows, and the opportunity to participate in quality improvement efforts, clinical scholarship, and teaching. Southern Connecticut boasts beautiful shoreline, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York City, as well as the New England shore and ski areas. Applicants should be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Emergency Medicine and qualified for an appointment to the faculty at Yale School of Medicine. Interested applicants should submit Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and three letters of reference to: https://apply.interfolio.com/191948. Please address inquiries, along with curriculum vitae, to Rakesh Mistry, MD, MS at rakesh.mistry@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191973": {
      "title": "Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation - Foot & Ankle - Assistant/Associate Professor (RFP-2347)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation are leaders in patient care, education, and surgical innovation. We seek a physician for a full-time faculty position with interest and expertise in Orthopaedic Foot & Ankle Surgery. Responsibilities will include involvement in clinical service, teaching, and research activities. Our department anticipates that the successful candidate will have a dynamic personality, outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to academic collaboration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be board-certified Orthopaedic surgeons with fellowship training in Orthopaedic Foot & Ankle Surgery. Academic appointment will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. All interested candidates are asked to apply via Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/191973 Please provide your curriculum vitae and a cover letter."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190888": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Organic Chemistry",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Chemistry Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Chemistry, Yale University, New Haven, CT invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant/Associate/Full Professor level rank to commence as early as July 1, 2027. We seek creative teacher-scholars to teach inspiring courses and develop outstanding research programs in organic chemistry broadly defined. Must have met the requirements for a PhD or equivalent degree at the time of hire in Organic Chemistry or a related field. Applicants should submit the documents requested below through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/190888 .  To receive full consideration for the first round of interviews, all application materials should be submitted by October 1, 2026. Materials required for applications at all ranks include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a teaching philosophy statement. Applications at the ranks of Assistant Professor should request three confidential letters of recommendation to be submitted on their behalf through Interfolio and provide a future research plan prefaced by a single-page summary, consisting of up to three proposals. Applicants for tenured positions are only asked to provide a research statement summarizing their current research program, and funding sources. For further information contact the Chair of the Chemistry Department, Prof. Nilay Hazari, at chemistry.chair@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190531": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Biophysical or Physical Chemistry",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Chemistry Location: New Haven, CT  The Department of Chemistry, Yale University, New Haven, CT invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level to commence as early as July 1, 2027. We seek creative teacher-scholars to teach inspiring courses and develop outstanding research programs in biophysical or physical chemistry broadly defined. Must have met the requirements for a PhD or equivalent degree at the time of hire in Physical Chemistry or a related field. Applicants should submit the documents requested below through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/195031 . To receive full consideration for the first round of interviews, all application materials should be submitted by October 1, 2026. Materials required for a complete application include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a future research plan prefaced by a single-page summary and consisting of up to three proposals, and a teaching-philosophy statement. The cover letter must clearly state the candidate’s self-identified division(s) of chemistry, e.g. experimental physical chemistry. Applicants should request three confidential letters of recommendation to be submitted on their behalf through Interfolio. Please direct questions to the department chair, Prof. Nilay Hazari, at chemistry.chair@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190675": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Chemistry related to Energy Science",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Physical Science: Chemistry Location: New Haven, CT The Energy Sciences Institute (ESI), in partnership with the Department of Chemistry, Yale University, New Haven, CT, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant/Associate/Full Professor level rank to commence as early as July 1, 2027. The ESI focuses on performing fundamental research that is connected to solving problems connected to the energy sector and is one of seven multidisciplinary research institutes at Yale University’s West Campus. Institute faculty hold a primary appointment in a physical science or engineering department. Currently, we seek to identify candidates whose research interests and accomplishments align with the Institute and the Chemistry Department. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in a relevant discipline, and an outstanding record of research that demonstrates originality in addressing significant questions in the study of energy broadly defined.  Applicants conducting research in materials chemistry with applications related to the conversion of solar energy into storable chemical energy, as well as those with interest in the development of transitional technologies are especially encouraged to apply.  Candidates will need to demonstrate that they can teach undergraduate and graduate courses in chemistry. Must have met the requirements for a PhD or equivalent degree at the time of hire in Energy Science, broadly defined or related field. Materials required for applications at all ranks include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a teaching philosophy statement. Applications at the ranks of Assistant Professor should request three confidential letters of recommendation and provide a future research plan prefaced by a single-page summary, consisting of up to three proposals. Applicants for tenured positions are only asked to provide a research statement summarizing their current research program, and funding sources. Please submit all materials through Interfolio at http://apply.interfolio.com/190675 .  The review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 and proceed until the position is filled. For further information, contact the Director of the ESI through Sherry Gray at sherry.gray@yale.edu or the Chair of the Chemistry Department at chemistry.chair@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191768": {
      "title": "Academic Positions in the PET Center at the Yale School of Medicine (R-2359, R-2361)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT, United States The PET Center / Radiology Department at the Yale School of Medicine invites applications for tenure-track assistant professor positions in positron emission tomography (PET) imaging. Successful candidates will be expected to teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in related areas, develop a research program in collaboration with an interdisciplinary team of faculty and secure research funding. Responsibilities may include the development, characterization and validation of novel imaging biomarkers with PET, pharmacokinetic modeling of novel radiopharmaceuticals, development of advanced image reconstruction algorithms for quantitative PET and PET/MR imaging and the development of deep learning methods to improve quantitative PET imaging. Yale School of Medicine educates and nurtures creative leaders in medicine and science, promoting curiosity and critical inquiry in an inclusive environment enriched by diversity. We advance discovery and innovation fostered by partnerships across the university, our local community, and the world. We care for patients with compassion, and commit to improving the health of all people. The Yale University PET Center located on Howard Avenue in New Haven, CT is a 22,000 sq. ft. facility established to advance the interests of Yale clinicians, scientists, and students in molecular imaging research. The Yale University PET Center is comprised of a technologically advanced radiochemistry laboratory engaged in the development and use of a rich set of PET radiopharmaceuticals labeled with the most common PET isotopes (11C, 15O, 13N, and 18F); and an imaging and data analysis section that oversees scanning procedures and optimizes data acquisition and analysis. The Yale University PET Center collaborates with other School of Medicine departments to provide educational opportunities for doctoral and postdoctoral trainees. Collaborations with industry partners serve to advance the use of molecular imaging in new medication discovery and the development of new PET radiopharmaceuticals. Current research interests focus on disorders of the central nervous system (CNS), oncology, cardiology, and diabetes. Successful candidates should have a Ph.D. or MD/PhD in biomedical engineering, physics, electrical and computer engineering, computer science, applied mathematics or related fields. They should have experience and a track record of publications in two of the following areas: PET imaging physics, modeling of PET data and corresponding physical corrections. Tomographic image reconstruction including conventional reconstruction algorithms and penalized image reconstruction techniques. Radiotracer development, acquisition of experimental data including arterial blood and plasma as well as radiometabolite analysis using HPLC techniques, pharmacokinetic modeling including blood-based and reference region-based models, and use of numerical solvers for model fitting. Deep learning tools and methods for image denoising, reconstruction, segmentation and classification. Besides a strong background in the listed areas, candidates should demonstrate the following technical skills: Experience with computer science and data science, image processing and analysis. Proficiency with programming languages such as C/C , Python, MATLAB, R, Linux scripting (e.g. bash). Strong verbal and written communication skills demonstrated by publication track record and experience with grant writing. Mentoring skills for undergraduate and graduate students, interns and visitors. Besides the requirements listed above, additional desired qualifications include: Experience with MR imaging and MR image reconstruction and analysis. Experience with brain imaging and knowledge of biomarkers in Alzheimer's and other neurodegenerative diseases. Familiarity with optimization theory and applications to inverse problems. Rank is dependent on the successful candidate’s qualifications. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to the following website: apply.interfolio.com/191768 . All final candidates will need to provide three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191797": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Full Professor & Division Chief of Pediatric Urology, New Haven, CT",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Urology Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Urology is a nationally recognized academic department dedicated to excellence in patient care, research, and education . We are seeking a full-time Chief of the Division of Pediatric Urology to provide visionary leadership and advance our clinical, research, and educational missions. This position will be based at Yale New Haven Hospital in New Haven, Connecticut. The successful candidate will lead a collaborative division committed to delivering exceptional, multidisciplinary care to children and their families. A strong commitment to clinical excellence, innovation, and an outstanding patient and family experience is essential. Active engagement in research is a requirement of the position , with opportunities to pursue and expand clinical, translational, or population-based research aligned with the candidate’s interests and expertise. We seek a dynamic and accomplished academic urologist with outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, a demonstrated commitment to academic collaboration, and a strong record of clinical excellence, scholarly achievement, and education. The successful candidate will foster a culture of academic excellence, innovation, mentorship, and collaboration while advancing the Division of Pediatric Urology and contributing to the broader mission of one of the nation’s leading academic medical centers. Interested candidates should apply through the provided link: https://apply.interfolio.com/191797 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190994": {
      "title": "Medical Director of Transfusion Medicine, VA",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Laboratory Medicine Location: VA Connecticut Medical Center The Department of Laboratory Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine, in concert with VA Connecticut Medical Center, seeks a Clinical Pathologist to serve as the Medical Director for Transfusion Medicine at the VA Connecticut.  The selectee must be certified in Clinical Pathology by the American Board of Pathology [ABP], with or without certification in Anatomic Pathology.  ABP board-certification or -eligibility in Transfusion Medicine is highly desirable. The position also involves general clinical pathology responsibilities, including especially Microbiology. Board-certification or -eligibility in Medical Microbiology or equivalent is desirable. The position is accompanied by an appointment at Yale School of Medicine at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, depending on qualifications. Serving veterans in Connecticut and southern New England, the VA Connecticut is a tertiary care facility classiﬁed as a Clinical Referral Level I-a Facility and one of the most complex medical centers in the VA system. It is a teaching hospital, providing a full range of patient care services, with state-of-the-art technology, as well as extensive education and research programs.  VA Connecticut has 55,558 unique and a total of 722,892 outpatient visits per year as well as 191 inpatient beds. Its primary site is in West Haven, CT near Yale University’s two major campuses in New Haven and in West Haven. It also has a major outpatient facility in Newington, CT and an additional 6 outpatient facilities across the state of Connecticut. VA Connecticut supports the Pathology and Laboratory Medicine residency program at Yale as well as pathology subspecialty fellowships in Transfusion Medicine, Microbiology, and Hematopathology, along with a Pathologist Assistant training program. It is also the home to three national VA reference laboratories: Virology, Mycobacteriology, and Molecular Diagnostics / Pharmacogenetics. It is one of the most active VA medical centers nationally in research, with approximately 500 active research projects, funded with approximately $45 million in grants, and run by 80 Yale principal investigators. Please send a cover letter and a CV to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190994 . Additional information may be found at the federal job opportunities site, USAJOBS.GOV: Physician Clinical Pathology Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Pre-application inquiries about the position can be addressed to the search committee chairs, Dr. Deepthi Rao ( deepthi.rao@va.gov ) and Dr. Harvey Rinder ( henry.rinder@yale.edu )."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191388": {
      "title": "Associate Research Scientist - RF Coil Engineer",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT Seeking to hire of a full-time radio frequency (RF) coil engineer who can support the Yale MRRC and Yale Biomedical Imaging Institute research programs. The primary responsibility as RF coil engineer will be focused on designing, constructing, and repairing RF coils for clinical and pre-clinical MR and PET/MR scanners. These activities will include, but are not limited to, perform EM simulations, CAD design, build and test coils on the bench, evaluate them in an MRI environment, and run safety tests. Secondary responsibilities include design and construction of electronic instrumentation to support research, such as those related to novel MRI hardware (gradient coils and amplifiers, frequency-conversion units), RF receiver paths (pre-amplifiers, T/R switching, pin-diode switching), fMRI stimulation, and interfacing of optical and other hardware to the magnet. This position will be funded by the MRRC core facility and grants that require their expertise on funded research projects. The position requires a minimum of two years of research training experience following the attainment of a PhD degree. Appropriate field(s) of study/research for an Associate Research Scientist are Biomedical Imaging, Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Physics, and other fields in the Biological and Biomedical Sciences. The ideal candidate also has experience with the development of MRI hardware, software, and applications, as well as medical image analysis. Interested candidates should apply through the provided link: https://apply.interfolio.com/191388"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191231": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, on Term",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: West Campus Location: West Haven, CT Yale Cancer Biology Institute (YCBI), part of the Yale Comprehensive Cancer Center (YCC) at Yale University School of Medicine, invites applications from basic and physician scientists for Assistant or Associate Professor, on term positions in the Traditional Track.  Appointment at Yale is available in a number of departments, and rank will be commensurate with experience and accomplishments.  Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or M.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellence in research and education.  The successful candidates will have experience in the field of cancer biology, with specific target areas being cancer metabolism, chemical biology, cancer genetics and genomics, epigenetics, tumor microenvironment, and immune cell signaling.  Responsibilities include establishing a vigorous and independently funded research program in cancer biology, supervising and mentoring students with diverse backgrounds, and contributing to the graduate and medical school educational missions.  We seek individuals with strong records of independent creative accomplishments, who will interact productively with colleagues within YCBI, across the Yale West Campus, the Yale Cancer Center, and the University generally – taking advantage of unique opportunities to translate basic science from the Institute into clinical practice. YCBI is one of 6 multi-disciplinary research institutes on Yale’s burgeoning West Campus, which is self-contained but conveniently linked to Yale’s nearby New Haven campuses and the Yale Cancer Center.  For more details, see: https://westcampus.yale.edu/research/science-medicine-engineering/institutes/cancer .  Additional West Campus assets include Yale’s Systems Biology, Biomolecular Design and Discovery, Nanobiology, and Microbial Sciences Institutes – as well as state-of-the-art core facilities in imaging, small molecule discovery, genome analysis, electron microscopy, physical biochemistry, mass spectrometry, and other technologies.  Linkage to these Institutes and technologies provides unique opportunities for interdisciplinary research in the Yale Cancer Biology Institute that is simultaneously poised for translation through close involvement with the YCC and Smilow Cancer Hospital at Yale-New Haven. Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or M.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellence in research and education.  The successful candidates will have experience in the field of cancer biology, with specific target areas being cancer metabolism, chemical biology, cancer genetics and genomics, epigenetics, tumor microenvironment, and immune cell signaling.  Responsibilities include establishing a vigorous and independently funded research program in cancer biology, supervising and mentoring students with diverse backgrounds, and contributing to the graduate and medical school educational missions.  We seek individuals with strong records of independent creative accomplishments, who will interact productively with colleagues within YCBI, across the Yale West Campus, the Yale Cancer Center, and the University generally – taking advantage of unique opportunities to translate basic science from the Institute into clinical practice. Please submit a letter describing qualifications, along with a CV, a two-page summary of current and proposed research, and three confidential letters of reference to the following Interfolio website: https://apply.interfolio.com/191231 . Informal inquiries may be submitted to Dr. Mark Lemmon, YCBI Co-Director, at cancerbiologyinstitute@yale.edu . Consideration of applications will begin November 30 th , 2026 , and will continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190516": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Chemical Biology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: West Campus Location: West Campus The Institute of Biomolecular Design & Discovery (IBDD), in partnership with the Department of Chemistry, Yale University, New Haven, CT, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor rank to commence as early as July 1, 2027. The IBDD is a chemical biology-focused research institute, one of seven multidisciplinary research institutes at Yale University’s West Campus. Institute faculty hold a primary appointment in a life science, physical science, or engineering department. Currently, we seek to identify candidates whose research interests and accomplishments align with the Institute and the Chemistry Department. We seek creative teacher-scholars to teach courses and develop outstanding research programs in chemical biology broadly defined. Candidates must possess a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in a relevant discipline. Please submit all materials through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/190516 . Materials required for a complete application include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a future research plan prefaced by a single-page summary and consisting of up to three proposals, and a teaching-philosophy statement. Applicants should also arrange for the submission of three letters of recommendation. The review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 , and proceed until the position is filled. For further information, contact the Director of the IBDD through Helen Tvedt at helen.tvedt@yale.edu or the Chair of the Chemistry Department at chemistry.chair@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191181": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor: Psychiatric Emergency Services",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Psychiatry, Yale School of Medicine seeks a psychiatrist to serve on Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital (YNHPH) Psychiatric Emergency Services. Yale-New Haven Hospital is the major teaching and clinical research facility of the Yale University School of Medicine and consistently ranks among the best hospitals in the United States. Yale-New Haven Hospital encompasses the Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital a 118 bed, acute care, psychiatric facility that consists of emergency services, inpatient programs, specialized step-down intensive outpatient/day hospital programs for adolescents and adults as well as Interventional Psychiatric Services. As an attending in Psychiatric Emergency Services, the candidate will be responsible for managing the multidisciplinary evaluation of patients presenting for emergency psychiatric evaluation.  In this capacity, you will work collaboratively with a team of nurses, social workers, psychiatric residents, and psychiatric APRNs.  Providing education to medical students and residents regarding diagnosis, medication management, treatment planning and care of patients in the acute phase of illness is a key component of the position.  Rewarding clinical and academic opportunities abound. The position will be a combination of day, night, and weekend hours, offering 20% of academic/administrative protected time (scheduled for 32 clinical hours & 8 hours of administrative time, per 40-hour work week). This position carries a faculty appointment within the Department of Psychiatry at the assistant or associate professor level depending upon the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Yale University offers Yale Signature Benefits, including but not limited to: ·         Medical coverage through Yale Health and Aetna ·         Dental coverage through Delta Dental ·         Vision coverage options through Eyemed ·         Yale University Retirement Account Plan ·         Paid time off ·         Disability coverage ·         Life insurance ·         Mortgage loan program ·         Commuter benefits ·         Yale Homebuyer program ·         College tuition benefit plan Yale ·         Advantage discount program (Discounts for Activities, Travel, services, shopping, etc.) Living in/near New Haven New Haven is recognized as a city of innovation, culture, diversity, and prosperity. It is located between Boston and New York on Long Island Sound, and has outstanding cultural amenities (museums, theater, music, and sports), award-winning restaurants (including several of the nation’s best pizza parlors), boutique shops and national brands, quaint neighborhoods and bustling downtown areas with a variety of living options. New Haven is accessible by plane, train, and automobile, and is easy to navigate on foot, by bicycle, or bus. A free shuttle service provided by Yale covers many areas in the city. Additional Information about New Haven, CT: Living in New Haven Candidate must be board-certified in Psychiatry. To apply to this position please use the following link apply.interfolio.com/191181 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. If you have questions about these job opportunities, please contact Hun Millard, Vice Chief of Psychiatry, via email at hun.millard@yale.edu for more information."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191178": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor: Acute Services Team",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: New Haven The Department of Psychiatry, Yale School of Medicine is currently recruiting for the following Acute Services positions affiliated with Yale-New Haven Hospital. Yale-New Haven Hospital is the major teaching and clinical research facility of the Yale University School of Medicine and consistently ranks among the best hospitals in the United States. Yale-New Haven Hospital encompasses the Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital a 118 bed, acute care, psychiatric facility that consists of five main inpatient programs, psychiatric emergency department units, and several specialized step-down intensive outpatient/day hospital programs for adolescents and adults across two hospital campus locations. These positions carry a faculty appointment within the Department of Psychiatry at the assistant or associate professor level depending upon the candidate’s qualifications and experience. As an attending on our Acute Services Team, the candidate will be responsible for managing the multidisciplinary evaluation of patients presenting for psychiatric evaluation to the Yale New Haven Hospital. In this capacity, you will work collaboratively with a team of nurses, social workers, psychiatric residents, and psychiatric APRNs. Providing education to medical students and residents regarding diagnosis, medication management, treatment planning and care of patients in the acute phase of illness is a key component of the position. Rewarding clinical and academic opportunities abound. Benefits: Yale University offers Yale Signature Benefits, including but not limited to: ·         Medical coverage through Yale Health and Aetna ·         Dental coverage through Delta Dental ·         Vision coverage options through Eyemed ·         Yale University Retirement Account Plan ·         Paid time off ·         Disability coverage ·         Life insurance ·         Mortgage loan program ·         Commuter benefits ·         Yale Homebuyer program ·         College tuition benefit plan Yale ·         Advantage discount program (Discounts for Activities, Travel, services, shopping, etc.) Living in/near New Haven New Haven is recognized as a city of innovation, culture, diversity, and prosperity. It is located between Boston and New York on Long Island Sound, and has outstanding cultural amenities (museums, theater, music, and sports), award-winning restaurants (including several of the nation’s best pizza parlors), boutique shops and national brands, quaint neighborhoods and bustling downtown areas with a variety of living options. New Haven is accessible by plane, train, and automobile, and is easy to navigate on foot, by bicycle, or bus. A free shuttle service provided by Yale covers many areas in the city. Please click here for additional Information about New Haven, CT. Candidate must be a licensed physician and board-certified in Psychiatry. To apply to this position please use the following link: apply.interfolio.com/191178 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. If you have questions about any of these job opportunities, please email Hun Millard at hun.millard@yale.edu for more information."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191180": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor: Acute Services Team",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Psychiatry, Yale School of Medicine is currently recruiting for the following Acute Services positions affiliated with Yale-New Haven Hospital. Yale-New Haven Hospital is the major teaching and clinical research facility of the Yale University School of Medicine and consistently ranks among the best hospitals in the United States. Yale-New Haven Hospital encompasses the Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital a 118 bed, acute care, psychiatric facility that consists of five main inpatient programs, psychiatric emergency department units, and several specialized step-down intensive outpatient/day hospital programs for adolescents and adults across two hospital campus locations. These positions carry a faculty appointment within the Department of Psychiatry at the assistant or associate professor level depending upon the candidate’s qualifications and experience. As an attending on our Acute Services Team, the candidate will be responsible for managing the multidisciplinary evaluation of patients presenting for psychiatric evaluation to the Yale New Haven Hospital. In this capacity, you will work collaboratively with a team of nurses, social workers, psychiatric residents, and psychiatric APRNs. Providing education to medical students and residents regarding diagnosis, medication management, treatment planning and care of patients in the acute phase of illness is a key component of the position. Rewarding clinical and academic opportunities abound. Benefits: Yale University offers Yale Signature Benefits, including but not limited to: ·         Medical coverage through Yale Health and Aetna ·         Dental coverage through Delta Dental ·         Vision coverage options through Eyemed ·         Yale University Retirement Account Plan ·         Paid time off ·         Disability coverage ·         Life insurance ·         Mortgage loan program ·         Commuter benefits ·         Yale Homebuyer program ·         College tuition benefit plan Yale ·         Advantage discount program (Discounts for Activities, Travel, services, shopping, etc.) Living in/near New Haven New Haven is recognized as a city of innovation, culture, diversity, and prosperity. It is located between Boston and New York on Long Island Sound, and has outstanding cultural amenities (museums, theater, music, and sports), award-winning restaurants (including several of the nation’s best pizza parlors), boutique shops and national brands, quaint neighborhoods and bustling downtown areas with a variety of living options. New Haven is accessible by plane, train, and automobile, and is easy to navigate on foot, by bicycle, or bus. A free shuttle service provided by Yale covers many areas in the city. Please click here for additional Information about New Haven, CT. Candidate must be a licensed physician and board-certified in Psychiatry. To apply to this position please use the following link: apply.interfolio.com/191180 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. If you have questions about any of these job opportunities, please email Hun Millard at hun.millard@yale.edu for more information."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190740": {
      "title": "Neuroscience Faculty Positions - Computational (2026-2027)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Basic Science -YSM: Neuroscience Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Neuroscience at Yale University seeks to hire new tenure-track faculty members with interests in computational or theoretical neuroscience. We recognize that artificial intelligence and machine learning are changing all aspects of neuroscience from analysis of neural activity to network modeling to imaging to bioinformatics to molecular modeling. We are enthusiastic about candidates using computational methods to link models with experimental data and are convinced that merging these disciplines is key to the progress of neuroscience. The successful candidates will be embedded in a richly collaborative community supporting intellectual creativity. The Department of Neuroscience at Yale realizes that the full potential of our research lies in the power that varied perspectives bring to the field. We seek to foster an environment where all members of our community are supported and empowered to push forward the frontiers of neuroscience. Emphasis will be placed on recruiting at the level of Assistant Professor, but appointments at Associate Professor level may be considered. The computational neuroscience community at Yale is dynamic and expanding, and includes the Department of Neuroscience, the Wu Tsai Institute, the Kavli Institute for Neuroscience, and the Department of Biomedical Informatics and Data Science. The Department of Neuroscience resides in a space optimized for modern science and maximal interaction and collaboration. New faculty will be supported by a generous start-up package and ongoing salary support. Faculty are expected to develop a productive and innovative research program that will include the opportunity to participate in graduate and medical education. Candidates must hold a Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree. Please send a cover letter, a community impact statement, a research statement, a curriculum vitae, and arrange for submission of 3 letters of recommendation. Cover letter: Indicate your desired level of appointment (Assistant or Associate Professor). Community impact statement (1-page max): Describe your experience, commitment, and ideas for building a successful community of neuroscientists. Research statement (3-page max, including optional figures and references): Describe your most significant scientific discoveries and accomplishments to date, as well as the focus and goals of your future research program. Curriculum Vitae: Include links to publications or website. All application materials should be submitted electronically to https://apply.interfolio.com/190740 .  Any questions regarding the application process may be addressed to pauline.charbogne@yale.edu . Applications will be reviewed as they are received until the positions are filled with priority given to those applications received by November 30, 2026 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190966": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Andrologist, Greenwich, CT (1825)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Urology Location: Greenwich, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Urology, is a leading provider of patient care. We are seeking a full-time Urologist with subspeciality in Male Reproductive and Sexual Medicine (Andrology) to join our team based in the Greenwich Hospital Delivery Network. A commitment to multidisciplinary care, clinical innovation, and a consistently outstanding experience for patients and their families is expected. Depending on the interests of the successful candidate, this position could involve various opportunities to participate in clinical, translational, or population-based research and the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows. Our department anticipates that the successful candidate will have a dynamic personality, outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to patient care and academic collaboration. Candidate is expected to continue to see patients in General Urology in addition to the above. Candidate is expected to partner with Division of Reproductive and Sexual Medicine at New Haven Campus to develop a comprehensive program in Fairfield County CT and Westchester County NY. Applicants must hold a M.D. degree and be board certified/board eligible in Urology to qualify. Academic appointment will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191230": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Pharmacology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pharmacology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Pharmacology at Yale University School of Medicine invites applications for Assistant Professor or Associate Professor on Term in the Traditional Track. Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or M.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research and education. Areas of focus in this search will be chemical biology, computational biology (structural/chemical or systems focused), neuropharmacology, cardiovascular pharmacology, metabolism, and pharmacology associated with infectious diseases, nucleic acids and glycobiology. Responsibilities include establishing a vigorous and independently funded research program while supervising and mentoring students with broad backgrounds plus contributing to the graduate and medical school educational missions. We seek individuals with strong records of creative accomplishments, who are also keen to interact productively with colleagues within the Department of Pharmacology, across Yale School of Medicine and at Yale more generally. Pharmacology at Yale University has a very rich history of pre-eminence in drug discovery, with the first cancer chemotherapy clinical trials having been conducted here. Today, the research in our Department encompasses a wide range of fields, with researchers aiming to both understand and treat human disease, with particular strengths in drug discovery, integrative cell signaling, structural biology, and neuroscience. For more details, see https://medicine.yale.edu/pharm/ . Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or M.D. or equivalent degree and have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research and education. Please submit through the following Interfolio website: https://apply.interfolio.com/191230 (i) Letter describing your qualifications (ii) C urriculum vitae (iii) Two-page summary of current and proposed research (iv) Three confidential letters of reference to the Interfolio website Informal inquiries may be submitted electronically to Professor Mark Lemmon, Chair of Pharmacology (mark.lemmon@yale.edu). Consideration of applications will begin November 30 th , 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190882": {
      "title": "Academic Anatomic Pathologist (2206)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pathology Location: Yale School of Medicine, Department of Pathology The Department of Pathology at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking an Anatomic Pathologist at the Assistant / Associate Professor or full Professor level. Fellowship training or subspecialty expertise in Dermatopathology is preferred. Participation in other subspecialty sign outs will be based on the candidate’s interest . The successful candidate will participate in the service responsibilities of diagnostic practice; contribute to medical student, resident, and fellow teaching; and develop an academic program reflective of their interests. The Department serves Yale New Haven Hospital and Bridgeport Hospital, major teaching and referral centers in southern Connecticut, and a robust outreach program providing consultative services to regional practitioners and beyond. Southern Connecticut offers beautiful shoreline, affordable housing, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York, Boston, Newport, Cape Cod, and the ski slopes of New England. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification in Anatomic Pathology (and/or AP/CP) from the American Board of Pathology and eligibility for medical licensure in Connecticut are required . Individuals with expertise and /or interest in clinical, translational or basic research are encouraged to apply. Academic rank and salary will depend on level of expertise and experience. All application materials must be uploaded through Interfolio , a t apply.interfolio.com/190882 . These include a curriculum vitae, a letter of interest, and names and contact information for letters of recommendation from three senior references who are familiar with applicant's work and accomplishments. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Specific inquiries may be directed to Chen Liu, MD, PhD, Professor, Chair and Chief of Pathology, Yale School of Medicine, chen.liu@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190806": {
      "title": "Emergency Radiology Clinical Instructor with Yale MBA training",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT Earn a Yale MBA tuition free while working as an Emergency & Trauma Radiology Clinical Instructor. The Yale University Department of Radiology & Biomedical Imaging at the Yale School of Medicine is actively seeking motivated candidates for our MBA Fellowship program while working in our thriving and progressive Emergency & Trauma Division. The candidate will join our section of nineteen faculty who collectively provide contemporaneous, attending led emergency & trauma imaging services across Yale New Haven Health System; one of the largest academic health systems in the nation. The position is a joint position between the Yale School of Medicine and the Yale School of Management, where the candidate will obtain an MBA in the Yale MBA for Executives (Healthcare) program. The position is ideal for those who aspire to administrative radiology leadership positions in private or academic practice. The clinical appointment is for 24 months with 22 months as a student at the Yale School of Management. Students will receive a comprehensive curriculum on business administration, including courses on managing teams, negotiation, micro and macro economics, accounting and corporate finance.  There are also a number of opportunities to work in the Chair’s office on various projects including: operations, capital budgeting, compensation/incentive development, process/quality improvement, strategic planning, or marketing. There may also be scope to participate in similar projects in the hospital at large if the applicant chooses. Protected time will be provided for the applicant to attend classes and all MBA events. The applicant may also take elective courses and become involved in projects at the Yale School of Management and across the entire Yale University campus. Applicants must have an MD or equivalent degree with completion of radiology residency and, ideally, subspecialist fellowship training. Interested applicants should be board-eligible and be able to obtain an unrestricted Connecticut license. Interested applicants should upload their CV to: apply.interfolio.com/190806"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190777": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty (2027-2028 Academic Year)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Management Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Management is seeking individuals with experience and expertise from a wide range of academic and business disciplines who are interested in teaching in a part-time capacity. Demonstrated content expertise and a well-developed syllabus are required. Applicants should either hold a terminal degree in their field or have significant senior level work experience. Previous teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Candidates must also be able to meet eligibility requirements for work in the United States at the time of the appointment and be able to work legally for the full term of the appointment. Applicants should submit the following: 1) a brief cover letter, including any restrictions on teaching availability; 2) a curriculum vitae or resume; and 3) a proposed course syllabus. Please ensure the focus and objective of the course are clearly outlined and session topics, readings, assessments, and grading rubrics are included. Only complete applications will be considered. Considerations will include whether the proposed course provides unique subject matter that is of interest to Yale SOM students and is a good fit for the school's curriculum. For more information on our course descriptions, please see: https://som.yale.edu/elective-core-courses . Part-time faculty are responsible for class content, delivery, and assignment of grades. Selected applicants are expected to work with the Dean's Office and cognizant faculty to make any necessary revisions to the scope or content of the course prior to its being offered. Level of compensation will be determined by course details; part-time faculty are non-ladder positions and do not include benefits. Review of applications will begin on September 1, 2026 and will continue until all positions have been filled. Part-time faculty start dates and assignment lengths vary during the academic year and are determined on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190809": {
      "title": "Emergency/ Trauma Radiologist (RFP-2018, 2023)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging at Yale University School of Medicine is seeking board eligible/certified radiologists with expertise and interest in emergency/trauma imaging for a full-time faculty appointment. Academic rank at Yale School of Medicine will be commensurate with experience, training, and achievements. The Emergency/Trauma section consists of 17 faculty members whose practice includes level one trauma and stroke centers, additional ER sites and urgent care centers, and partial coverage of the VA West Haven Medical Center Emergency Room (via tele-radiology). This program was the first in the nation to provide contemporaneous 24 X 7 imaging interpretation for our Emergency/Trauma patients. Our group has a track record of collaborative research, flexibility in scheduling shifts, and a commitment to the best clinical care. The primary site of coverage at YNHH is centrally located in New Haven, with access to a vibrant and passionate University. Multiple shifts are work-from-home allowing for a hybrid schedule. Board eligible/certified Radiologist with optional fellowship training (Trauma/ER, or Neuroradiology training preferred) for a full-time faculty appointment. Rank is commensurate with experience. A strong interest in clinical care and education (undergraduate medical and graduate medical) is required. Clinical responsibilities include CT, ultrasound, plain radiography and rarely emergency fluoroscopic studies. Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to the following website: apply.interfolio.com/190809 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190676": {
      "title": "Neuroradiologist  (R-1820, R-2112)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging at Yale University School of Medicine invites applications for  board eligible/certified radiologists with expertise in neuroradiology imaging for a full-time faculty appointment. Academic rank at Yale School of Medicine will be commensurate with experience, training, and achievements. The Neuroradiology Section at the Yale Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging has a track record of providing high quality, timely and progressive neuro imaging using high-end equipment.  We are highly valued by our clinical colleagues for our subspecialist expertise, which we plan to expand to include attending led, contemporaneous evening services seven days/week.  A new $838M Neuroscience Center is also being planned on our St Raphael’s Campus in New Haven.  The neuroradiology services we offer are in high demand across the Yale New Haven Health System and we are now looking for additional skilled attendings to join our team of dedicated neuroradiologists.  We work side by side with our annual complement of 12 twelve talented Yale neuroradiology fellows and radiology residents in a vibrant and engaging University town. Our team-based reading rooms are located in our Yale New Haven York Street and St. Raphael Campuses, both of which are centrally located in New Haven, where we read additional studies from regional hospital and outpatient imaging centers in surrounding New Haven and Fairfield Counties. We enjoy a very flexible work schedule, competitive salaries, and a generous benefits package. The Yale School of Medicine is a world-renowned center for biomedical research, education, and advanced health care. New Haven has been home to the university for three centuries. It is also a center for business and a mecca for the arts with the city recognized for its innovation and culture, great restaurants and its wealth of activities for families and single professionals of all ages.  New Haven is also conveniently located between New York and Boston, and both are easily accessible due to the area’s robust rail transit system. Board eligible/certified Radiologists with Neuroradiology fellowship training who have clinical proficiency in advanced CT, MRI and neuro fluoroscopic studies are encouraged to apply.  Leadership roles and other opportunities for professional development are available depending on the applicant’s interests, goals, and experience. A commitment to teaching residents and fellows is also required. Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to: apply.interfolio.com/190676 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190434": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Research - Endocrinology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Endocrinology Location: New Haven, CT The Section of Endocrinology at the Yale School of Medicine (YSM) invites applications for a full-time faculty position for an MD or MD, PhD Endocrinologist with either a strong background in health systems science, population health, implementation or outcomes research, health disparities and/or clinical epidemiology (OR) a strong background in basic and/or translational, laboratory-based endocrine research. We are seeking a visionary clinician-investigator to develop a research program that will complement the Section’s traditional strengths in diabetes, metabolism, obesity and/or mineral and bone metabolism. The successful candidate should have a track record of research productivity, established or pending external research funding and academic credentials supporting their appointment to be Assistant or Associate Professor at Yale Medical School. Depending on the specific needs of the role, the candidate would have access to a rich set of resources including the Yale Diabetes Research Center, the Yale Obesity Research Center, the Yale Human Translational Immunology Program, the Yale Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation, the National Clinical Scholars Program at Yale, the Yale School of Public Health, the Yale Center for Molecular and Systems Metabolism, the Yale Program for Mitochondrial Biology and Intermediary Metabolism, and the Yale Center for Clinical Investigation and its associated inpatient and outpatient human research units. Selected candidates will also be provided with research space in a newly opened facility and competitive start-up funds commensurate with their rank and/or demonstrated programmatic needs. The Section of Endocrinology and Metabolism currently includes 50 full-time research and clinical faculty and is growing. The Yale New Haven Health System (YNHHS) includes a network of 5 hospitals across Connecticut and Rhode Island, Yale Medicine, and the New England Medical Group, that collectively record over 3.6 million outpatient encounters and over 150,000 inpatient discharges per year.   All parts of YNHHS are interconnected within a single electronic medical record and a unified IRB, making it an ideal platform for clinical research at scale. YSM is also affiliated with VA Connecticut Healthcare System, a 1A VA hospital system with a strong track record of research in clinical outcomes and informatics, supported by the Cooperative Studies Program (CSP) Coordinating Center and Clinical Epidemiology Research Center (CERC). Experience in research involving artificial intelligence in healthcare would be advantageous. Key Responsibilities: Conduct high-impact, externally funded research in implementation science, health disparities, clinical epidemiology and population-based care directed at reducing the burden of endocrine and metabolic disease (OR) conduct high-impact, externally funded basic or translational research directed at reducing the burden of endocrine and metabolic disease. Contribute to clinical care in endocrinology. Mentor graduate students, clinical trainees and junior faculty in basic, translational and/or clinical research and community-engaged scholarship. Serve as a strategic leader in interdisciplinary collaborations across the health system and surrounding communities or across the Endocrine Section and related Basic Science Departments and Programs. Qualifications: MD, or MD. PhD (or equivalent) with board certification in Endocrinology, Diabetes & Metabolism. Strong background in health services research, outcomes research, clinical epidemiology, implementation science, public health and/or community-engaged research (OR) a strong background in basic or translational research Track record of securing competitive research funding (NIH, AHRQ, PCORI, foundations, etc.). Experience collaborating across departments, clinical disciplines, and community-based organizations. Eligibility for medical licensure in CT. All applications materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190434."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190603": {
      "title": "Cardiac Electrophysiologist Yale School of Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT Position Overview The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Cardiac Electrophysiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive care to patients referred to the Cardiac Electrophysiology program in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Perform procedures, including ablations and device implantations. Participate in on-call rotations. Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in both Cardiovascular Medicine and Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188603": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, Anthropology of South Asia",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Anthropology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anthropology at Yale University seeks to hire a full-time tenured associate or full professor in the sociocultural anthropology of South Asia beginning as early as January 1, 2028. The topic of specialization is open. The selected scholar will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in sociocultural anthropology and South Asian studies; these courses may include theoretical, topical, methodological, and/or other offerings, as appropriate to specialization. The teaching expectation is normally four courses per academic year, plus service to the department and university. Mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students is also expected. The appointee must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should apply via apply.interfolio.com/188603 . An initial application includes a cover letter, up-to-date CV, and 2-page statement of research interests and plans. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please email Doug Rogers, Chair of Anthropology, at doug.rogers@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190577": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Department of Chronic Disease Epidemiology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, Connecticut The Department of Chronic Disease Epidemiology in the School of Public Health at Yale University (YSPH) is seeking applicants at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the Tenure or Educator Scholar Tracks. We are particularly interested in applicants with demonstrated records of conducting cutting-edge and community engaged research using epidemiologic methods to address the leading chronic disease causes of death and disability at a national or global level. Areas of interest include but are not limited to: development and application of novel epidemiologic methods (including in causal inference, data science and AI and measurement), mental health, substance use disorders, cardiovascular disease, diabetes, and women’s health. We also welcome candidates who investigate the role that social and structural determinants play in shaping chronic disease epidemics and the intersection across multiple chronic diseases and employ research strategies to address these issues across the lifecourse. As one of the first schools of public health in the nation, YSPH has a rich history of being at the forefront of innovative research and education. YSPH serves local, national, and international communities through its high impact interdisciplinary research and training of a diverse group of master’s and doctoral students. The goal of Yale School of Public Health (YSPH) is to link science and society to make public health foundational to all communities. Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and maintain an active, externally funded, independent research program focused on addressing major chronic disease causes of death and disability. Apply highly rigorous epidemiologic methods, including in relation to measurement, causal inference, the application of data science and AI, and the creation of novel data sources for epidemiologic research. Publish and present research results in peer-reviewed professional journals and disseminate findings to scientific, clinical, policy, and community audiences. Contribute to the growth and impact of the educational mission, including through student recruitment, curriculum innovation, teaching at least one course at the masters/doctoral level each year and mentoring students. Foster collaborations and strengthen interactions with other schools across campus. Provide service to the department, school, and university in alignment with the YSPH Strategic Plan and Yale University priorities. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in epidemiology or a related field. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated capacity to work both collaboratively and independently. Prior record of independent funding and high-impact publications. Applicants are asked to submit (1) a cover letter that addresses research/professional accomplishments/ interests, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching statement that includes teaching philosophy and experience, and (4) the names and contact information of three references. About the Department of Chronic Disease Epidemiology The Department currently has 17 faculty whose research fields include cancer, cardiovascular disease, perinatal and maternal child health, nutrition, exercise and obesity, global health, aging, genetic epidemiology, injury, substance use, and health disparities. The department faculty serve as principal investigators of approximately $9M of extramurally funded research annually, lead several T32s, and work across the full spectrum of translational research. The department has vibrant educational programs at both the MPH and PhD level with a focus on research and leadership in the field. Approximately 75 masters and 12 PhD students are enrolled in CDE each year. The MPH graduates go on to a variety of careers in epidemiology and public health leadership in the application of science to the prevention and treatment of chronic disease. The PhD program counts among its alumnus faculty and leadership at YSPH and peer schools of public health, leadership roles at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, and State Departments of Health. About the Yale School of Public Health The Yale School of Public Health, founded in 1915, is one of the oldest accredited schools of public health in the nation and has a rich history in research leadership and innovation in public health. Under the leadership of Dean Megan Ranney, the school has embarked on a strategic plan that at its core seeks to link science to society, helping communities everywhere to thrive based on a foundation of public health. More details on the School’s current strategic plan can be found here: https://ysph.yale.edu/about-school-of-public-health/strategic-plan/ About Yale University Yale University, established in 1701, is a private research university located in New Haven, Connecticut. It is renowned for its rigorous academic programs, distinguished faculty, and vibrant intellectual community. Yale is committed to improving the world today and for future generations through outstanding research and scholarship, education, preservation, and practice. About New Haven New Haven, Connecticut, is a city with a rich history and a thriving cultural scene. Home to Yale University, New Haven is a community rooted in academic and artistic excellence and it surroundings offer a unique blend of urban living with quick access to outdoor green spaces a community rooted in academic and artistic excellence. New Haven is also well-connected, with convenient access to major cities like New York and Boston."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190587": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Maternal-Fetal-Medicine (202607-2311)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences Location: New Haven and Waterbury, CT The Yale University Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences seeks to hire a full time faculty member to join our team. Academic appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor;  in the Division of Maternal-Fetal-Medicine (MFM). The MFM Division has enjoyed unprecedented clinical, academic and research growth.  The successful candidate would participate in a rotational schedule to provide inpatient, consultative and prenatal diagnostic services at Yale University and affiliated clinical locations.  Interest and experience in basic and/or translational research will be considered an asset.  The Department is currently ranked 6th among Ob/Gyn departments in NIH funding, supports numerous clinical trials, and has a large Division of Reproductive Sciences which houses outstanding basic and translational research in the areas of pregnancy sciences, uterine biology, cancer biology and ovarian/gamete biology led by physician-scientists and PhD researchers. A commitment to teaching is required in order to provide outstanding instruction to medical students, residents and fellows in various clinical venues. We are seeking a full-time, fellowship-trained Maternal-Fetal Medicine specialist. Academic rank and appointment will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and qualifications. Applicants must submit a current curriculum vitae; a cover letter is optional but strongly encouraged. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190587"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190370": {
      "title": "Professor and Department Chair, Yale School of Public Department of Environmental Health Sciences",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, Connecticut The Yale School of Public Health (YSPH) seeks an inspiring and strategic leader to serve as Chair of its Environmental Health Sciences department. Under the vision of Dean Megan Ranney, the school is advancing strategic academic public health leadership by linking science to society. This position presents an exceptional opportunity to help (re)shape the future of public health education and research at one of the world’s leading academic institutions. As the department’s academic and administrative leader, the Department Chair will collaborate with School leadership and lead strategic efforts to grow and elevate the department’s national and global impact. The Chair will foster a dynamic academic community, including the recruitment and mentoring of additional world class faculty. The Chair will also lead the department’s educational programs and provide a vision for both near-term cutting-edge curriculum initiatives and long-range program planning. This includes recruiting, teaching, and ensuring support for MPH, MS and PhD students. YSPH values collaborative leadership, a commitment to mentorship, and an academic approach that bridges research and practice. The successful candidate will bring a strong academic record that merits appointment as Full Professor with tenure at Yale, effective teaching, mentoring and leadership skills, internationally recognized scholarship in environmental health sciences research and a vision for advancing public health science. Come join us at the Yale School of Public Health, where your leadership can help shape the future of public health and help link science to society to improve lives around the globe. About the Department of Environmental Health Sciences The Department ( https://ysph.yale.edu/research/department-research/environmental-health-sciences/ ) currently has faculty whose research fields include environmental epidemiology, molecular toxicology, green chemistry, climate epidemiology and exposomics. The department faculty serve as principal investigators of approximately $7M of extramurally funded research annually, lead several T32 training grants, and work across the full spectrum of translational research. The department has vibrant educational programs including MPH, MS, and PhD that attract students with a focus on research and leadership in the field. The MPH and MS graduates go on to a variety of careers in environmental health sciences and public health leadership in the application of science to policy and research to address environmental impacts on health. About the Yale School of Public Health The Yale School of Public Health, founded in 1915, is one of the oldest accredited schools of public health in the nation and has a rich history in research leadership and innovation in public health. Under the leadership of Dean Megan Ranney, the school has embarked on a strategic plan that at its core seeks to link science to society, helping communities everywhere to thrive based on a foundation of public health. More details on the School’s current strategic plan can be found here: https://ysph.yale.edu/about-school-of-public-health/strategic-plan/ About Yale University Yale University, established in 1701, is a private research university located in New Haven, Connecticut. It is renowned for its rigorous academic programs, distinguished faculty, and vibrant intellectual community. Yale is committed to improving the world today and for future generations through outstanding research and scholarship, education, preservation, and practice. About New Haven New Haven, Connecticut, is a city with a rich history and a thriving cultural scene. Home to Yale University, New Haven is a community rooted in academic and artistic excellence and it surroundings offer a unique blend of urban living with quick access to outdoor green spaces a community rooted in academic and artistic excellence. New Haven is also well-connected, with convenient access to major cities like New York and Boston. Nominations and expressions of interest for this position can be sent to ysphfacultyaffairs@yale.edu . For fullest consideration please submit a letter of interest detailing your vision for public health research and leadership in environmental health sciences, as well as details of previous academic mentorship and leadership, research accomplishments, and a full curriculum vitae by September 15, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190447": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate in Microbial Metabolomics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, CT A funded postdoctoral associate position is available in the Department of Environmental Health Sciences at Yale School of Public Health. Research projects will focus on microbial metabolomics, host–microbial interactions, and colorectal cancer. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to lead metabolite identification and downstream translational analyses, while also developing independent research directions related to microbiome metabolism, cancer metabolomics, environmental exposures, tumor biology, or host–microbial interactions. Our Lab provides a collaborative and supportive research environment, with access to metabolomics platforms and opportunities for professional development. There is also scope to branch into related projects across cancer metabolomics, early-onset colorectal cancer, environmental exposures, microbiome-derived metabolites, and host–microbial interactions. Salary will be based on the Yale Postdoctoral Compensation policy . Support for travel to conferences and professional development activities are available. Information regarding benefits can be found here: Benefits | Office for Postdoctoral Affairs We are looking for a candidate with a Ph.D. in Chemistry, Life Sciences, or a related discipline, with demonstrated hands-on experience in LC-MS-based metabolomics. The candidate will also be encouraged to apply for external postdoctoral funding and contribute to grant applications. To apply: Please submit a cover letter,  CV with full bibliography, and contact information for three professional references. Please contact Dr. Caroline Johnson with any questions ( caroline.johnson@yale.edu )."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189783": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate, Yale Center for Natural Carbon Capture",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Yale Center for Natural Carbon Capture Location: New Haven, CT The Yale Center for Natural Carbon Capture ( YCNCC) is accepting applications for its Postdoctoral Fellowship Program . The YCNCC was established in 2021 to advance fundamental and applied science on enhancing natural Earth systems to create safe, effective, and scalable methods of reducing greenhouse gas concentrations in the atmosphere. The YCNCC mission strongly emphasizes meaningful ecological and social co-benefits, and the Center’s efforts span departments and schools at Yale, convening faculty, research scientists, postdoctoral researchers, graduate students, and staff to work collaboratively on natural solutions for climate mitigation. We welcome applicants to the Postdoctoral Fellowship Program with research interests across the Center’s three areas of focus : Eco system Capture , Geological & Ocean Carbon Capture , and Industrial Carbon Utilization . The Program prioritizes applicants who bring new ideas and capabilities to the Center and to Yale. Candidates should identify and contact faculty with the relevant expertise to discuss their proposed project and ensure the faculty member is willing and able to host them. In addition to YCNCC’s Scientific Leadership Team and Faculty Affiliates , f aculty hosts can be from any school/department at Yale, including the School of the Environment , the School of Engineering and Applied Science , and any relevant department within the Faculty of Arts Sciences . Applications lacking a letter of support from a potential Yale faculty host will not be considered . Candidates selected for the program will be contacted by the end of February 202 7 and are expected to accept or decline as soon as possible, but no later than March 31, 202 7 . Successful candidates are expected to begin their program at Yale between July 1 and December 31, 202 7 . Successful candidates will be appointed as postdoctoral associates for an initial period of one year and may be extended for a second year upon satisfactory performance and available funding. Postdoctoral associated will be provided a stipend based on the current Yale postdoctoral salary scale (currently $68,500/year), and base research funds ($6,000/year), plus health care benefits and limited expenses for relocation. A PhD or equivalent degree in a relevant discipline and less than a total of four years of prior postdoctoral experience. Complete applications must be submitted to Interfolio ( apply.interfolio.com/189783 ) by December 1, 202 6 , 11 :59pm ET . For questions about this position, please contact Toby Bryce, Managing Director, at ycncc@yale.edu. A complete application includes: Full CV, including a complete bibliography. Research proposal, 2 pages maximum (not including figures and references) that outlines how the proposed project would advance the mission of the Center. 2 Letters of Recommendation PDFs of 1 to 2 publications (in prep or submitted manuscripts are permissible) Letter of support from a Yale faculty member, 1 page maximum, which should: o Specify the research infrastructure that will be available to the applicant to complete their project, such as facilities, equipment , computing resources, field sites, etc. o Provide a brief description of the faculty advisor’s mentoring philosophy and approach, including how they foster an inclusive environment o Explain how the candidate’s project expands the faculty member’s research enterprise and adds to Yale’s overall expertise in the field o Note that this letter should not be about the applicant’s qualifications, but rather about the support that will be provided by the faculty mentor."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189916": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Medieval European History",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: History Location: New Haven, CT The Department of History and the Humanities Program at Yale University seek to jointly appoint a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor in the history of medieval Europe with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027.  The teaching expectation is normally four courses academic year. The focus of these courses would be medieval European history, but candidates will also be encouraged to teach more broadly within premodern global or comparative history and expected to teach in the Directed Studies program.  Applicants may be specialists in any period or area of European history from 400–1500 CE. Critically, their profile must reflect a strong investment in cross-disciplinary engagement and general education, which will contribute to Yale’s Directed Studies program and Humanities major. The appointee must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent degree or have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. by June 1, 2027. Applicants should submit an application to https://apply.interfolio.com/189916 . They should submit a cover letter, CV, teaching statement, research statement, writing sample prepared for anonymous reading (40 pages or fewer), and three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin on September 4, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please email Mrs. Denise Scott, Senior Administrative Assistant in the Department of History, at denise.scott@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190510": {
      "title": "Emergency Medicine Simulation Chief",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Emergency Medicine Location: New Haven, CT Seeking Section Chief of Emergency Medicine Simulation in the Department of Emergency Medicine at Yale School of Medicine The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking faculty interested in joining as Chief of the Section of Emergency Medicine Simulation in our nationally leading academic Department of Emergency Medicine. The position seeks candidates who meet the Yale School of Medicine criteria for the Associate/Professor level, rank, and track commensurate with their qualifications and experience. Yale’s Section of Emergency Medicine Simulation The Section of Emergency Medicine Simulation is dedicated to improving healthcare through innovative medical education, assessment, research, and outreach. Currently, Emergency Medicine Faculty in the section oversee the Yale Center for Medical Simulation (YCMS), one of the largest medical school simulation centers in the country and Society for Simulation in Healthcare accredited. The Section currently includes eight primary faculty with several secondarily appointed faculty spanning multiple clinical departments. The Section of Simulation faculty has a track record of academic productivity, receiving several federal and foundation grants, publishing their work in top tier scientific journals, and developing highly innovative, adaptive strategies for virtual simulation. Notably, section faculty serve as Principal Investigators of a R25 Science Education Partnership Award from the National Institute of General Medical Sciences, for The Simulation Academy at Yale: Youth Entering Science (SAY‑YES!)   program that offers hands‑on STEM experiential learning to local high school students and the application of new emerging technologies. About Yale Emergency Medicine Yale Emergency Medicine staffs the three campuses of Yale New Haven Hospital with a total patient volume exceeding 190,000 visits per year. It is home to a four-year EM residency of 76 residents, an APP advanced training program, numerous fellowship programs including a Medical Simulation fellowship that has been continuously filled, and graduated leaders in medical simulation across the nation. Clinical opportunities include a range of acuity from our primary academic campus, a Level 1 trauma and comprehensive stroke care center, to community and freestanding EDs as well as the opportunity to care for a range of clinical acuity from critical care to observation medicine. The department has been ranked second by the Blue Ridge Institute for Medical Research for NIH funding in emergency medicine and was ranked first in prior years since 2021. The department is currently home to 10 of the top 100 funded investigators in emergency medicine.  The research portfolio of the department is broad and well diversified including focus areas in addiction medicine, geriatrics, implementation science, clinical informatics, health services research, critical care clinical trials, and public health. Board certification in Emergency Medicine Preferred: Proven track record of academic and administrative leadership in medical simulation. Experience in faculty mentorship and working within matrixed environments and organizations. To join our team, applicants should submit their cover letter and CV to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190510 Should you have any technical difficulties with Interfolio, please reach out to: Meghan Gaudioso at meghan.gaudioso@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188467": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, U.S. Cultural History and Cultural Studies",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Humanities: American Studies Location: New Haven, CT The American Studies Program at Yale University is looking to hire a full-time, tenure-track or tenured faculty member available at all ranks, including Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor levels, in U.S. Cultural History and Cultural Studies with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek to hire a colleague whose scholarship examines the nineteenth- and/or twentieth-century cultural history of the United States, nationally and transnationally. While we will consider applications from any subfield, we are especially interested in applicants whose work focuses on: labor histories; disability history and disability studies; environmental studies and environmental history; or the historical study of colonialisms and empires. We are especially interested in applications from colleagues with a Ph.D. in American Studies or another appropriate interdisciplinary field who has an active record of undergraduate and graduate teaching, advising, and program-building in an American Studies department, as well as demonstrated experience in and commitment to the public humanities. The teaching expectation is normally four courses per academic year, plus service to the program, including teaching in an undergraduate core course and advising graduate students. The appointee must hold a PhD or equivalent degree or have completed all requirements for the PhD in American Studies or another appropriate interdisciplinary field by June 2027. To ensure full consideration, applicants should submit an application via Interfolio < https://apply.interfolio.com/188467 > that includes a cover letter, CV, and research statement (2 single-spaced pages) by October 15, 2026 . Candidates seeking an appointment without tenure should also arrange to have the names and contact information of three (3) contact references submitted via Interfolio from whom the committee will collect reference letters at a later stage. Candidates seeking a tenured appointment may opt to provide names of references on their curriculum vitae. Contact Nikki Strong, Chair's Assistant, at <nikki.strong@yale.edu> with any questions."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190083": {
      "title": "General Interventional Consultative Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT Position Description The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190083 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190081": {
      "title": "General Consultative Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT Position Description The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/190081 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188997": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Developmental Psychology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Psychology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Psychology at Yale University invites applications for an open rank (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) faculty position with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027, to be situated within the department’s Developmental Psychology area. We are particularly interested in scholars who add breadth to our existing developmental offerings while effectively integrating with our generally cognitive approach. In addition to more traditional developmental foci, we are excited to consider cross-cultural approaches as well as researchers who address fundamental questions about cognition in non-human animals. Priority will be given to outstanding scholars who contribute effectively to both undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring and who are ready to conduct a generative research program. Eligible applicants must have a PhD or equivalent degree at the time of hire. Application must be submitted through Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/188997 Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and up to three selected publications (published or unpublished). Candidates seeking an appointment with tenure do not need to furnish letters of recommendation. Candidates seeking an appointment without tenure should also arrange to have three (3) letters of recommendation submitted via Interfolio. Cover letter: The one-page cover letter should include the applicant’s name, the title of the position the applicant is submitting materials for, a 3-5 sentence description of the applicant’s professional focus, and a brief comment on how the applicant views themselves as adding to the department. Research statement: The research statement should consist of two parts. One part is the “past research statement” (1000 words max). This should summarize the applicant’s main research activities to date. The second part is the “future research statement” (500 words max). This should summarize the applicant’s plans for research activities over the next 5 years (i.e., if given a generous startup package what does the applicant envision for their work? What questions does the applicant want to tackle?). Teaching statement: The teaching statement (1000 words max) should include a summary of the applicant’s teaching style inside (formal courses) and outside (mentoring, supervision) of the classroom. The applicant should also mention the types of courses they would be excited to teach. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Lindsey Fuller, Academic Appointment Specialist, lindsey.fuller@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189746": {
      "title": "Surgery, Surgical Outcomes, Assistant/Associate Professor (2291)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Surgical Outcomes Location: New Haven, CT Department of Surgery, Surgical Outcomes Yale University, School of Medicine The Department of Surgery at the Yale School of Medicine is currently seeking a PhD or equivalent scientist to join our comprehensive and growing team. Applications are invited for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Surgery. The Department of Surgery would like to appoint an Assistant or Associate Professor in Surgical Outcomes to enhance the research mission of our department. We are seeking a candidate that will have positive, immediate, medium, and long-term salutatory effects on the Department, School, and University. In the short term, we seek a candidate who will bring experience in health services research with expertise in one or more of the following: mixed methods research, novel trial design, implementation science, decision science, or patient-centered outcomes. The candidate will join the community of health services researchers in the department and become part of our newly established mixed-method core. The Assistant or Associate Professor should serve as a beacon for trainees and faculty, with a strong commitment to mentorship across the funding continuum and should set expectations for the level of science that should be emulated in the Department. In addition, the candidate should be an engaged collaborator and equipped to build interdisciplinary teams in surgical outcomes. In the mid-term, we expect the candidate to amplify collaboration with faculty in Surgery and elsewhere at Yale, resulting in the development of new grants. In the long term, we expect this Assistant or Associate Professor’s approach and example will enhance the rigor and scientific culture in health services research within the Department of Surgery, the medical school, and Yale University. Applicants should expect to work in a friendly environment with collegial and supportive administration. Candidates must have exceptional interpersonal skills and a commitment to make contributions to the field of Surgical Outcomes. This position is an opportunity to join a growing faculty and build a robust research community in a department committed to furthering and growing its research mission. New Haven is conveniently located between Boston and New York. It is a great place to live, work, do business and enjoy life. There are ample opportunities to live within 20 minutes on the coast or in surrounding villages with small town charm. The greater New Haven area offers some of the top public and private schools in the country. P hD (or equivalent) from an accredited institution. At least 1 year of postdoctoral training and experience in one or more of the following fields:  mixed methods research, novel trial design, implementation science, decision science, or patient-centered outcomes. Qualified candidates will have a strong record of scientific excellence with accomplishments in collaborating on successful grant submissions and impactful publications.   When working in a collaborative research effort, the candidate's creative contributions must be distinguished and identifiable. All application materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/189746 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Should you have any questions, please reach out to: Name: Rachel A. Greenup, MD, MPH Title: Section Chief, Breast Surgery & Director of Mixed Methods Health Science Core, Department of Surgery Email: rachel.greenup@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189692": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Professor, Medical Director of Liver Transplantation",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Digestive Diseases Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine seeks qualified candidates at the rank of Associate Professor/Professor level for a full-time academic position as Medical Director of Liver Transplantation for the Yale-New Haven Hospital (YNHH) Liver Transplant Program. The Medical Director will provide operational, administrative, and clinical leadership for a team of transplant hepatologists, including oversight of on-site and outreach transplant clinics, transplant recipient selection, and quality/safety. Academic responsibilities include supervision and teaching of students, medical housestaff, and GI/hepatology fellows, participation in clinical and educational conferences, and an opportunity to engage in clinical research. The Section of Digestive Diseases serves as the home of over 20 faculty hepatologists with national and international expertise across multiple domains of clinical hepatology, including specialty clinical programs (e.g. MASH, Viral Hepatitis, Autoimmune/Cholestatic, Wilson’s, Gaucher’s, Alcohol/Addiction, Liver Cancer) as well as the Yale Liver Center, one of three NIH/NIDDK-funded core research centers focused on hepatology. Candidates must hold a Medical Degree and be board-certified in Gastroenterology and Transplant Hepatology (Certificate of Added Qualification). Prior leadership experience in transplant hepatology is preferred. Please apply to the position using the following link: apply.interfolio.com/189692"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189706": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Nursing Location: Orange, CT The Yale School of Nursing (YSN) invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor. We seek exceptional early-career scholars whose innovative research has the potential to transform health, healthcare, and nursing science. We welcome applicants from all areas of nursing and interdisciplinary health research whose scholarship advances scientific discovery, improves health outcomes, and addresses complex challenges across clinical care, population health, health systems, education, technology, policy, and the future of healthcare. Candidates employing diverse methodological approaches including quantitative, qualitative, mixed methods, implementation science, clinical and translational research, data science, artificial intelligence, community-engaged research, behavioral science, systems science, and other innovative approaches are encouraged to apply. As one of the world's leading schools of nursing, Yale is committed to advancing bold ideas that improve the health and well-being of individuals, families, and communities. Our faculty are internationally recognized leaders whose scholarship shapes clinical practice, informs health policy, drives innovation, and transforms healthcare delivery. Through an intellectually vibrant and highly collaborative environment, faculty work across Yale University, Yale New Haven Health, and a broad network of national and international partners to address some of the most pressing challenges facing society. YSN is distinguished by its commitment to excellence in research, education, clinical innovation, and interdisciplinary collaboration. We are committed to preparing the next generation of nurse scientists, educators, clinicians, and leaders while advancing discoveries that improve health locally and globally. Responsibilities Faculty appointed to the tenure track are expected to develop internationally recognized programs of scholarship that advance nursing science and improve health while contributing to Yale's missions of research, education, clinical excellence, and service. The successful candidate will: Develop and sustain an innovative, externally funded program of independent scholarship with the potential for national and international impact. Produce influential scholarly work through publications in leading peer-reviewed journals, presentations at major scientific meetings, and other forms of knowledge dissemination. Teach and mentor master's, doctoral, and postdoctoral trainees, fostering excellence in research, scholarship, and professional development. Contribute to the continued innovation and excellence of YSN's graduate educational programs. Build collaborative research partnerships across Yale University, Yale New Haven Health, and national and international academic, healthcare, industry, government, and community organizations. Participate actively in the intellectual life of the School through interdisciplinary collaboration, faculty governance, academic leadership, and professional service. Help cultivate an inclusive, collaborative, and intellectually stimulating academic community that supports excellence in research, education, and innovation. Applicants should demonstrate outstanding promise as emerging scholars and educators. Required qualifications include: An earned doctoral degree in nursing or a related discipline. Evidence of scholarly productivity and funding, and strong potential to establish an externally funded program of research. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, mentorship, and collaborative scholarship. Ability to contribute effectively within an interdisciplinary academic environment. Eligibility for licensure as appropriate to the candidate's discipline is desirable. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Applicants should submit: Cover letter describing research accomplishments, future scholarly vision, and interest in joining Yale School of Nursing. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement describing teaching philosophy, experience, and mentoring approach. Research statement outlining current scholarship, future research agenda, and plans for developing an externally funded program. Names and contact information for three professional references. For additional information about the Yale School of Nursing, please visit https://nursing.yale.edu . Questions regarding this position may be directed to: fao.ysn@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189642": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate in Injury Epidemiology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven School: Yale School of Public Health Department: Department of Health Policy & Management Anticipated Appointment Date: 9/1/2026 Fixed Term: One year, 10 months, Full-time. A postdoctoral position is available with Senior Research Scientist Kerri Raissian in the Department of Health Policy & Management at the Yale School of Public Health. Dr. Raissian is a quantitative, social policy researcher who uses causal research techniques to identify strategies to improve the criminal justice system response to domestic violence and firearm injury.  This postdoctoral fellowship is supported by a grant from Arnold Ventures related to further establishing a grant pipeline in criminal justice interventions. The position is housed within a rapidly growing team at YSPH focused on injury and violence prevention—led by Dr. Raissian, Dr. Christopher Morrison, Dr. Magdalena Cerda (Chair, Chronic Disease Epidemiology), and Dr. Megan Ranney (Dean, YSPH)—and will include opportunities of collaboration with other investigators within YSPH and across Yale University. The Postdoctoral Associate will receive training and mentorship in grant writing, causal methods, and establishing research partnerships. They will have structured opportunities to develop their proposal writing, methodological skills, and content expertise in the science of injury and violence prevention. The Postdoctoral Associate will be expected to lead and co-author manuscripts and applications for extramural funding, to continue their research currently in progress, and to develop new research ideas related to injury and violence prevention. Salary & Benefits Salary will be based on the Yale Postdoctoral Compensation policy . Support for travel to conferences and professional development activities are available. Information regarding benefits can be found here: Benefits | Office for Postdoctoral Affairs Applicants must have a doctoral degree from an accredited institution by the start of the appointment. The successful applicant will have a background in causal methods and quantitative techniques.  A PhD in in economics, public policy, public health, or related field is required. Highly desirable is demonstrated expertise in domestic violence, crimes related to firearms, or violence prevention. Opportunities for advancement may be available contingent on success during the postdoctoral appointment. Please apply online. Interested applicants should submit a (1) CV, (2) cover letter describing your research and interest in the position, and (3) contact information for three professional references via Interfolio."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189399": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiologist (R-2232, R-2412)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine’s Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging invites applications from board-certified Interventional Radiologists for a faculty appointment. Rank will be commensurate with experience. A strong interest in clinical care and education is required.  Scholarly output is encouraged but not required. Yale Interventional Radiology (YIR) is a nationally leading academic section which provides the entire spectrum of IR procedures with high-volume oncologic, vascular, transplant, trauma and pediatric services. Due to increasing service successes, the section is expanding. It is currently composed of 18 faculty, 8 advanced practice providers and 20 integrated and independent IR residents with access to a wide range of imaging modalities. The practice includes a large tertiary multi-disciplinary hospital (~1500 beds) with an associated NCI-designated cancer center, two affiliated peripheral inpatient hospitals (>500 beds), a VA hospital, two out-patient IR facilities and numerous IR clinics. Applicants should be enthusiastic about joining a mutually supportive group of nationally recognized faculty who excel at practicing “state-of-the art” IR within an academic environment. Within the Yale School of Medicine, the Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging is a research, teaching, and clinical center of excellence, devoted to providing optimal patient care through excellence in imaging and image guided therapy. The department has a long history as a pioneer in the field of Radiology and Imaging Sciences, and more than 100 years ago, was the first site in the United States to generate X-Rays. As the historical cradle of American radiology, our Department is currently listed nationally as one of the top 5 ranked research institutions as funded by the National Institutes of Health. New Haven has been home to the university for three centuries. With a population of 130,000 residents and measuring approximately 20 square miles, New Haven is “large enough to be interesting, yet small enough to be friendly.”  As a center for business and a mecca for the arts, the city is recognized for its innovation and culture, with great restaurants and a wealth of activities for families and single professionals of all ages.  New Haven is also conveniently located between New York and Boston, and both are easily accessible due to the area’s robust rail transit system. In addition to providing excellent clinical care, the candidate will be expected to expand the academic profile of the program in education and, if desired, clinical research. The candidate is expected to have multi-modality image guidance expertise, be technically proficient in a wide variety of procedures and have strong clinical acumen.  Depending on specific applicant credentials, protected non-clinical time will be provided to develop and expand practice and participate in national level CME. At least 3-5 years of clinical experience are expected from the applicant. The ideal applicant should have training and experience in advanced vascular interventions e.g. peripheral venous and arterial interventions, DVT and PE thrombectomies, vascular reconstruction and recanalization, aortic interventions (e.g. advanced graft endoleak repair) and be experienced in complex venous access / dialysis management. Prior experiences in logistics and management of these interventions in outpatient centers / OBL are encouraged. While the position is designed as 100% clinical IR, experience in diagnostic cardiovascular imaging would be strongly encouraged. Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to: apply.interfolio.com/189399 All final candidates will need to provide three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189153": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Nephrology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Nephrology Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Section of Nephrology is recruiting for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. The successful candidate will be an exceptional clinician with experience in the care of complex renal patients in the inpatient and ambulatory settings, and with a strong commitment to innovative clinical program development. They will have superb teaching skills for active participation in the teaching curriculum of the Nephrology fellowship program, and to supervise Nephrology fellows, Internal medicine residents and medical students in a busy clinical setting. Candidates must hold a Medical Degree and be board-eligible or board certified in nephrology. Candidates must also have excellent clinical training. Salary and academic rank will be determined by previous experience. Please apply to the position using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/189153 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188348": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business & the Environment, Sustainable Finance, or Environmental Markets",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of the Environment Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of the Environment (YSE) invites applications for an assistant professor position in Business & the Environment, Sustainable Finance, or Environmental Markets. We seek scholars whose research connects business or finance and the environment or natural resources to join a vibrant interdisciplinary community. This position is intentionally wide in scope. We welcome applicants from any area of business, finance, economics, marketing, supply‑chain management, environmental markets, or related interdisciplinary fields. Applicants should demonstrate potential to publish in top journals while collaborating with other scholars in the School of Environment. Examples of research focus include, but are not limited to: Connections between financial and environmental risks and their management, including insurance and risk‑management innovation; Financing solutions for conservation, climate adaptation, or biodiversity Commodity, natural resource, or environmental markets (timber, critical minerals, oil and gas, carbon or conservation credits etc.); Marketing and consumer behavior related to conservation and the environment; Environmental management within procurement, supplier reliability, supply chains, and logistics; Land markets, investment, easements, extraction rights, and transactions; Environmental connections to tax strategy. Advantages of working at Yale The Yale School of the Environment is a professional school that attracts outstanding students. YSE has strong connections with Yale’s School of Management (SOM), Yale’s Law School, and other departments across the university. The Yale School of Environment, together with the School of Management, runs the Center for Business and Environment at Yale (CBEY), which can provide a platform for the successful candidate. Yale also offers a high level of institutional support for high-impact scholarship. Disciplinary and interdisciplinary publications are valued by YSE. Prior to applying, candidates are encouraged to explore the School’s website ( http://environment.yale.edu ). The successful candidate will Have or show strong potential to develop an internationally recognized research program that connects business or finance and the environment or natural resources, Be enthusiastic about teaching business-related topics to master’s and PhD students in the Yale School of the Environment and in The Forest School which is part of the School of the Environment, Mentor YSE graduate students, Have a PhD in finance, marketing, business, supply chain & logistics, economics, or an interdisciplinary PhD with evidence of strong relevant PhD-level training. Applicants should apply online through interfolio.  Consideration of applications will begin October 15, 2026. Please upload: Curriculum Vitae, Statement of research, Statement of teaching interests A job market paper or representative sample of a research publication, The names and contact information of three professional references who can provide letters of recommendation upon request. Questions about the faculty search process can be directed to deansoffice.yse@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189040": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, Assistant/Associate Professor (2297)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Yale New Haven Hospital, Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Bridgeport Hospital, and/or Lawrence + Memorial Hospital, with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care as well as resident and fellow education.  There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/189040 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189041": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, Assistant/Associate Professor (2298)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Yale New Haven Hospital, Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Bridgeport Hospital, and/or Lawrence + Memorial Hospital, with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care as well as resident and fellow education.  There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/189041 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189060": {
      "title": "Academic Surgical Pathologist, GI (2195 & 2235)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pathology Location: Department of Pathology, YSM The Department of Pathology at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking an academic Surgical Pathologist at the Assistant/Associate Professor or full Professor level. Fellowship training or subspecialty expertise in GI is preferred. Participation in other subspecialty sign outs may be possible based on the candidate’s interest.  The successful candidate will participate in the service responsibilities of diagnostic practice; contribute to medical student, resident, and fellow teaching; and develop an academic program reflective of their interests. The Department serves Yale New Haven Hospital and Bridgeport Hospital, major teaching and referral centers in southern Connecticut, and a robust outreach program providing consultative services to regional practitioners and beyond. Southern Connecticut offers beautiful shoreline, affordable housing, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York, Boston, Newport, Cape Cod, and the ski slopes of New England. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification in Anatomic Pathology (and/or AP/CP) from the American Board of Pathology and eligibility for medical licensure in Connecticut are required.  Individuals with expertise and /or interest in clinical, translational or basic research are encouraged to apply. Academic rank and salary will depend on level of expertise and experience. All application materials must be uploaded through Interfolio, at apply.interfolio.com/189060 . These include a curriculum vitae, a letter of interest, and names and contact information for letters of recommendation from three senior references who are familiar with applicant's work and accomplishments. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Specific inquiries may be directed to Chen Liu, MD, PhD, Professor, Chair and Chief of Pathology, Yale School of Medicine, chen.liu@yale.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188970": {
      "title": "Adams Neuroscience Center - Endocrinology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Endocrinology Location: New Haven, CT The Section of Endocrinology is seeking an outstanding candidate at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the Academic Clinician track at Yale Medical School (YMS).  Candidates should be able to demonstrate outstanding skills in patient care and clinical teaching and must meet the requirements for clinical privileges at Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH).  YNHH is part of the Yale New Haven Health System (YNHHS), which includes a network of 5 hospitals across Connecticut and Rhode Island, Yale Medicine, and the New England Medical Group.  Collectively, YNHHS records over 3.6 million outpatient encounters and over 150,000 inpatient discharges per year providing a rich and diverse referral population. Successful applicants will have experience in all aspects of clinical endocrinology, interest in developing a robust inpatient and ambulatory practice, and excitement to practice in a teaching environment.  Over time, academic clinicians at YMS are expected to develop specific areas of disease expertise and regional and national prominence in their field of interest.  Current areas of interest include diabetes and obesity, bone and mineral metabolism, lipid disorders and endocrine neoplasia.  Position includes protected time for academic development. Required: Board certified in Internal Medicine, must have completed an Endocrinology fellowship in an ACGME-accredited program and be BC/BE in Endocrinology.  M.D. or D.O. All applications materials should be submitted electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/188970 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188175": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Yale Center for Healthcare Simulation",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine Location: New Haven, CT The Executive Director of the Yale Center for Healthcare Simulation (YCHS) provides strategic vision and operational leadership for Yale’s multidisciplinary simulation enterprise, advancing education, clinical care, and patient safety through high-quality, evidence-informed simulation programming. YCHS serves all Yale School of Medicine (YSM) medical and physician associate students, residents, fellows, and faculty, and supports clinicians and staff across Yale New Haven Health System (YNHHS) and its delivery networks. The Executive Director leads and integrates a comprehensive portfolio of simulation modalities—including high-fidelity manikin simulation, procedural simulation with task trainers, virtual reality simulation, in situ simulations, and Yale’s simulated participant program—ensuring that YCHS remains responsive to evolving educational standards, clinical priorities, and technological innovation. This position reports to the Deputy Dean for Education at Yale School of Medicine, with a dual reporting relationship to the Executive Vice President and Chief Clinical Officer of Yale New Haven Health System. The Executive Director is accountable for administrative leadership, educational quality and growth, outreach, innovation and technology strategy, and a robust simulation research agenda, including funding development and scholarly dissemination. Principal Responsibilities Provide strategic and operational leadership for YCHS across YSM and YNHHS, ensuring high-quality, reliable, and scalable simulation operations aligned with institutional priorities. Lead and develop YCHS personnel and faculty leadership, including supervision, mentoring, recruitment, and coordination with Human Resources for performance management and annual reviews. Convene and lead regular faculty and staff meetings to align operational, educational, clinical, and research priorities and drive continuous quality improvement. Build and sustain partnerships across YNHHS delivery networks and YSM departments/programs to extend and integrate simulation programming, including nursing and multidisciplinary education. Oversee and continuously improve all YCHS educational activities, ensuring instructional quality, learner experience, evaluation, and (as applicable) accreditation alignment. Provide operational and strategic oversight of core simulation modalities and programs, including the Simulated Participant Program, high-fidelity/manikin, procedural/task trainer, in situ, virtual reality (VR) / augmented reality (AR) , and related offerings. Expand and sustain simulation curricula and training across key clinical and training domains (e.g., Internal Medicine, Surgical Specialties, OB/GYN, Anesthesia, Pediatrics, Psychiatry, Neurology) and specialty-specific needs. Strengthen and scale debriefing education, including course offerings, faculty development, and dissemination of best practices across the system. Advance competency-based procedural and clinical training and assessment (including performance-based procedural assessment) and support learner portfolios and program evaluation where applicable. Expand and oversee interprofessional education and emergency medical services ( EMS ) training initiatives in collaboration with designated faculty and staff leaders. Ensure reliable daily center operations through coordination of technical functioning, scheduling, prioritization, and resource allocation. Provide budget planning and stewardship in collaboration with YSM and YNHHS partners; align financial resources to strategic priorities. Support communications, web presence, publicity, and philanthropic engagement in partnership with strategy/development leadership and YSM/YNHHS stakeholders. Oversee the Medical Simulation Fellowship and plan for future fellowship expansion across specialties. Coordinate and serve as a non-voting member of the YCHS Advisory Board, including planning and executing biannual meetings. Represent - or delegate representation of - YCHS on relevant institutional committees and working groups across YSM and YNHHS (e.g., simulation/education committees, curriculum committees, clinical skills assessment, continuing medical education ). Develop, evaluate, and expand outreach initiatives (e.g., Simulation Academy at Yale ) and steward major funded outreach/education programs (e.g., NIH R25). Review, approve, and prioritize internal and external requests to use YCHS facilities and programming for research, clinical training, outreach or other purposes, ensuring alignment with mission and capacity. Collaborate with YSM education al technology innovation leadership and coordinate with YSM/YNHHS IT partners to ensure robust technology infrastructure supporting simulation operations. Evaluate and implement emerging simulation technologies (including AR/VR platforms) and guide purchasing decisions consistent with instructional goals, evidence, privacy/security requirements, and sustainability. Oversee and advance YCHS research strategy and operations, including governance, mentorship, investigator support, and integration with educational and clinical priorities. Develop and oversee charge structures and budgeting guidance for use of YCHS resources on research grants in coordination with YSM/YNHHS finance leadership. Required Skills and Abilities Demonstrated ability to lead complex, cross-organizational programs spanning academic medicine and an integrated health system. Proven people leadership, including staff supervision, performance management, mentoring, recruitment, and team development. Strong operational leadership skills, including resource prioritization across high-demand educational and clinical initiatives. Excellence in stakeholder management and partnership-building with deans, department leaders, faculty directors, clinical leaders, and administrative teams. Ability to design, oversee, and continuously improve simulation-based education, including debriefing, assessment, and learner progression across training levels. Strong understanding of simulation modalities and infrastructure (manikin-based simulation, procedural/task training, VR/AR, in situ simulation, and simulated participant programming). Strong communication skills (written, verbal, and facilitation), including the ability to represent YCHS to internal and external audiences. Familiarity with research program development, including collaboration support, funding strategy, and dissemination through conferences and publications. Budget stewardship and the ability to align financial planning with programmatic priorities in partnership with academic and health system finance leaders. Preferred Skills and Abilities Experience directing a simulation center or comparable clinical education enterprise at scale. Demonstrated expertise in debriefing education and faculty development for simulation facilitation. Experience integrating simulation into undergraduate medical education, graduate medical education, and continuing professional education. Experience with educational technology innovation, including evaluation and implementation of AR/VR/ artificial intelligence (AI) -enabled learning tools. Track record of securing external funding (e.g., NIH, AHRQ, foundations) and serving as PI or co-investigator. Evidence of scholarly and professional contributions to health care simulation, medical education, patient safety, or human factors. Experience developing outreach programs and pipeline initiatives (e.g., K–12/high school programming, admissions-related outreach). Required Education and Experience Advanced degree (e.g., MD, DO, PhD, EdD, or comparable) in a relevant field. Progressive responsibility in health care education, simulation operations, or academic/clinical program leadership, including significant management experience with staff and faculty leaders . D emonstrated success leading complex, cross-stakeholder initiatives . E xperience overseeing budgets and operational planning in partnership with academic and/or health system stakeholders. Preferred Education and Experience Formal training and/or recognized expertise in health care simulation, medical education, patient safety, human factors, or quality improvement. Experience as PI or co-investigator on externally funded projects (federal and/or foundation). Record of peer-reviewed scholarship and professional leadership in health care simulation or medical education. Experience leading technology-enabled education initiatives, including AR/VR/AI applications in simulation. Candidates are asked to provide their CV and a statement of interest directly through the provided link. https://apply.interfolio.com/188175"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188507": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: General Medicine Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the Section of General Medicine. This will be in a clinical practice at New Haven Primary Care Consortium, a patient-centered medical home academic adult primary care and the main site for the traditional Internal Medicine residents ambulatory training. Primary responsibilities are management of a primary care panel of patients, conducting in-person clinic sessions as well as telehealth sessions, as well as all administrative work associated with the clinical practice. Teaching responsibilities include precepting in resident clinic, supervising and evaluating a team of the residents, and teaching medical students in the ambulatory practice. Up to 4 weeks of inpatient attending on a resident team is required. Participation in the care of the NHPCC team on-call coverage in rotation as well as attendance at regular meetings of the NHPCC  clinical team and participation in projects to improve quality of care. Participation in the academic activities of the Section of General Internal Medicine. Opportunities exist for other educational and scholarly work depending on the interest of the faculty member. ABIM Board-Certified, Internal Medicine with interest/expertise in office-based practice. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. Candidates should apply directly through Interfolio at the link: https://apply.interfolio.com/188507 Candidates are asked to provide their CV, Cover Letter, and three letters of recommendation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188502": {
      "title": "Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation - AI Researcher - Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Professor (RFP-2277)",
      "description": "Posted: Jun 22, 2026 Deadline: Jun 21, 2028 Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation Location: New Haven, CT Faculty Position in AI-Driven Musculoskeletal Research Yale University School of Medicine – Department of Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation The Department of Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation at Yale University School of Medicine invites applications for a faculty position (Instructor, Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) in the tenure track for candidates with expertise in artificial intelligence (AI) and a strong interest in musculoskeletal (MSK) research and/or orthopedic surgery. Applicants must hold a PhD and/or MD (or equivalent degree) and demonstrate outstanding qualifications in research and education. Areas of Interest Include: · Artificial intelligence and machine learning applications in musculoskeletal medicine and orthopedic surgery · Biomedical data science and modeling relevant to MSK health · Image analysis and computer vision for orthopedic imaging · Clinical informatics and outcomes research in orthopedics · Precision medicine and personalized approaches to MSK disorders · Biomechanical modeling, simulation, and computational orthopedics · Integration of AI with electronic medical records and surgical workflows Responsibilities: · Establish and maintain a vigorous, independently funded research program in AI-driven musculoskeletal science · Collaborate with clinical and research faculty in orthopedics, engineering, and data science · Supervise and mentor students, residents, and fellows from diverse backgrounds · Contribute to the educational missions of the department and Yale School of Medicine · Foster an environment of collaboration, innovation, and scientific discovery · PhD and/or MD (or equivalent) with demonstrated expertise in AI, data science, or related fields · Track record of independent, creative research accomplishments · Track record of federally funded (NSF, NIH, etc) research · Interest or experience in musculoskeletal research and/or orthopedic surgery is preferred · Strong scientific, management, and interpersonal skills All interested candidates are asked to apply via Interfolio: apply.interfolio.com/188502 Please provide your curriculum vitate and a list of three references."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188477": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Urologic Oncology (202606-2279)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Urology Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Urology is a leading provider of patient care. We are seeking a full-time Urologic Oncologist to join our team. The applicant will be a member of Yale Medicine and will join the medical staff of Yale-New Haven Hospital. A commitment to multidisciplinary care, clinical innovation, and a consistently outstanding experience for patients and their families is expected. Depending on the interests of the successful candidate, this position could involve various opportunities to participate in clinical, translational, or population-based research and the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows. Our department anticipates that the successful candidate will have a dynamic personality, outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to academic collaboration. Applicants must hold a M.D. degree and be board certified/board eligible in Urology to qualify. Academic appointment will be commensurate with experience. Interested candidates should apply directly through the provided link. https://apply.interfolio.com/188477"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188341": {
      "title": "Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation - PM&R –Interventionalist  - Assistant/Associate Professor (RFP-2266)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation Location: Bridgeport, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Orthopaedics & Rehabilitation are leaders in patient care, education, and non-surgical and surgical innovation. We seek a PM&R physician for a full-time faculty position with interest and expertise in Interventional Physiatry. Primary responsibilities will include: · Outpatient clinical services focused on spine and general musculoskeletal care. o This includes fluoroscopically guided spinal procedures. o Proficiency in ultrasound guided musculoskeletal interventions is also preferred. · Participate in the training of residents, medical students, and other allied health students. Secondary Opportunities may include: · Research: if desired, engage in research activities, depending on the wishes and skill set of the candidate. Research is supported and valued. · Orthobiologics if interested. · NCS/EMG skillset is not required but there are opportunities for interested candidates. · Interventional spasticity management if interested. · Inpatient consultations if interested. Academic Appointment: · Assistant or Associate Professor commensurate with experience and qualifications. Practice Details: Competitive Salary's with RVU based bonus Outpatient practice working primarily Monday through Friday. No in-person call. Telephone call service divided amongst the outpatient physiatry team which is generally light. Residents are first call. Primary practice location(s): Fairfield County ·         Board Eligible/Certified in Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (PM&R) · Fellowship training in either Interventional Spine and Musculoskeletal Medicine or Pain Medicine is required. All interested candidates are asked to apply via Interfolio: apply.interfolio.com/188341 Please provide your curriculum vitate and a list of three references."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188219": {
      "title": "Child and Adolescent Psychiatrist - Greenwich Hospital",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: Greenwich, CT The Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Health at Greenwich Hospital seeks to recruit a Child and Adolescent Psychiatrist to join our adolescent psychiatry team. Located at our Greenwich Office (500 West Putnam Avenue), the psychiatrist will provide medication management for adolescents engaged in the department’s intensive outpatient program (IOP) and for adolescents and young adults seeking pharmacotherapy. The psychiatrist will work collaboratively with an APRN on site and the treatment team to provide diagnostic and therapeutic services for patients. What sets this role apart is the opportunity to work side-by-side with other staff on an interdisciplinary team, follow patients across IOP and outpatient settings, and provide clinical care on a team that is embedded within a larger department of psychiatry and behavioral health. This is an ideal role for a psychiatrist who enjoys structured program work, values real-time collaboration, and wants the satisfaction of building ongoing therapeutic relationships in outpatient care. Responsibilities will include: · Providing triage, initial assessments, and management of patients and their family needs throughout the treatment process as an integral part of an interdisciplinary team. · Working in collaboration with the APRN and LCSWs as part of the treatment team. · Participating in team-based case conferences, treatment planning, and coordinating discharge planning. Benefits Yale University offers Yale Signature Benefits, including but not limited to: ·         Medical coverage through Yale Health and Aetna ·         Dental coverage through Delta Dental ·         Vision coverage options through Eyemed ·         Yale University Retirement Account Plan ·         Paid time off ·         Disability coverage ·         Life insurance ·         Mortgage loan program ·         Commuter benefits ·         Yale Homebuyer program ·         College tuition benefit plan Yale ·         Advantage discount program (Discounts for Activities, Travel, services, shopping, etc) The successful candidates will have completed a residency in psychiatry leading to board eligibility or board certification and will have also completed a child and adolescent psychiatry fellowship in addition to being licensed within the State of Connecticut. To apply to this position, please use the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/188219. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. If you have questions about this job opportunity, please contact Kourtney Koslosky via email at Kourtney.Koslosky@yale.edu for more information."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187944": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor; YIMA General Internal Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: General Medicine Location: New Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the Section of General Medicine. The position is based at Yale Internal Medicine Associates (YIMA), a highly collegial, premier academic adult primary care faculty practice.  YIMA physicians practice at the top of their license, supported by an exceptional, highly coordinated team of advanced practice providers, nursing professionals, and administrative staff that streamlines care and reduces nonclinical burden. Primary responsibilities are management of a primary care panel of patients, conducting in-person clinic sessions as well as telehealth sessions, and administrative work associated with clinical practice. Teaching responsibilities include teaching of medical students and residents in the ambulatory practice setting. Up to 4 weeks of inpatient attending on a resident teaching firm at Yale-New Haven Hospital may be required. The position includes participation in YIMA on-call coverage, in regular collaborative meetings of the YIMA clinical team, and in the academic activities of the Section of General Internal Medicine. Opportunities exist for other educational and scholarly work depending on the interest of the faculty member. A Departmental incentive program is available. ABIM Board-Certified, Internal Medicine with interest/expertise in office-based practice. Review of applications will commence immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Applicants are asked to apply online: https://apply.interfolio.com/187944"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187918": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Neurohospitalist ANC (RFP 202603-2213)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New Haven County The Department of Neurology at the Yale School of Medicine seeks to hire a neurohospitalist at the rank of Assistant/ Associate Professor to complement our services at the Adam Neuroscience Center  at Yale-New Haven Hospital Saint Raphael's Campus in New Haven, CT.  Rank will be based on education and experience. The position is composed of 24 service weeks (Monday – Sunday) and will include evaluation and management of the whole spectrum of neurological disorders in the emergency department, the intensive care units, as well as on the medical and surgical floors. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to excellence in patient care, the highest quality and safety standards, as well as education of the next generation of neurologists. The position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied clinical or academic interests within our department. It is an exciting time to join Yale Neurology with the upcoming opening of The Adams Neurosciences Center at Yale New Haven Hospital. The ANC will serve as an integrated inpatient academic hub for the diagnosis, treatment, and investigation of complex neurological and neurosurgical disorders and serve as a major access point of patients requiring continuing outpatient care. Anchored in advanced translational research and multidisciplinary clinical expertise, the Center will provide comprehensive, evidence-based care across the full spectrum of medical and surgical therapies. Through the integration of clinical innovation, emerging technologies, and collaborative research, the Center will advance scientific discovery while delivering highly individualized treatment strategies aimed at improving patient outcomes in disorders of the brain and nervous system. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent and be board certified/board eligible in Neurology and may have subspecialty fellowship training.  Applicants must meet the criteria for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Faculty rank will be based on experience. Please upload a brief statement of interest, current CV and three contact references to the following link: apply.interfolio.com/187918 For additional information, please contact YSMNeurology.facultyaffairs@yale.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186941": {
      "title": "2027-2028 Lewis Walpole Library Visiting Fellowships and Travel Grants",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Library: Lewis Walpole Library Location: Lewis Walpole Library, Farmington, CT The Lewis Walpole Library funds four-week visiting fellowships and two-week travel grants to support research in the library’s rich collections of mostly British materials from the long eighteenth-century. Fellowship and Travel Grant Award recipients also have access to additional resources at Yale, including those in the Sterling Memorial Library, the Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, and the Yale Center for British Art. Awards include: the round-trip cost of travel between the Lewis Walpole Library and the recipient’s home institution or residence reimbursement of the cost of a rental car or local travel expenses accommodation for four weeks (fellowships) or two weeks (travel grants) in an eighteenth-century house on the Library’s campus a per diem living allowance to cover living expenses for four-week Fellows and two-week Travel Grant Recipients*. The per diem is calculated using the US General Services Administration’s current per diem rates (M & IE portion) for the Hartford, CT area. The Fellowship Year runs between June 1, 2027 through May 31, 2028. *Please note that payments to non-U.S. citizens (nonresident alien for U.S. tax purposes) are subject to up to 30% federal tax withholding, per Internal Revenue Service (IRS) regulations, which you may be eligible to have reimbursed by the Internal Revenue Service. Please also note that a visa may be required for non-US citizens depending upon the country of your citizenship. ELIGIBILITY : who is invited to apply: Scholars pursuing postdoctoral or advanced research Doctoral candidates at work on a dissertation EXPECTATIONS : all Fellowship and Travel Grant Award recipients are expected to: complete fellowships within the fellowship year (June 1 through May 31) be in residence at the library. The Library requires Fellows stay in the Timothy Root House on campus for the duration of their award. Housing is provided to Fellows only (no guests, partners, or children) be free of other significant professional obligations during their stay take their fellowship in one uninterrupted period focus research substantially on the Lewis Walpole Library’s collections An application form completed online A curriculum vitae, including educational background, professional experience and publications (3 pages maximum) A brief outline of the research proposal (1200 words maximum) that includes a detailed explanation of how the Lewis Walpole Library’s collections will support the research project the value of your project to your field A detailed list of Lewis Walpole Library collection materials to be examined during your fellowship or travel grant, including titles (from Quicksearch ), collection names (from Archives at Yale ), call numbers, and any other relevant identifying details. Two confidential letters of recommendation. Letters should specifically address the merits of the candidate’s project and its relevance to the collections available at the Lewis Walpole Library. General letters of recommendation or dossier letters will not be considered. The online application includes a link to request letters of recommendation and which the recommenders use to upload letters directly."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187326": {
      "title": "Postgraduate Associate - Reilly Lab, Dept. of Genetics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Genetics Location: New Haven, CT We are looking for strong, ambitious candidates with previous research backgrounds in molecular biology, human genetics, evolutionary biology, genomic technologies, bioinformatics, or machine-learning. We value students who appreciate challenging themselves and take pride in providing a supportive environment in which trainees can flourish and grow as scientists. The trainee will receive hands-on education in molecular genomics, population genetics, evolutionary theory, non-coding regulatory biology, and/or bioinformatics via their participation in research projects in the laboratory. This genomics-focused training would prepare a trainee for a future graduate or medical school applications, or any relevant field where hands-on research experience is required. The trainee will gain direct education into data analysis, experimental design, problem solving, and time management. There is some flexibility to match the trainee’s interests and aptitude to specific projects of interest. If primarily interested in wet lab, the Postgraduate Associate will train in developing and deploying genomic techniques such as MPRA and CRISPR screens. They will be expected to learn advanced cell culture, cloning, and next-generation sequencing techniques. Potential projects include investigating the gene targets of disease-related variation and exploring gene regulation across different cell types. If primarily interested in computational work, the Postgraduate Associate will train in developing new computational tools and techniques to advance our understanding of the human genome and its role in disease and evolution. Potential projects include applying machine learning models and population genetic methods to predict and understand regulatory variants, collaborating with experimental biologists on developing novel uses of high-throughput reporter assays, and analyzing CRISPR editing and high-throughput reporter assay data to uncover new insights into the genetics of human disease and evolution. The Postgraduate Associate is expected to develop into an integral, valued member of the lab, to participate in weekly lab meetings/journal clubs, to present their research findings, and to attend research seminars. The Reilly lab takes its role in training future scientists seriously and sees the postgraduate’s future success as the lab’s own success. The Postgraduate Associate will meet regularly with the PI and/or direct mentors to discuss scientific progress and career development. Previous trainees have gone onto top-tier graduate programs, medical schools, and industry positions. Postgraduates completing a full term in lab have each left with authorship on at least one manuscript. As a part of the Department of Genetics at the Yale School of Medicine, the lab offers an outstanding and fully resourced training environment which provides the flexibility to meet the trainee’s professional goals. The candidate should display a high level of initiative, logic, and creative problem solving skills, as well as a must have bachelor’s degree in biology, genetics, bioinformatics, or relevant field. The candidate is also required to have excellent personal initiative and should be excited by the prospect of working in a dynamic team. They should demonstrate aptitude for time management skills in coordinating concurrent assignments in a multi-faceted project. Candidates should possess strong communication and computer skills, with the ability to develop technical documents and presentations. For wet-lab candidates , 1+ years of prior molecular biology research experience is required. Strong coursework in molecular biology/genetics is beneficial. For computational candidates, excellent coding skills and coursework in molecular biology/genetics are required. Candidates with experience in bioinformatics, evolutionary biology, genetics, machine learning, mammalian cell culture, molecular biology, or sequencing are especially encouraged to apply. The appointment will be for 1 year, with the possibility of extension or further opportunities. Interested candidates should apply via Interfolio (insert link). The application should include: (1) CV; (2) a cover letter including a brief description of research interests and how they align with the lab; and (3) either (a) letters from or (b) contact information for 2-3 references."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187100": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Field of Early Psychosis",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Psychiatry Location: New Haven The position focuses primarily on advancing knowledge in the field of early psychosis. Specific duties include: Assisting with leadership of two large NIMH-funded multi-center studies for youth at CHR; including developing experience with oversight of: site management, recruitment and retention, data quality, fiscal resources, and NIMH reporting; Establishing an independent research focus in early psychosis; Securing independent funding for research in early psychosis; Prescribing study medication for youth at CHR participating in clinical trials; Prescribing clinical medication for PRIME Clinic patients Other clinical responsibilities as interested; Teaching responsibilities as invited or as interested Applicants must have demonstrated academic productivity, hold the degree of Medical Doctor and have completed a psychiatry residency. In addition, applicants must be license eligible in the State of Connecticut to practice medicine, be a US citizen, or permanent resident, or holder of visa permitting employment. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  A cover letter, a CV, and 3 letters of recommendation are required. Apply to this position through Interfolio using this link http://apply.interfolio.com/ 187100 .  If you have questions about this position, please contact Dr. Scott Woods via email using scott.woods@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184726": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate Position — Functional Genomics / Regulatory Genomics / Human Evolution & Disease (Reilly Lab)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Genetics Location: New Haven, CT The Reilly Lab seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Associate to join an interdisciplinary research program focused on understanding how genetic variants impact human health, evolution, and disease. The lab seeks to answer a fundamental question remaining in biology: \"how do genetic changes lead to functional changes at the molecular, cellular, and phenotypic level?\" The Reilly Lab is funded by the NIH, the Pew Charitable Trusts, and other foundations, and is an affiliate of the Impact of Genomic Variation on Function (IGVF) consortium as well as part of an ENCODE functional characterization center. The lab is especially interested in non-coding cis-regulatory elements (CREs) and the variation within them, using high-throughput experimental approaches such as non-coding CRISPR screens, the Massively Parallel Reporter Assay (MPRA), saturation mutagenesis, and synthetic sequence design, alongside machine-learning models of regulatory grammar. The postdoctoral associate will – based on their research interest – contribute across one or more of the lab's five core themes: Genomic Technology: Design and execute new, large-scale experimental screens to perturb CREs, including non-coding CRISPR screens and MPRAs. Deciphering Regulatory \"Grammar\": Use saturation mutagenesis paired with machine-learning models to understand the rules by which CREs regulate gene expression. Interrogating Genetic Architectures: Explore how combinations of variants together create a phenotype or disease state through phenotype associations and network logic models. Writing Novel Genome Function: Design and validate synthetic sequences that promote cell-type-specific gene expression. Exploring Evolution & Human Health: Investigate how changes in the non-coding genome shape modern human phenotypes, disease risk, and the evolution of our species, including signals of positive selection across global populations. In addition, the postdoctoral associate will: Analyze and interpret large-scale genomic, functional genomics, and population genetics datasets Contribute to manuscript preparation, grant writing, and collaborative projects within the lab and across the IGVF and ENCODE consortia Participate in written and oral communication of research findings Prep and publish original research, including abstracts and peer-reviewed manuscripts Mentor trainees (as appropriate) and participate in a highly interactive research environment We're looking for inquisitive, creative, and passionate researchers with a PhD, MD, or MD/PhD (or related field such as genetics, genomics, computational biology, biochemistry, machine learning, population genetics, or evolutionary biology). The lab is multi-disciplinary, and applicants from a variety of backgrounds — including those interested in human evolution, building new genomic tools, or analyzing complex data — would find a project here. Strong communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team are essential. A two-year commitment is required. Interested postdoctoral applicants should apply via Interfolio: https://apply.interfolio.com/184726 and include (1) a CV, (2) a brief description of their scientific interests and how these intersect with the lab's interests, and (3) copies of their major manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187000": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor-Maternal Fetal Medicine (202605-2258)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences Location: New Haven, CT Academic appointment will be at Yale University at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor in the Division of Maternal-Fetal-Medicine (MFM). The MFM Division has enjoyed unprecedented clinical, academic and research growth.  The successful candidate would participate in a rotational schedule to provide inpatient, consultative and prenatal diagnostic services at Yale University and affiliated clinical locations.  Interest and experience in basic and/or translational research will be considered an asset.  The Department is currently ranked 6th among Ob/Gyn departments in NIH funding, supports numerous clinical trials, and has a large Division of Reproductive Sciences which houses outstanding basic and translational research in the areas of pregnancy sciences, uterine biology, cancer biology and ovarian/gamete biology led by physician-scientists and PhD researchers. A commitment to teaching is required in order to provide outstanding instruction to medical students, residents and fellows in various clinical venues. We are seeking a full-time specialist, fellowship-trained in maternal fetal medicine. Commensurate with experience and CV required, cover letter highly recommended. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae to: https://apply.interfolio.com/187000"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186922": {
      "title": "Department of Radiology, Nuclear Medicine Radiologist (R-2262)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Radiology and Biomedical Imaging Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Radiology & Biomedical Imaging at Yale School of Medicine is seeking a Nuclear Medicine Radiologist for a full-time faculty appointment in the Nuclear Medicine Section. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. The successful candidate will join a dynamic and expanding nuclear medicine program and will play an integral role in managing and advancing a progressive clinical service. Clinical responsibilities include the full spectrum of general nuclear medicine, nuclear therapies, PET/CT, and participation in a rapidly growing theranostics program encompassing both clinical care and research activities. PET/MRI capabilities are being introduced with the installation of a new system in Yale’s $848 million Neuroscience Tower, providing exceptional opportunities for clinical innovation and translational research. Faculty members are expected to devote a significant portion of their effort to clinical service while maintaining a strong commitment to the education and mentorship of radiology residents and nuclear medicine fellows. Teaching occurs across clinical rotations, conferences, and interdisciplinary forums. There are outstanding opportunities for research and scholarly activity, particularly in molecular imaging. Faculty have access to the world-renowned Yale PET Center within the Yale Biomedical Imaging Institute, with established tradition in research excellence and research facilities that include a medical cyclotron, PET radiochemistry with over 40 active INDs, high resolution brain PET-CT (HRRT and NeuroExplorer), 2 whole body PET-CT, 4 whole body 3T MR, one whole body 4T MR as well as state-of-the art small animal imaging resources. Collaborative research with basic scientists, clinician investigators, and industry partners is strongly supported and encouraged. Depending on experience and interest, candidates may pursue leadership roles, participate in program development, and engage in institutional initiatives aligned with Yale’s missions in clinical excellence, education, and discovery. Yale School of Medicine offers a collegial academic environment, robust institutional support, and outstanding resources to support clinical excellence, education, and research. Board certified or board eligible in Diagnostic Radiology (ABR) and Nuclear Medicine (ABNM), with certification expected within one year of hire if board eligible Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut Demonstrated commitment to clinical excellence and high-quality patient care Strong dedication to teaching residents and fellows Interest in research, innovation, and multidisciplinary collaboration is highly desirable Interested applicants should upload their CV and cover letter to: apply.interfolio.com/186922 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186720": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Yale Center for Research on Aging (Y-Age)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pathology Location: Yale School of Medicine, Department of Pathology The Department of Pathology at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking applications a tenure track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level (Ph.D. or M.D./DVM/Ph.D.) to build an interdisciplinary research program in the new Yale Center for Research on Aging (Y-Age).  The Center is largely housed in the Department of Pathology, but has strong ties with other Yale School of Medicine Departments and Centers and the Yale University community. The position will be supported by a generous startup package and resources of Yale. Successful candidates will be expected to establish a competitive and impactful research program in the basic biology of aging, but with an eye on translation of findings into the chronic diseases of aging in the broad areas of Inflammation, Immunosenescence, metabolism, nutrition, neuroimmunology, epigenetics, senescence or cancer.  Other responsibilities will include contributions to Yale’s teaching and service missions and, if appropriate, its clinical programs. The application package should include a curriculum vitae, a summary of present and future research interests (maximum 3 pages), and a mentorship and diversity statement (maximum 1 page). Three letters of reference will be requested for select candidates only. All application materials must be uploaded through the following Interfolio website: apply.interfolio.com/186720 . Specific inquiries can be directed to: Vishwa Deep Dixit, DVM., Ph.D. Waldemar Von Zedtwitz Professor of Pathology, Comparative Medicine and Immunobiology, Director, Yale Center for Research on Aging, Yale School of Medicine 310 Cedar Street, New Haven CT 06510 email: Vishwa.dixit@yale.edu Additional inquiries may be directed to Monica Solorzano, Faculty Affairs Department of Pathology, Yale School of Medicine, 310 Cedar Street, New Haven CT 06520 email: monica.solorzano@yale.edu Review of applications will begin May 13, 2026 but the position will remain open until filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185611": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Neuromuscular Division (RFP# 202604-2238)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New Haven County The Neuromuscular Program is dedicated to the delivery of expert clinical care as well as to the education of both patients and colleagues at all levels of training. Members of the Program faculty are all board certified/eligible neurologists with special training in neuromuscular disease and electromyography. The program is very active in basic science and clinical research in various areas of neuromuscular disease, with faculty as members of both the Northeast ALS Alliance Consortium (NEALS) and the World Federation of Neurology ALS Consortium. We specialize in ALS, Myasthenia Gravis, Myopathy, Neuropathy, Muscular Dystrophy and related disorders. We seek motivated academics with clinical expertise in: 1) the evaluation and treatment of adult neuromuscular and neurology patients, 2) performing EMG testing 3) teaching residents, fellows, and medical students. It is anticipated that these positions will be primarily clinical and located in both New Haven and North Haven. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to the education of the next generation of subspecialty experts. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. This position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied academic interests within our division. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent and be board certified/board eligible in Neurology and have completed a fellowship in Neuromuscular Medicine.  Applicants must meet the criteria for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Faculty rank will be based on experience. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and three contact references by applying the following link : apply.interfolio.com/185611"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185331": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Public Health",
      "description": "Posted: Apr 24, 2026 Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, CT  The Yale School of Public Health (YSPH), Data Science and Data Equity (DSDE) Initiative invites applications for a Senior Lecturer in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Public Health . This is a teaching - and training - focused faculty appointment for an individual who will help advance DSDE’s educational mission by developing and delivering high-quality instruction in data science and artificial intelligence and its responsible application in public health research, practice, and policy. The home department within YSPH will be decided based on background of the applicant. The successful candidate will contribute to YSPH’s growing efforts to prepare students to understand, evaluate, and apply AI methods in ways that are rigorous, ethical, and relevant to real-world public health contexts. The Senior Lecturer will develop and teach courses on AI in Public Health and help build institutional capacity through workshops, short courses, summer programs, certificate programs, and other educational programming and offerings for students, faculty, and staff. This faculty member will work collaboratively with colleagues across YSPH and Yale to strengthen teaching and training at the intersection of AI, data science, and public health. The ideal candidate will bring strong applied expertise, a record of exceptional teaching and educational leadership, and the ability to connect emerging AI methods and tools with the needs of public health learners and practitioners. Senior Lecturer Expectations In keeping with Yale’s expectations for Senior Lecturers, the successful candidate will demonstrate: Superior teaching that effectively brings practice into the classroom in a way that is linked to a rigorous body of knowledge. Intensive engagement in the activities of the School , such that the YSPH position is the faculty member’s primary career focus. Hands-on coding and visualization expertise in R and Python augmented by new AI capabilities to support an applied researcher/student with cutting-edge use of data science and AI. Through teaching and engagement, the provision of experience and expertise that the School views as essential but otherwise lacks in the area of AI in Public Health. Serve as an academic lead for the launch of certificate programs in data science and AI in public health. A graduate degree in a relevant field such as public health, biostatistics, epidemiology, data science, computer science, informatics, mathematics, health services research, health policy, or a related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in AI methods and their applications in public health or closely related domains. Demonstrated experience with coding in R and Python. Evidence of exceptional teaching ability and educational leadership, such as prior instruction, curriculum development, training leadership, workshop facilitation, or comparable contributions. Demonstrated ability to teach technical concepts clearly to learners with varied backgrounds. Commitment to an academic environment that values intellectual rigor, integrity, and inclusive excellence. Preferred Doctoral degree in a relevant field. Prior experience teaching graduate students and/or professionals. Experience applying AI in public health practice settings such as government, health systems, nongovernmental organizations, implementation settings, industry, or research environments. Experience teaching or developing content on responsible AI, including topics such as ethics, fairness, transparency, governance, privacy, and evaluation. Experience with generative AI, large language models, or related computational tools, especially in ways that support teaching, training, or applied public health problem-solving. A record of 5 or more years of exceptional teaching and educational leadership consistent with Senior Lecturer consideration. Yale University and the Yale School of Public Health are committed to excellence. We welcome applications from candidates who will contribute to the academic vitality of YSPH and to the education of public health leaders prepared to use AI responsibly and effectively for population health impact. Appointment terms, start date, and compensation are competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants should submit: A cover letter describing interest in the position and relevant experience in teaching data science and AI in Public Health. Curriculum vitae. A teaching statement that describes the applicant’s approach to instruction, inclusive teaching, and integration of applied practice with scholarly rigor. Sample syllabi or course/workshop materials, if available (including an AI use policy). Teaching evaluations, if available. Names and contact information for three references."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185445": {
      "title": "Associate Research Scientist, Brain Metastasis Group",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pathology Location: Yale Department of Pathology and Yale Cancer Center The Brain Metastasis group at the Department of Pathology and Yale Cancer Center wishes to hire an Associate Research Scientist (ARS) who will coordinate translational research collaborations and anchor clinical and basic research projects on brain metastasis. This position will serve as the interface between the clinical and laboratory settings for development of shared research resources, ongoing collection of clinical specimens, and integration of laboratory data into research databases.  This person will be responsible for overall program cohesion as well as management of the above shared resources across multidisciplinary and multi-institutional projects.  With a high degree of independence, the ARS will coordinate with university and hospital departments as well as collaborating physicians and research laboratories to participate in all aspects of translational research. Expected responsibilities would include: a) Ensuring compliance with HIC/IRB for both basic science and clinical protocols. b) Screen weekly Operating room (OR), gamma knife (GK) and clinic schedules to identify project relevant cases for clinical data and tissue collection c) Consent of research patients for the collection of tissue samples d) Collect relevant samples from Yale OR and Trumbull clinic and transfer to lab for processing e) Data entry and maintenance of GK and clinical databases f) Extraction of data, with potential statistical analysis for publication or inclusion in multidisciplinary and multicentered studies g) Assistance with MPI grant submission and progress reports The successful candidate should have a PhD or MD degree in a biomedical or clinical related field, preferably with at least 2 years of prior research experience. Interested applicants should upload their CV, cover letter, and three letters of reference to apply.interfolio.com/185445 ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185231": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, NORA, Assistant/Associate Professor (2189)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care, including non-operating room anesthesia, as well as resident and fellow education. There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/185231 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185237": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, NORA, Assistant/Associate Professor (2190)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care, including non-operating room anesthesia, as well as resident and fellow education. There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/185237 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185232": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, NORA, Assistant/Associate Professor (2194)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care, including non-operating room anesthesia, as well as resident and fellow education. There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/185232 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185234": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, General, NORA, Assistant/Associate Professor (2193)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care, including non-operating room anesthesia, as well as resident and fellow education. There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/185234 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185136": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, General Neurology  (RFP 202509-2030)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New Haven County The Division of General Neurology evaluates and treats all neurological conditions. The division includes the Yale Headache Center, which specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of headaches, and the Yale Neurology Resident Clinics. The Resident Clinics offer specialized care in general neurology and stroke and include the Neurology Urgent Access Clinic (NUAC). The goal of NUAC is to allow expedited evaluation of patients seen in the emergency room as well as those referred from physicians requiring an urgent assessment. A major role of the division is to ensure patients are seen by appropriate sub-specialists within the department. If the diagnosis is unclear or the patient would benefit from sub-specialty care, then the General Neurology Division will initially evaluate patients and make internal referrals to the appropriate sub-specialists to allow for the best possible care. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. This position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied academic interests within our division and department. Rank will be based on education and experience. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to the education of the next generation of subspecialty experts. We seek motivated academic physicians with clinical expertise in: 1) the care of adult general neurology and subspecialty patients, 2) Participation in clinical trials, 3) Opportunity to teach. Practice location will be in New Haven County. It is an exciting time to join Yale Neurology with the upcoming opening of The Adams Neurosciences Center at Yale New Haven Hospital. The ANC will serve as an integrated inpatient academic hub for the diagnosis, treatment, and investigation of complex neurological and neurosurgical disorders and serve as a major access point of patients requiring continuing outpatient care. Anchored in advanced translational research and multidisciplinary clinical expertise, the Center will provide comprehensive, evidence-based care across the full spectrum of medical and surgical therapies. Through the integration of clinical innovation, emerging technologies, and collaborative research, the Center will advance scientific discovery while delivering highly individualized treatment strategies aimed at improving patient outcomes in disorders of the brain and nervous system. The community of New Haven and the surrounding areas provides a beautiful landscape to settle which has something for everyone including music, theater, a foodies’ delight, beaches, boating, shoreline towns, and tons of outdoor adventure. Yale University further offers the benefits of the academic environment, collegiate events, literary and art collections, and performance art. Proximity to New York, Boston, and the rest of New England offers additional opportunities, and we are happy to work with faculty to provide opportunities to practice in locations that meet their needs. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent and be board certified/board eligible in Neurology and have completed a fellowship in General Neurology.  A pplicants must meet the criteria for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Faculty rank will be based on experience. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and three contact references by applying the following link: apply.interfolio.com/185136"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185089": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate in Injury Epidemiology",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Public Health Location: New Haven, CT Posting Date: 04/20/2026 Title of Position: Postdoctoral Associate School: Yale School of Public Health Department: Department of Chronic Disease Epidemiology Anticipated Appointment Date: 9/1/2026 Fixed Term: One year, Full-time, renewable for additional term dependent on performance. Position Description: A postdoctoral position is available with Associate Professor Christopher Morrison in the Department of Chronic Disease Epidemiology at the Yale School of Public Health. Dr. Morrison is a social epidemiologist who uses spatial analytic methods to identify strategies to prevent injuries and violence. This postdoctoral fellowship is supported by ongoing federally funded projects related to firearm violence, road traffic crash injuries, and alcohol-related injuries. The position is housed within a rapidly growing team at YSPH focused on injury and violence prevention—led by Dr. Morrison, Dr. Kerri Raissian, Dr. Magdalena Cerda (incoming Chair, Chronic Disease Epidemiology), and Dr. Megan Ranney (Dean, YSPH)—and will include opportunities of collaboration with other investigators within YSPH and across Yale University. The Postdoctoral Associate will receive training and mentorship in grant writing, spatial epidemiologic methods, and injury prevention science. They will have structured opportunities to develop their proposal writing, methodological skills, and content expertise in the science of injury and violence prevention. The Postdoctoral Associate will be expected to lead and co-author manuscripts and applications for extramural funding, to continue their research currently in progress, and to develop new research ideas related to injury and violence prevention. Applicants must have a doctoral degree from an accredited institution by the start of the appointment. The successful applicant will have a background in social epidemiology, spatial epidemiology, human geography, or related public health or social science disciplines. Highly desirable is demonstrated expertise in spatial epidemiology or injury and violence prevention, including via peer reviewed publications and external presentations. Opportunities for advancement may be available contingent on success during the postdoctoral appointment. Salary will be based on the Yale Postdoctoral Compensation policy . Support for travel to conferences and professional development activities are available. Information regarding benefits can be found here: Benefits | Office for Postdoctoral Affairs To apply: Interested applicants should submit a (1) CV, (2) cover letter describing your research and interest in the position, and (3) contact information for three professional references via Interfolio. Please apply online."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185042": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, YNHH, Pediatric Cardiac, Assistant/Associate Professor (2229)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology at Yale University School of Medicine is recruiting full time, fellowship-trained Pediatric Cardiac Anesthesiologists to support the continuing growth of our congenital cardiac program.  Our team currently supports all cardiopulmonary bypass cases ranging from complex neonates through adult congenital patients, cardiac catheterization lab, non-cardiac surgery for patients with significant congenital heart disease, and imaging in patients with significant congenital heart disease.   We are an integral part of a pediatric interdisciplinary team of cardiologists, cardiothoracic surgeons, intensivists, nurses, and perfusionists. You will work with pediatric anesthesiology fellows, residents and CRNAs. There are robust clinical/translational research programs within the Department. Opportunities for J-1 visa candidates are available. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/185042 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184814": {
      "title": "Full-Time Urologist, VA & YSM (RFP 2214)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Urology Location: New Haven and West Haven, CT The Yale School of Medicine, Department of Urology is a nationally recognized academic department dedicated to excellence in patient care, research, and education. We are seeking a full-time Chief to lead Veteran’s Affairs (VA) Urology Services to provide visionary leadership and advance our clinical, research, and educational missions. This position will be based at the VA Hospital in West Haven, CT with optional clinical activity at Yale Urology for those who desire additional academic clinical exposure This is a rare and exciting opportunity to practice urology at the highest level while serving those who have served our nation. VA Connecticut is a fully accredited, academically vibrant healthcare system with close ties to Yale University - one of the world's leading medical institutions. The VA chief will receive  the benefits of a federal career combined with the intellectual stimulation of an academic medical environment. Our urologists work alongside a team of talented advanced practice providers (APPs) in a supportive, and collaborative environment. You will have access to a surgical robot, comprehensive diagnostic capabilities, and innovative treatment technologies such as prostate cancer ablation (IRE, cryoablation, TULSA) and BPH ablation (Aquablation), all within a collegial culture that prioritizes both patient outcomes and provider well-being. The successful candidate will engage in a full range of urological care, including: * Outpatient urology clinic - comprehensive evaluation and management of urologic conditions * Surgical care in a fully equipped operating room environment * Management of complex urologic conditions including oncology, BPH, urolithiasis, incontinence, and reconstructive cases * Collaboration with APPs for efficient clinic workflow and continuity of care * Participation in multidisciplinary tumor boards and case conferences * On-call responsibilities shared equitably among team members * Optional clinical activity at Yale Urology for those who desire additional academic clinical exposure VA Connecticut holds a formal affiliation with Yale School of Medicine and Yale Urology, providing our physicians with unparalleled academic resources and professional development pathways. This position offers a meaningful academic footprint for those who value teaching and scholarly activity. * Faculty appointment through Yale School of Medicine (commensurate with experience) * Active involvement in the training of urology residents and medical students * Opportunities to participate in clinical research, quality improvement projects, and publications * Option to perform clinical work at Yale Urology if desired * Access to Yale's grand rounds, visiting lectureships, and CME programming * Mentorship opportunities within a nationally recognized academic urology program Qualifications * Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree * Completion of an ACGME-accredited urology residency program * Board certified or board eligible in Urology * Active, unrestricted medical license (Connecticut licensure required or in process) * U.S. citizenship required for VA federal employment * Fellowship training is a plus but not required * Strong commitment to veteran-centered care, teaching, and teamwork * At least 5 years’ experience is preferred. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/184814"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184664": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor General Neurology (RFP 202603-2198)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New Haven County The Division of General Neurology evaluates and treats all neurological conditions. The division includes the Yale Headache Center, which specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of headaches, and the Yale Neurology Resident Clinics. The Resident Clinics offer specialized care in general neurology and stroke and include the Neurology Urgent Access Clinic (NUAC). The goal of NUAC is to allow expedited evaluation of patients seen in the emergency room as well as those referred from physicians requiring an urgent assessment. A major role of the division is to ensure patients are seen by appropriate sub-specialists within the department. If the diagnosis is unclear or the patient would benefit from sub-specialty care, then the General Neurology Division will initially evaluate patients and make internal referrals to the appropriate sub-specialists to allow for the best possible care. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to the education of the next generation of subspecialty experts. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. This position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied academic interests within our division. Rank will be based on experience. The community of New Haven and the surrounding areas provides a beautiful landscape to settle which has something for everyone including music, theater, a foodies’ delight, beaches, boating, shoreline towns, and tons of outdoor adventure. Yale University further offers the benefits of the academic environment, collegiate events, literary and art collections, and performance art. Proximity to New York, Boston, and the rest of New England offers additional opportunities, and we are happy to work with faculty to provide opportunities to practice in locations that meet their needs. We seek motivated academic physicians with clinical expertise in: 1) the care of adult general neurology and subspecialty patients, 2) Participation in clinical trials, 3) Opportunity to teach. Practice location will be in New Haven County. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to the education of the next generation of subspecialty experts. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent and be board certified/board eligible in Neurology and have completed a fellowship in General Neurology.  Applicants must meet the criteria for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Faculty rank will be based on experience. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and three contact references by applying the following link: apply.interfolio.com/184664"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184553": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, General Neurology (RFP 202604-2225)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New London County The Division of General Neurology evaluates and treats all neurological conditions. The division includes the Yale Headache Center, which specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of headaches, and the Yale Neurology Resident Clinics. The Resident Clinics offer specialized care in general neurology and stroke and include the Neurology Urgent Access Clinic (NUAC). The goal of NUAC is to allow expedited evaluation of patients seen in the emergency room as well as those referred from physicians requiring an urgent assessment. A major role of the division is to ensure patients are seen by appropriate sub-specialists within the department. If the diagnosis is unclear or the patient would benefit from sub-specialty care, then the General Neurology Division will initially evaluate patients and make internal referrals to the appropriate sub-specialists to allow for the best possible care. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. This position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied academic interests within our division and department. Rank will be based on education and experience. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to the education of the next generation of subspecialty experts. Practice location will be in New London County. New London, Connecticut is a small, coastal city with a big heart. Its historic downtown boasts world-class dining and a multitude of renowned arts and cultural attractions. Protected green spaces, a sprawling waterfront, an all-magnet school district, quaint residential streets, and a bustling transportation hub make New London very livable. A short commute to Yale University, as well as to Yale Neurology’s New London clinic location, make this small city an ideal place to live, work, and play. We seek motivated academic physicians with clinical expertise in: 1) the care of adult general neurology and subspecialty patients, 2) Participation in clinical trials, 3) Opportunity to teach. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent and be board certified/board eligible in Neurology and have completed a fellowship in General Neurology.  Applicants must meet the criteria for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Faculty rank will be based on experience. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and three contact references by applying the following link: apply.interfolio.com/184553 For additional information, please contact YSMNeurology.facultyaffairs@yale.edu Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183084": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, Financial Economics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: Faculty of Arts and Sciences: Social Science: Economics Location: New Haven, CT  The Economics Department in the Faculty of Arts and Sciences at Yale University is seeking to appoint an Associate or Full Professor with tenure in the field of financial economics. Candidates should be scholars who have made contributions to our understanding of financial markets. They would be expected to teach undergraduates and Ph.D. students, and to supervise Ph.D. dissertations. Applicants must show outstanding scholarly achievement and the Ph.D., or equivalent degree, must be completed. Please electronically submit a letter of interest, CV, research and teaching statements to https://apply.interfolio.com/183084 . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning on May 15, 2026, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027 . If you have specific questions about the position for which you are applying, please contact Nicole Whitcher, Assistant to the Chair, (nicole.whitcher@yale.edu)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183676": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Infectious Diseases",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Infectious Diseases Location: New Haven, CT  The Department of Internal Medicine, Section of Infectious Diseases at the Yale School of Medicine is recruiting a new faculty member at the Assistant/Associate Professor level. Applicants should have an MD, or MD/PhD training in infectious diseases, and an exceptional potential for a career in academic medicine.  Candidates are expected to establish an independent, extramurally funded research program and participate in educational activities of the section.  Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should have an MD, or MD/PhD training in infectious diseases, and an exceptional potential for a career in academic medicine. Please apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/183676 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183664": {
      "title": "General Consultative Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/183664 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183667": {
      "title": "General Consultative Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/183667 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183668": {
      "title": "Sports & Preventative Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time General Consultative Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic Sports Cardiology and Preventive Cardiovascular Health program, dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. There are also opportunities to join ongoing partnerships with local universities’ sports programs, expand our referral network across the state, and grow our cardio-pulmonary exercise laboratory. Primary Responsibilities Provide expert consultative and risk-management care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Manage elite athletes and master’s athletes – including risk assessment, assessment and management of complex cardiac disease and sports participation Diagnosis and management of complex lipid disorders, hypertension, and CKM Collaboration with related specialties, including EP and ACHD, along with genetics Expand the cardiopulmonary exercise testing laboratory Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties in addition to prevention and sports cardiology, including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). The Preventive Cardiovascular Health Program opened in 2018, offering expert outpatient consultations and comprehensive risk management that includes novel-risk reductive pharmacotherapies, as well as nutrition, exercise, and psychological support services. Yale Sports Cardiology opened formally in 2020.  The program sees athletes with concerns for, or diagnosis of, cardiovascular diseases, and also has ongoing partnerships with colleges for screening and follow-up.  This program is a founding member of the new Sports Cardiology Society. Both the Prevention and Sports Cardiology Programs are national leaders with representation at scientific conferences, policy forums and documents. Faculty in both programs have active research programs and are leaders in advancing clinical-care and policies to support cardiovascular health in athletes and the general population. About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified or Board Eligible in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in lipidology, hypertension, obesity medicine, and sports cardiology are encouraged to apply. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter and three confidential letters of recommendation to: https://apply.interfolio.com/183668 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183671": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, ANC, General, Assistant/Associate Professor (2187)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care as well as resident and fellow education.  There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/183671 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183673": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, ANC, General, Assistant/Associate Professor (2188)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team in the Division of General Anesthesia. Clinical assignments may include Adams Neurosciences Center (ANC), Saint Raphael Campus (SRC), and/or Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) with the possibility of other locations as needed. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care as well as resident and fellow education.  There is also an opportunity for clinical and translational research, as well as outcomes related research.  In the event that you have formal post-residency subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made if feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/183673 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183582": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, BH, General, Assistant / Associate Professor (2164)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team at our Bridgeport Hospital location. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care. In the event that you have formal post-fellowship subspecialty training, some assignment to that area will be made feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/183582 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183584": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology, BH, General Assistant / Associate Professor (2166)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Anesthesiology Location: New Haven, CT The Department of Anesthesiology is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor level Anesthesiologist to join our team at our Bridgeport Hospital location. Faculty will be involved in providing clinical care. In the event that you have formal post-fellowship subspecialty training, some assignemnt to that area will be made feasible and desirable to the candidate. Candidates must be Board Certified / Board Eligible and qualify for a Connecticut license. Candidates in subspecialty areas must be fellowship trained. In addition, candidates should have excellent clinical and interpersonal skills and the commitment to make important contributions to the field of Anesthesia. Interested candidates should apply using the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/183584 Questions specific to this position may be sent to lisa.leffert@yale.edu. Review of applications will begin immeditately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183575": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Developmental Behavioral Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Pediatrics: General Pediatrics Location: New Haven The Yale Department of Pediatrics is recruiting for a Developmental Behavioral Pediatrician on the Academic Clinician track in the Developmental Behavioral Program within the Section of Developmental Behavioral Pediatrics to join our outstanding team committed to the care of children and families in our community. The Yale DBP Program is currently directed by a physician-scientist DBP who conducts research on the genetics of autism, directs an early autism diagnostic clinic, directs the DBP Fellowship Program, and co-directs the Pediatrics Resident Rotation in DBP. There is an additional DBP clinician who has a broad-spectrum clinic serving children and adolescents with diverse diagnoses, including ADHD, genetic disorders, speech-language delays, post-traumatic stress disorders, autism, and cerebral palsy. They also care for patients in the Yale Multidisciplinary Spina Bifida Clinic and support the education and research efforts. The Yale DBP Program has strong collaboration with the general pediatricians at an affiliated federally qualified health care center as well as with psychologists, neuropsychologists, SLPs, and social workers at the Yale Child Study Center. Furthermore, they work closely with the Medical-Legal Partnership program to meet the needs of a vulnerable patient population. The recruited faculty member will have an excellence in clinical care, which will include developmental and behavioral pediatric care at our 350 George Street office in New Haven. In addition, this job involves participation in the educational mission of the Section, including training of residents and medical students. The successful applicant will be appointed at the Yale School of Medicine as an Assistant Professor of Pediatrics commensurate with their level of qualifications and experience on the Academic Clinician Track. Yale University and the Department of Pediatrics offer an excellent benefits package. Southern Connecticut boasts beautiful shoreline, excellent schools, numerous recreational opportunities, and easy access to New York City, as well as the New England shore and ski areas. The optimal candidate will have an interest in quality improvement initiatives. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in developmental-behavioral pediatrics and qualified for an appointment to the faculty at the Yale School of Medicine. Interested applicants should submit Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and three Letters of Reference to: https://apply.interfolio.com/183575 For any questions or inquiries regarding this position please contact Mona Sharifi, Chief, Section of General Pediatrics, Department of Pediatrics, 333 Cedar Street, New Haven, CT 06520-8064. Email: mona.sharifi@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183475": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Vascular Division of Neurology -( RFP 202601-2128)",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Neurology Location: New Haven County The Department of Neurology at the Yale School of Medicine seeks to hire a neurohospitalist at the rank of Assistant/ Associate Professor to complement our services at Yale-New Haven Hospital in New Haven, CT.  Rank will be based on education and experience. The position is composed of 24 service weeks (Monday – Sunday) and will include evaluation and management of the whole spectrum of neurological disorders in the emergency department, the intensive care units, as well as on the medical and surgical floors. We anticipate faculty applicants to be dedicated to excellence in patient care, the highest quality and safety standards, as well as education of the next generation of neurologists. The position offers applicants an exciting opportunity for individual programmatic development and goal discovery across varied clinical or academic interests within our department. The neurohospitalist will join the ladder faculty at Yale School of Medicine and a team of general and subspecialty-trained neurologists providing advanced neurologic care using a patient-centered multidisciplinary approach. We provide a highly collaborative, supportive, and mentored environment that promotes specialists to pursue career growth within their specific area of interest. The clinical team reviews its experience and discusses challenging cases in weekly conferences and seminars and refines its approach through shared quality and safety endeavors. Yale University and Yale School of Medicine offer the benefits of a rich academic environment, a cosmopolitan community of clinicians, scientists, educators, and students, a variety of collegiate events, literary and art collections, as well as performing arts. Yale New Haven Hospital (YNHH) is a 1,541-bed teaching hospital affiliated with Yale Schools of Medicine and Nursing. YNHH is the flagship member of Yale New Haven Health System, Connecticut’s leading healthcare system. The community of New Haven and the surrounding areas provide a beautiful landscape to settle which has something for everyone including music, theater, a foodies’ delight, beaches, boating, shoreline towns, and tons of outdoor adventure. Proximity to New York, Boston, and the rest of New England offers additional opportunities. Candidates must have an MD or equivalent, be board certified/ board eligible in Neurology, and eligible for medical licensure in the State of Connecticut. Please upload a brief statement of interest, current CV and three contact references to the following link: apply.interfolio.com/183475 For additional information, please contact YSMNeurology.facultyaffairs@yale.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183086": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Infectious Diseases",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Infectious Diseases Location: New Haven, CT  The Department of Internal Medicine, Section of Infectious Diseases at the Yale School of Medicine is recruiting a new faculty member at the Assistant/Associate Professor level. Applicants should have an M.D., or M.D./Ph.D., training in infectious diseases, and exceptional potential for a career in academic medicine, with a focus on transplant infectious diseases.  Candidates are expected to establish an independent, extramurally funded research program in transplant infectious diseases, and participate in the clinical and educational activities of the section. Applicants should have an M.D., or M.D./Ph.D., training in infectious diseases, and exceptional potential for a career in academic medicine, with a focus on transplant infectious diseases. Please apply at: http://apply.interfolio.com/183086 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182937": {
      "title": "Medical Director, Cardiac Critical Care",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: New Haven, CT Position Overview The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine, in conjunction with the Yale New Haven Health System, is seeking a full-time Critical Care Cardiologist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level to serve as the Medical Director of Cardiac Critical Care. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will lead an important element of our clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide overall clinical leadership for Cardiac Intensive Care across the health system, with particular focus on the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit (CICU) at Yale New Haven Hospital. Serve as attending cardiologist in the dedicated Cardiac Intensive Care Units which provide critical care services to patients with acute cardiovascular conditions including acute myocardial infarction, acute decompensated heart failure, and unstable arrhythmias requiring advanced support including mechanical circulatory support devices. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Contribute to subspecialty services (e.g., advanced heart failure, imaging, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology—based on expertise) Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and either Board Certified in both Cardiovascular Medicine and Critical Care, as well as have a minimum of three years of experience providing cardiac intensive care in an academic setting.  Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES) and have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Interested applicants should submit all required materials through the link provided: https://apply.interfolio.com/182937 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182939": {
      "title": "CVM Fellowship Director, Bridgeport Hospital",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: Bridgeport, CT The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine at the Yale School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Program Director for the Cardiovascular Medicine Fellowship at Yale New Haven Health System’s Bridgeport Hospital. This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a nationally recognized academic cardiology program dedicated to excellence in patient care, medical education, and clinical research. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic clinical practice while participating in the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows within a collaborative academic environment. Primary Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership, academic oversight, and administrative direction for the institution’s accredited Cardiovascular Disease Fellowship Program. Supervise curriculum development, faculty engagement, trainee supervision, recruitment, evaluation, and continuous program improvement to foster excellence in clinical care, scholarship, and professional development. Provide comprehensive cardiovascular care in inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in consultative cardiology services and on-call rotations. Teach and mentor trainees, including medical students, residents, advanced practice providers and fellows. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate to career track (clinical research, clinical trials, quality improvement, medical education innovation, or translational collaboration). Participate in institutional and departmental career development opportunities. About Yale School of Medicine & Cardiology The Yale School of Medicine is one of the nation’s oldest, and most prestigious medical schools. The Section of Cardiovascular Medicine, within the Department of Internal Medicine, has more than 130 full-time ladder track faculty, engaged in clinical, education and research missions. In partnership with Yale New Haven Health System, our faculty provide comprehensive clinical care for cardiovascular conditions, with subspecialties including cardiovascular genetics, echocardiography, electrophysiology, heart failure, inherited cardiomyopathy, interventional cardiology (structural and vascular heart disease, peripheral vascular disease, coronary heart disease), and transplantation. The Section oversees a world-class training program, which includes more than 50 fellows, training in general cardiovascular medicine, as well as subspecialty training in advanced heart failure and transplantation, electrophysiology, interventional cardiology (coronary interventions, peripheral vascular interventions, and structural heart disease), cardiac Imaging and cardio-oncology, in addition to several research fellowships. Our cardiologists are actively engaged in cutting edge collaborative research, spanning basic science, translational research and clinical trials. The section fosters close collaboration with departments across the university, supporting discovery in areas such as genomics, artificial intelligence and data science, biomedical engineering, and health outcomes while providing robust mentorship and training opportunities for fellows, early-career faculty, and physician-scientists committed to advancing cardiovascular medicine. Specialized research centers within the Section include Yale Cardiology Research Group (YCRG), Yale Translational Research Imaging Center (YTRIC), Cardiovascular Clinical Trials Program, the Center for Outcomes Research and Evaluation (CORE), and the Yale Cardiovascular Research Center (CVRC). About Yale New Haven Health System’s Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) Yale New Haven Health System is Connecticut’s leading healthcare system, which includes 5 hospitals with nearly 2700 beds, supported by more than 7500 university and community physicians and advanced practice providers. Yale New Haven Hospital Heart and Vascular Center (HVC) treats more heart and vascular patients than any other facility in Connecticut. The multidisciplinary team of physicians, nurses and other professionals are dedicated to providing our patients with excellence in cardiac care. With a history of pioneering cardiology specialists and innovation that includes cardiology firsts, Yale New Haven Hospital is one of the nation’s leading providers of heart and vascular services, offering the most advanced technology and facilities. Bridgeport Hospital, with over 500 licensed beds, is the second largest hospital in the system, providing a full spectrum of cardiac care, including cardiac surgery, 24/7 cardiac catheterization, a full-service electrophysiology program and noninvasive testing. Successful candidates must be fellowship-trained and Board Certified in cardiovascular medicine. Candidates must meet criteria for appointment as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine in the Academic Clinician (AC) or Clinician Educator Scholar Track (CES). In addition, candidates must have a minimum of 3-5 years of experience in graduate medical education and demonstrated leadership in medical education. Candidates must have an active unrestricted medical license in Connecticut or be eligible for licensure. Candidates with additional training, experience and interest in subspecialty cardiology are encouraged to apply. Applicants should submit all application materials through the provided link: https://apply.interfolio.com/182939 For more information on this position, or any other positions with Yale Cardiovascular Medicine, please contact cvmrecruiting@yale.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182385": {
      "title": "Clinical Ladder (open rank, Assistant, Associate or Full) - Pediatric Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Nursing Location: Orange, CT  The Yale School of Nursing invites applications for an open-rank clinical faculty position (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) in the Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Program, with an anticipated start date as early as January 1, 2027, or July 1, 2027. We seek an outstanding clinician–educator committed to excellence in teaching, clinical practice, and service. Our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized for their scholarship in chronic health conditions, geriatrics, maternal and child health, sleep science, and global health. They collaborate extensively with colleagues across Yale University and with community and clinical partners to advance innovative models of care and education. Our graduate programs attract exceptional students from around the world, fostering a vibrant and truly global academic community. We invite candidates to join a supportive, mission-driven team whose work has meaningful impact locally and worldwide. The priority application deadline is Friday, August 14, 2026. Applications received after this date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Faculty at the Yale School of Nursing teach graduate-level courses and mentor and supervise graduate students. They are eligible for Yale University’s comprehensive and competitive benefits package, including health coverage, and are encouraged to take advantage of the extensive professional development opportunities available through the Poorvu Center for Teaching and Learning and the School of Nursing Dean’s Office. The position requires an earned doctoral degree in Nursing or a related field. Certification in a pediatric area and previous teaching experience in a related program are preferred. Clinical practice expertise, strong leadership, scholarly achievements, and eligibility for licensure as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in CT are also necessary. The complete application should include (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a 2-page statement that highlights past teaching accomplishments. The application should be submitted at https://apply.interfolio.com/182385. Inquiries should be directed to the Office of Faculty Affairs at FAO.YSN@yale.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182388": {
      "title": "Clinical Ladder (open rank, Assistant, Associate or Full) - Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Nursing Location: Orange, CT  The Yale School of Nursing invites applications for an open-rank clinical faculty position (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) in the Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner Program, with an anticipated start date as early as July 1, 2027. We seek an outstanding clinician–educator committed to excellence in teaching, clinical practice, and service. Our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized for their scholarship in chronic health conditions, geriatrics, maternal and child health, sleep science, and global health. They collaborate extensively with colleagues across Yale University and with community and clinical partners to advance innovative models of care and education. Our graduate programs attract exceptional students from around the world, fostering a vibrant and truly global academic community. We invite candidates to join a supportive, mission-driven team whose work has meaningful impact locally and worldwide. The priority application deadline is Friday, August 14, 2026. Applications received after this date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Faculty at the Yale School of Nursing teach graduate-level courses and mentor and supervise graduate students. They are eligible for Yale University’s comprehensive and competitive benefits package, including health coverage, and are encouraged to take advantage of the extensive professional development opportunities available through the Poorvu Center for Teaching and Learning and the School of Nursing Dean’s Office. The position requires an earned doctoral degree in Nursing or a related field. Certification as a Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner and previous teaching experience in a related program are preferred. Clinical practice expertise, strong leadership, scholarly achievements, and eligibility for licensure as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in CT are also necessary. The complete application should include (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a 2-page statement that highlights past teaching accomplishments. The application should be submitted at https://apply.interfolio.com/182388. Inquiries should be directed to Megan Hauck, Senior Administrative Assistant for Faculty Affairs at FAO.YSN@yale.edu."
    },
